const WORD_SRC = {"available (adj.)":[["leader-113-22","Will you be \u0001available\u0002 to go with me?",""],["leader-113-52","A: Do you have brochures in Spanish? B: No, sorry, they're only \u0001available\u0002 in English.","A:你們有西班牙文的簡介手冊嗎? B:抱歉,只有英文版。"]],"complimentary (adj.)":[["guide-115-17","Some hotels in Taiwan offer \u0001complimentary\u0002 nice breakfast. You could try asking the front desk if your stay at the hotel includes a free breakfast.","台灣有些飯店提供免費招待的美味早餐。你可以問櫃台,你的住宿是否含免費早餐。"],["leader-114-38","The hotel provided each guest with a voucher for a \u0001complimentary\u0002 breakfast.","飯店提供每位客人一張免費早餐的兌換券。"]],"reservation (n.)":[["leader-115-4","Peter: Judy, I hope our \u0001reservation\u0002 at the restaurant is confirmed. Judy: Don't worry, I received the confirmation email this morning.","Peter:Judy,希望我們餐廳的訂位已經確認了。 Judy:別擔心,我今早收到確認信了。"],["leader-115-31","When visiting museums and other attractions in Paris, even if you have purchased a museum pass, making a(n) \u0001reservation\u0002 is still required.","在巴黎參觀博物館等景點時,即使買了博物館通票,仍需要事先預約。"]],"departure (n.)":[["guide-115-60","Before \u0001departure\u0002, please check the airline's official website to confirm that your flight is operating normally.","出發前,請查看航空公司官方網站,確認你的航班正常運作。"],["leader-113-19","This is your captain speaking. We apologize for our late \u0001departure\u0002, but as is sometimes the case at San Francisco, the fog was too thick for taking off.","我是機長。我們為延遲起飛道歉,但如舊金山常有的情況,霧太濃無法起飛。"]],"fasten (v.)":[["leader-113-16","Passenger: Would you please show me how to \u0001fasten\u0002 the seat belt?",""],["guide-113-26","Ladies and Gentlemen, as we are encountering some turbulence, the cruising is not stable. Please return to your seat and \u0001fasten\u0002 your seatbelt.","各位女士先生,由於我們遇到一些亂流,飛行不太穩定。請回座並繫好安全帶。"]],"accommodation (n.)":[["guide-115-3","Top \u0001accommodations\u0002 can be booked up weeks or even months in advance, so it's best to plan ahead before travelling abroad.","頂級住宿可能提前數週甚至數月就被訂滿,所以出國前最好提早規劃。"],["guide-113-62","Hotels operated by chains normally provide \u0001accommodations\u0002 ranging from budget to luxurious ones. However, there are still many privately owned inns and hotels that provide much less expensive rooms and meals than chain hotels.","連鎖經營的飯店通常提供從平價到豪華不等的住宿。然而,仍有許多私人經營的旅館提供比連鎖飯店便宜許多的房間與餐點。"]],"customs (n.)":[["leader-115-15","John: Mary, do we need to fill anything out for the souvenirs we bought abroad? Mary: Yes, we need to complete the \u0001customs\u0002 declaration form at the airport for items that may be restricted or taxable.","John:Mary,我們在國外買的紀念品需要填什麼嗎? Mary:要,對於可能受限制或需課稅的物品,得在機場填海關申報單。"],["guide-115-12","If you are bringing animals, plants, or their products into the country, to avoid penalties, apply for quarantine at \u0001customs\u0002 or the Animal and Plant Health Inspection Agency upon entry.","若攜帶動物、植物或其產品入境,為免受罰,請於入境時在海關或動植物防疫檢疫署申請檢疫。"]],"declare (v.)":[["leader-115-27","If you have nothing to \u0001declare\u0002, simply walk through the Green Channel, stopping only if asked to do so by a customs agent.","如果你沒有任何東西要申報,就直接走綠線通道,除非海關人員要求你停下。"],["leader-114-45","Make sure to \u0001declare\u0002 any items you bought abroad.",""]],"destination (n.)":[["leader-115-70","While we are en route to our next \u0001destination\u0002, I will point out the beautiful beach and the famous golf course for your reference.","在我們前往下一個目的地的途中,我會為各位指出美麗的海灘和著名的高爾夫球場。"],["guide-115-48","Jiufen, a mountain village in New Taipei City, is a popular \u0001destination\u0002 for international travelers mainly because of its old street.","九份是新北市的山城,主要因其老街而成為國際旅客熱門景點。"]],"facilities (n.)":[["guide-115-39","In Taiwan, special rental places such as \"whole-house lodging\" can be found. You can rent a whole house just for your party and have access to your own private \u0001facilities\u0002.","在台灣可找到「整棟出租(包棟民宿)」這類特別的租宿。你可以只為自己的團體租下整棟房子,擁有使用自己專屬設施的權利。"],["leader-113-12","The receptionist of a hotel is responsible for politely completing the check-in procedure and introducing the \u0001facilities\u0002 and services the hotel provides.","飯店櫃台負責禮貌地完成入住手續,並介紹飯店提供的設施和服務。"]],"indigenous (adj.)":[["guide-115-18","Taiwanese \u0001indigenous\u0002 people often use natural materials in their everyday items, such as clothes, accessories, and tools. For example, the Atayal often make clothing from ramie.","台灣原住民常在日常用品(如衣物、飾品、工具)中使用天然材料。例如,泰雅族常用苧麻製衣。"],["guide-115-46","The \u0001indigenous\u0002 people of Alishan, the Tsou people, are comprised of nine major tribes, each holding their own celebrations every year from September to December jointly referred to as the famous \"Tsou Annual Festival\" of Alishan.","阿里山的原住民鄒族由九大部落組成,各部落每年 9 月至 12 月舉辦自己的慶典,合稱著名的阿里山「鄒族年度祭典」。"]],"itinerary (n.)":[["guide-113-35","When you come to Penghu, you may sign up for an island-hopping tour with everything from half-day to multi-day \u0001itineraries\u0002 available.","來澎湖時,你可以報名跳島之旅,從半日到多日的行程都有。"],["leader-112-38","Here is the \u0001itinerary\u0002 for my trip to Europe this coming summer. Do you have any suggestions?","這是我今夏歐洲之旅的行程表。你有什麼建議嗎?"]],"passport (n.)":[["leader-115-3","Before entering the country, each visitor must have a valid \u0001passport\u0002 ready for inspection.","入境前,每位旅客都必須備妥有效護照以供查驗。"],["guide-113-53","Passenger: Hi, I'd like to check in for my flight to New York, please. Check-in Agent: Of course, may I have your \u0001passport\u0002 and e-ticket, please?","旅客:你好,我想辦理飛往紐約的報到。 報到人員:當然,請給我你的護照和電子機票好嗎?"]],"prohibited (adj.)":[["leader-115-60","In many museums, touching the exhibited items is a behavior that is absolutely \u0001prohibited\u0002.","在許多博物館,觸摸展示品是絕對被禁止的行為。"],["leader-114-46","The security officer had to confiscate the \u0001prohibited\u0002 items from the passenger's luggage.","安檢人員必須從乘客行李中沒收違禁品。"]],"souvenir (n.)":[["leader-113-67","To buy \u0001souvenirs\u0002 at the local market, tourists often need to exchange their currency for the local money.","要在當地市場買紀念品,遊客常需把貨幣兌換成當地錢幣。"],["guide-113-76","While some people travel to see historic sights or hit the road in search of boutiques and \u0001souvenirs\u0002, more and more people are getting bit by the culinary travel bug.","",1]],"discount (n.)":[["leader-114-30","To bring more tourists to Taiwan, the government should offer attractive incentive like \u0001discounts\u0002 and special deals.","為了吸引更多遊客來台灣,政府應提供有吸引力的誘因,例如折扣和特別優惠。"],["leader-113-36","A Periodic Ticket allows an unlimited number of rides to and from designated stations at a bargain rate within the offer validity period. The \u0001discount\u0002 is calculated based on the full fares for Non-reserved Seats.","定期票在效期內,可於指定車站間無限次搭乘,享優惠費率。折扣依非劃位車廂的全票價計算。"]],"landmark (n.)":[["leader-115-48","On the city tour, the guide asked everyone to take a photo in front of the famous \u0001landmark\u0002 that represents the history of the area.","市區觀光時,導遊請大家在代表當地歷史的著名地標前拍照。"],["guide-115-61","The \"Yehliu Geopark\" is one of the most famous \u0001landmarks\u0002 of Taiwan.","「野柳地質公園」是台灣最著名的地標之一。"]],"luggage (n.)":[["leader-114-36","Ground Staff: Can you identify which one resembles your \u0001luggage\u0002? (Showing a card with various types of luggage.) Amy: Mine looks similar to Type D.","地勤:你能辨認出哪一個像你的行李嗎?(出示各種行李款式的卡片) Amy:我的很像 D 型。"],["guide-114-49","Make sure that your \u0001luggage\u0002 has successfully passed through X-ray inspection before you leave the check-in area.","離開報到區前,請確認你的行李已順利通過 X 光檢查。"]],"receipt (n.)":[["leader-113-41","Do you have your \u0001receipt\u0002?",""],["leader-112-62","A: Besides the discount, we can also keep the \u0001receipts\u0002 to get a VAT (value-added tax) refund at the airport. B: So great!","A:除了折扣,我們還能留著收據到機場辦加值稅退稅。 B:太棒了!"]],"refund (n.)":[["leader-112-62","A: Besides the discount, we can also keep the receipts to get a VAT (value-added tax) \u0001refund\u0002 at the airport. B: So great!","A:除了折扣,我們還能留著收據到機場辦加值稅退稅。 B:太棒了!"],["guide-112-46","If you are not completely satisfied with our product, you can return it for a full \u0001refund\u0002.","如果你對我們的產品不完全滿意,可以退貨並獲得全額退款。"]],"attraction (n.)":[["leader-115-38","The destination is a big city with countless tourist \u0001attractions\u0002; we plan to visit at least six or more of the most recommended ones.","這個目的地是個有無數觀光景點的大城市;我們計畫至少參觀六個以上最推薦的。"],["leader-115-66","Drawing many people's attention, Jurassic World: The Experience at Cloud Forest is one of the most recently added \u0001attractions\u0002 in Singapore.","吸引眾人目光的「侏羅紀世界:雲霧森林體驗」是新加坡最新增設的景點之一。"]],"bill (n.)":[["leader-115-61","Let me calculate your \u0001bill\u0002 for you. It all adds up to NT$15,000, Sir.","先生,我幫您算帳,全部加起來總共台幣 15,000 元。"],["leader-113-34","The answer to how much we should tip a waitress can be varied. Some people think 10 to 15% of your \u0001bill\u0002 is the proper amount.","我們該給服務生多少小費,答案不一。有些人認為帳單的 10–15% 是適當金額。"]],"brochure (n.)":[["leader-113-52","A: Do you have \u0001brochures\u0002 in Spanish? B: No, sorry, they're only available in English.","A:你們有西班牙文的簡介手冊嗎? B:抱歉,只有英文版。"],["guide-113-25","Here is a guidebook and some \u0001brochures\u0002 providing detailed information about the city and the city tours.",""]],"confirm (v.)":[["leader-115-4","Peter: Judy, I hope our reservation at the restaurant is \u0001confirmed\u0002. Judy: Don't worry, I received the confirmation email this morning.","Peter:Judy,希望我們餐廳的訂位已經確認了。 Judy:別擔心,我今早收到確認信了。"],["guide-115-60","Before departure, please check the airline's official website to \u0001confirm\u0002 that your flight is operating normally.","出發前,請查看航空公司官方網站,確認你的航班正常運作。"]],"declaration (n.)":[["leader-115-15","John: Mary, do we need to fill anything out for the souvenirs we bought abroad? Mary: Yes, we need to complete the customs \u0001declaration\u0002 form at the airport for items that may be restricted or taxable.","John:Mary,我們在國外買的紀念品需要填什麼嗎? Mary:要,對於可能受限制或需課稅的物品,得在機場填海關申報單。"],["leader-112-18","Passengers arriving in Taiwan must fill out a health \u0001declaration\u0002 form.","抵達台灣的旅客須填寫健康申報表。"]],"emergency (n.)":[["leader-115-65","Tourists on the plane were reminded how to use oxygen masks in case of \u0001emergency\u0002.","機上乘客被提醒如何在緊急情況下使用氧氣面罩。"],["leader-112-3","Flight attendant: Don't inflate your life jacket until you've left the plane in case of \u0001emergency\u0002.","空服員:緊急時,離開飛機前請勿為救生衣充氣。"]],"flight (n.)":[["leader-111-42","Customer: I would like to confirm my \u0001flight\u0002 from Taipei to Los Angeles. Airline agent: May I have your name and ticket number, please?","顧客:我想確認台北到洛杉磯的航班。 地勤:能給我你的姓名和票號嗎?"],["guide-111-45","Did Alex's \u0001flight\u0002 to Taipei depart on time?","Alex 飛台北的班機準時起飛了嗎?"]],"passenger (n.)":[["guide-115-44","A: Can I bring my pet along on the trip? B: No, to protect the rights and comfort of all \u0001passengers\u0002, pets are forbidden on board.","A:我可以帶寵物一起去嗎? B:不行,為保障所有乘客的權益與舒適,寵物禁止上車/機。"],["leader-112-18","\u0001Passengers\u0002 arriving in Taiwan must fill out a health declaration form.","抵達台灣的旅客須填寫健康申報表。"]],"prescription (n.)":[["guide-113-57","The pharmacy is where you can fill your \u0001prescriptions\u0002 and purchase over-the-counter medications and health-related products.","藥局是你可以領處方藥、購買成藥與健康相關產品的地方。"],["leader-112-23","Some \u0001prescription\u0002 medications are illegal in Taiwan. Authorities may jail or fine you if you have them.","有些處方藥在台灣是違法的。若攜帶,當局可能將你監禁或罰款。"]],"quarantine (n.)":[["guide-115-12","If you are bringing animals, plants, or their products into the country, to avoid penalties, apply for \u0001quarantine\u0002 at customs or the Animal and Plant Health Inspection Agency upon entry.","若攜帶動物、植物或其產品入境,為免受罰,請於入境時在海關或動植物防疫檢疫署申請檢疫。"],["leader-112-25","Effective from October 13, 2022, Taiwan has lifted the \u0001quarantine\u0002 requirement for all arrivals, so arriving travelers will no longer be required to quarantine.","自 2022 年 10 月 13 日起,台灣取消所有入境者的隔離要求,入境旅客不再須隔離。"]],"route (n.)":[["guide-115-22","The trail around Sun Moon Lake in Nantou is listed as one of the 10 best cycling \u0001routes\u0002 in the world by CNN.","南投日月潭的環湖步道被 CNN 列為全球十大最佳自行車路線之一。"],["leader-114-65","The new \u0001route\u0002 to the northern coast region creates more opportunities for tourists to enjoy all the spectacular view of the area.","通往北海岸地區的新路線,為遊客創造更多欣賞該區壯麗景色的機會。"]],"turbulence (n.)":[["guide-113-26","Ladies and Gentlemen, as we are encountering some \u0001turbulence\u0002, the cruising is not stable. Please return to your seat and fasten your seatbelt.","各位女士先生,由於我們遇到一些亂流,飛行不太穩定。請回座並繫好安全帶。"],["guide-112-11","You must remain seated while the fasten-seat-belt signals are illuminated during \u0001turbulence\u0002.","亂流期間,當繫安全帶指示燈亮起時,你必須保持坐好。"]],"abroad (adv.)":[["guide-112-13","Do I need to dial the international area code while making a call \u0001abroad\u0002?","打國際電話時,我需要撥國際區碼嗎?"],["guide-112-62","Before going \u0001abroad\u0002, you need to understand the current exchange rates and have some New Taiwan dollars converted into U.S. dollars.","出國前,你需要了解目前的匯率,並把一些新台幣兌換成美元。"]],"airport (n.)":[["leader-110-6","You need to be at the \u0001airport\u0002 by 10:00.",""],["leader-107-2","It is very kind of you to give me a ride to the \u0001airport\u0002.","你真好心載我去機場。"]],"belongings (n.)":[["guide-115-1","When you are in public places, be sure not to leave your personal \u0001belongings\u0002 unattended.","在公共場所,務必不要讓你的個人隨身物品無人看管。"],["leader-114-28","Make sure to purchase a strong and durable carry-on bag to ensure your \u0001belongings\u0002 are safe during travel.","務必買一個堅固耐用的隨身包,確保旅行時物品安全。"]],"capacity (n.)":[["leader-114-33","European airlines are increasing their \u0001capacity\u0002 as the expansion trend that began late last year continues.","隨著去年底開始的擴張趨勢持續,歐洲航空公司正在增加運能。"],["guide-114-72","Boosting the \u0001capacity\u0002 of the sector to attract, retain and develop a strong and sustainable workforce is a further area of ongoing focus.","",4]],"culinary (adj.)":[["guide-114-31","It is said that one of the great strengths of its \u0001culinary\u0002 landscape is its accessibility.",""],["guide-113-76","\u0001Culinary\u0002 tourism is one of the hottest trends in travel.","",1]],"exceed (v.)":[["guide-114-18","The medical assistive devices used by passengers may not \u0001exceed\u0002 125 cm in length, 90 cm in width, and 185 cm in height.","乘客使用的醫療輔助裝置不得超過長 125 公分、寬 90 公分、高 185 公分。"],["leader-112-27","Foreigners with a valid passport/travel document and whose stay in R.O.C does not \u0001exceed\u0002 a period of 183 days are eligible to apply for a tax refund.","持有效護照/旅行證件、且在台停留不超過 183 天的外國人,符合退稅資格。"]],"immigration (n.)":[["leader-115-32","Officers at \u0001immigration\u0002 check all passports and visas before travelers can enter the country.","入境查驗處的官員會查驗所有護照和簽證,旅客才能入境。"],["guide-114-40","\u0001Immigration\u0002 is the place where government officials check travelers to make sure they can legally get in or get out of the country.","證照查驗處是政府官員查驗旅客、確保他們能合法入境或出境的地方。"]],"infer (v.)":[["leader-115-73","Based on the information presented in this passage, what can be \u0001inferred\u0002?","根據本文資訊,可以推論出什麼?"],["guide-114-79","Which of the following can be \u0001inferred\u0002 from the passage?","根據本文,下列何者可以被推論出來?"]],"museum (n.)":[["leader-110-38","Technology allows people to go on virtual tours on their computers to see \u0001museums\u0002, world heritage sites, and other attractions before they plan a trip.","科技讓人能在電腦上進行虛擬導覽,在規劃旅程前先看博物館、世界遺產和其他景點。"],["leader-109-22","Ian needed to look at the map on his mobile phone several times because he didn't know the route to the \u0001museum\u0002.","Ian 得看好幾次手機地圖,因為他不知道去博物館的路線。"]],"purpose (n.)":[["leader-115-75","What can be described as the \u0001purpose\u0002 of this passage?","本文的寫作目的為何?"],["leader-113-69","What is the \u0001purpose\u0002 of your visit?",""]],"restriction (n.)":[["leader-114-12","Due to the \u0001restrictions\u0002 on the size of the carry-on luggage, it can be challenging to choose the ideal personal bag for flights.","由於隨身行李尺寸的限制,要選到理想的個人包包可能很有挑戰性。"],["leader-114-34","Passengers often get upset due to long lines and confusion about ticket \u0001restrictions\u0002 hidden in the small print of discounted fares.","乘客常因長長的隊伍,以及對折扣票價小字裡隱藏的票務限制感到困惑而不悅。"]],"spectacular (adj.)":[["leader-115-21","The \u0001spectacular\u0002 Northeast Coast is a popular tourist destination that serves both as a fascinating natural classroom and as an enchanting coastal playground.","壯觀的東北角海岸是熱門觀光勝地,既是迷人的天然教室,也是迷人的海岸遊樂場。"],["leader-114-65","The new route to the northern coast region creates more opportunities for tourists to enjoy all the \u0001spectacular\u0002 view of the area.","通往北海岸地區的新路線,為遊客創造更多欣賞該區壯麗景色的機會。"]],"sustainable (adj.)":[["guide-114-71","These strategies look to build on recent momentum to shift to more \u0001sustainable\u0002 models of tourism, to adapt to an increasingly dynamic environment and engage stakeholders around a common vision for the future of the sector.","",1],["leader-113-45","Ecological tourism encourages \u0001sustainable\u0002 travel, fostering appreciation for natural wonders while promoting conservation efforts crucial for preserving our planet's biodiversity.","生態旅遊鼓勵永續旅行,培養對自然奇景的欣賞,同時推動對保護地球生物多樣性至關重要的保育工作。"]],"treasure (n.)":[["guide-115-33","The Alishan Forest Railway is a \u0001treasure\u0002 of Taiwan. Every day, the train takes passengers on wonderful rides forward through different forest types.","阿里山森林鐵路是台灣的瑰寶。每天,火車載著旅客穿越不同森林類型,展開美妙的旅程。"],["guide-115-62","The National Palace Museum houses the world's largest collection of priceless Chinese art \u0001treasures\u0002.","故宮博物院收藏著全世界最大的無價中華藝術珍寶典藏。"]],"valid (adj.)":[["leader-115-3","Before entering the country, each visitor must have a \u0001valid\u0002 passport ready for inspection.","入境前,每位旅客都必須備妥有效護照以供查驗。"],["leader-112-27","Foreigners with a \u0001valid\u0002 passport/travel document and whose stay in R.O.C does not exceed a period of 183 days are eligible to apply for a tax refund.","持有效護照/旅行證件、且在台停留不超過 183 天的外國人,符合退稅資格。"]],"vendor (n.)":[["leader-115-7","Be ready for the warm-hearted \u0001vendors\u0002 on these streets; they are super friendly and always eager to persuade you to buy their items.","要有心理準備,這些街上有熱情的攤販;他們超友善,總是急著說服你買他們的東西。"],["leader-115-8","If you buy some souvenirs from local \u0001vendors\u0002 in Thailand, you should try to bargain for a good deal because the first price offered is usually much higher.","如果你在泰國向當地攤販買紀念品,應該試著殺價以爭取好價錢,因為對方開出的第一個價通常高很多。"]],"allowance (n.)":[["leader-112-43","Each passenger can have two pieces of checked baggage \u0001allowance\u0002 and one carry-on bag.","每位乘客可有兩件託運行李額度和一件隨身行李。"],["leader-112-46","If you carry more than the duty-free \u0001allowance\u0002, including a bottle of alcohol, the items will be confiscated.","若攜帶超過免稅額度(含一瓶酒),物品將被沒收。"]],"authentic (adj.)":[["leader-114-32","Tourists now seek more \u0001authentic\u0002 experiences involving real communities and people instead of simply following a tour guide's flag.","遊客現在尋求更道地的體驗,涉及真實的社區與人們,而不是單純跟著導遊的旗子走。"],["guide-113-76","Travel has been trending increasingly towards \u0001authentic\u0002 experiences.","",4]],"book (v.)":[["leader-113-7","As soon as your traveling date is fixed, you need to \u0001book\u0002 yourself a flight ticket and make your hotel reservations.","旅行日期一確定,你就得訂機票和訂飯店。"],["leader-112-50","A: Is it possible to \u0001book\u0002 an opera ticket and a local tour for me?",""]],"breathtaking (adj.)":[["leader-115-18","The magnificent waterfall is truly the most \u0001breathtaking\u0002 feature of this national park.","那壯麗的瀑布真是這座國家公園最令人屏息的特色。"],["guide-114-36","When in central Taiwan, railroad enthusiasts can plan a railway journey to Changhua Sector Garage. It has a round platform with 12 tracks that spread out like a fan—a \u0001breathtaking\u0002 sight!","在中台灣時,鐵道迷可以規劃一趟前往彰化扇形車庫的鐵道之旅。那裡有座圓形月台、12 條軌道如扇形展開——令人驚豔!"]],"concierge (n.)":[["leader-112-50","The \u0001concierge\u0002 service in our hotel can help.",""],["guide-112-61","A \u0001concierge\u0002 is someone who is employed in a hotel to help guests arrange things, such as local tours, theatre tickets and restaurant reservations.","禮賓員是飯店雇用來協助客人安排事務(如當地旅遊、劇院票券和餐廳訂位)的人。"]],"cuisine (n.)":[["guide-114-26","Common ingredients of Taiwanese \u0001cuisine\u0002 are pork, seafood, rice, soy, and chicken.","台灣料理常見的食材有豬肉、海鮮、米、大豆和雞肉。"],["guide-112-31","A: How does Mexican \u0001cuisine\u0002 taste? B: It has a spicy and heavy flavor.","A:墨西哥菜嚐起來如何? B:它味道又辣又重。"]],"currency (n.)":[["leader-113-67","To buy souvenirs at the local market, tourists often need to exchange their \u0001currency\u0002 for the local money.","要在當地市場買紀念品,遊客常需把貨幣兌換成當地錢幣。"],["leader-112-47","Changing money at the airport is convenient to get local \u0001currency\u0002, but you may be charged some service fees.","在機場換錢方便取得當地貨幣,但可能被收手續費。"]],"destroy (v.)":[["leader-115-36","Littering in natural parks can \u0001destroy\u0002 the beauty tourists come to admire.","在自然公園亂丟垃圾會破壞遊客前來欣賞的美景。"],["leader-114-1","The Maui wildfire in Hawaii last year took 102 lives and \u0001destroyed\u0002 80% of the town of Lahaina.","夏威夷茂宜島去年的野火奪走 102 條人命,並摧毀了拉海納鎮 80% 的地區。"]],"dish (n.)":[["leader-115-5","If you plan to try some exotic \u0001dishes\u0002 when traveling to a different country, please do some research about what those dishes are.","如果你到不同國家想嘗試一些異國風味的菜,請先研究一下那些是什麼菜。"],["leader-113-13","There are also vegetarian \u0001dishes\u0002 on our à la carte menu.",""]],"domestic (adj.)":[["leader-112-63","Excuse me, could you show me how to make a \u0001domestic\u0002 long-distance call from San Diego to New York?","不好意思,能教我怎麼從聖地牙哥打國內長途電話到紐約嗎?"],["guide-112-25","To compensate for the loss of foreign tourists caused by COVID-19 restrictions, Taiwanese travel businesses have shifted gears towards \u0001domestic\u0002 trips.","為彌補 COVID-19 限制造成的外國遊客流失,台灣旅遊業者已轉換方向(改變策略)轉向國內旅遊。"]],"embassy (n.)":[["leader-112-70","A: What can I do if I lose my passport during the trip? B: You have to go to the \u0001embassy\u0002 to have a new one reissued.","A:旅途中護照弄丟了怎麼辦? B:你得去大使館補發一本新的。"],["leader-111-58","If a traveler loses his or her passport, he or she needs to find his or her country's \u0001embassy\u0002 to apply for a temporary passport.","若旅客遺失護照,須找到自己國家的大使館申請臨時護照。"]],"exhibition (n.)":[["guide-109-50","A: Do I need tickets for Taiwan Culinary \u0001Exhibition\u0002? B: It's free and open to the public.","A:台灣美食展需要門票嗎? B:免費且對大眾開放。"],["leader-108-76","The new \u0001exhibition\u0002 allows people to analyze why they love and hate certain foods.","",4]],"explore (v.)":[["leader-115-35","The city's urban center is quite compact and easy to \u0001explore\u0002 on foot or by bike.","這座城市的市中心相當緊湊,很適合步行或騎單車遊覽。"],["leader-114-50","Nancy: At least we can \u0001explore\u0002 the airport shops while we wait.",""]],"fare (n.)":[["leader-115-42","Passengers simply add value to a smart card and swipe it at the gate to enter. The \u0001fare\u0002 is automatically deducted.","乘客只要為智慧卡加值,在閘門刷卡進入,車資就會自動扣除。"],["leader-113-35","Do you know how much the \u0001fare\u0002 is?",""]],"guarantee (v.)":[["guide-112-49","The salespersons \u0001guaranteed\u0002 that their organic foods do not have preservatives.","售貨員保證他們的有機食品不含防腐劑。"],["leader-109-34","The agent in a car rental company \u0001guaranteed\u0002 that he would reserve a car for Nancy if she could pay a deposit to confirm her reservation.","租車公司的專員保證,只要 Nancy 付訂金確認,就會為她預留一輛車。"]],"heritage (n.)":[["guide-115-31","Longshan Temple, located in Wanhua, is one of Taipei's finest examples of Taiwan's architectural and historical \u0001heritage\u0002.","位於萬華的龍山寺,是台灣建築與歷史遺產的最佳範例之一。"],["leader-115-71","Tourism is often a primary source of income for many regions, especially those rich in natural beauty, historical importance, or cultural \u0001heritage\u0002.","",1]],"infrastructure (n.)":[["guide-115-76","That analysis factors in the cost of purchasing an electric car and outfitting it with autonomous technology, installing and using electric vehicle charging \u0001infrastructure\u0002, fleet maintenance, insurance, vehicle teleoperation and other costs.","",1],["guide-114-71","Tourism destinations and businesses need support to keep pace with rapid technological developments, while resources are also required to develop the transport and other \u0001infrastructure\u0002 needed to better manage tourism development.","",1]],"landscape (n.)":[["leader-115-78","What does the word \"fragmented\" in the phrase \"fragmented regulatory \u0001landscape\u0002\" most nearly mean?","在「fragmented regulatory landscape(破碎/各自為政的法規環境)」這個詞組中,\"fragmented\" 一字最接近的意思是?"],["guide-114-21","Taroko National Park is a popular destination for international travelers because of its spectacular \u0001landscapes\u0002.","太魯閣國家公園因其壯觀的景觀,成為國際旅客的熱門景點。"]],"maintenance (n.)":[["guide-113-64","I'll speak to the \u0001maintenance\u0002 department.",""],["leader-112-51","I will send a \u0001maintenance\u0002 staff up right away.",""]],"pilgrimage (n.)":[["guide-115-14","The Mazu \u0001pilgrimage\u0002 is one of the most noted folk religious festivals in Taiwan. People go on a journey to honor the goddess Mazu.","媽祖遶境進香是台灣最著名的民間宗教節慶之一。人們踏上旅程來敬奉媽祖女神。"],["guide-114-27","The Mazu \u0001pilgrimage\u0002, which lasts over a week and covers hundreds of kilometers, is one of Taiwan's religious festivals. It is like an enormous birthday celebration for the “Goddess of the Sea.”","媽祖遶境進香持續一週以上、綿延數百公里,是台灣的宗教節慶之一,就像為「海上女神」舉辦的盛大生日慶典。"]],"popular (adj.)":[["leader-112-40","Taiwan has become more and more \u0001popular\u0002 among foreign tourists because it is quite affordable and friendly.","台灣越來越受外國旅客歡迎,因為它相當物價實惠又友善。"],["leader-111-53","Many immigrants live in Australia, so ethnic food is very \u0001popular\u0002 here.","許多移民住在澳洲,所以異國(族裔)料理在這很受歡迎。"]],"rate (n.)":[["guide-113-5","Caller: How much are your single rooms? Front Desk Clerk: The \u0001rates\u0002 vary depending upon the season and type of single rooms.","來電者:你們的單人房多少錢? 櫃台:價格會依季節與單人房型而有所不同。"],["leader-111-20","International calls to mobile phones registered in another country are charged higher \u0001rates\u0002. The first zero of an international number must be deleted since it is a \"trunk prefix\" only for domestic calls within many countries.","打到在他國註冊的手機的國際電話會被收取較高費率。國際號碼開頭的 0 須刪去,因它是在許多國家只供國內電話使用的「長途字冠」。"]],"reserve (v.)":[["leader-112-14","Waiter: Good evening, Grand Restaurant, may I help you? Customer: I would like to \u0001reserve\u0002 a table for tonight.","服務生:晚安,Grand 餐廳,能為您服務嗎? 顧客:我想預訂今晚的位子。"],["leader-111-50","Tourist: I would like to \u0001reserve\u0002 a room for this weekend.",""]],"restricted (adj.)":[["leader-115-15","John: Mary, do we need to fill anything out for the souvenirs we bought abroad? Mary: Yes, we need to complete the customs declaration form at the airport for items that may be \u0001restricted\u0002 or taxable.","John:Mary,我們在國外買的紀念品需要填什麼嗎? Mary:要,對於可能受限制或需課稅的物品,得在機場填海關申報單。"],["guide-114-41","You must declare or dispose of any prohibited or \u0001restricted\u0002 goods before you reach customs.","抵達海關前,你必須申報或丟棄任何違禁或受限制的物品。"]],"shuttle (n.)":[["leader-114-68","There is a wide variety of hotels conveniently located near the airport and many of them offer hotel courtesy \u0001shuttles\u0002.","機場附近有各式各樣位置便利的飯店,許多提供免費接駁車。"],["leader-111-49","Many hotels in New York provide free airport \u0001shuttle\u0002 service. You could also take the subway if you are comfortable with public transportation.","紐約許多飯店提供免費機場接駁服務。若你習慣搭大眾運輸,也可搭地鐵。"]],"species (n.)":[["guide-113-15","The conservation of jungles and rainforests is critical to the survival of many \u0001species\u0002.","叢林與雨林的保育對許多物種的生存至關重要。"],["guide-111-26","The Formosan black bear is a \u0001species\u0002 indigenous to Taiwan and currently listed as “endangered” under Taiwan's Wildlife Conservation Act.","台灣黑熊是原生於台灣的物種,目前依《野生動物保育法》被列為「瀕危」。"]],"volcano (n.)":[["guide-115-40","The \u0001volcano\u0002 on the island has been unusually active over the past few days; many residents are afraid that it is going to erupt in no time.","島上的火山過去幾天異常活躍;許多居民擔心它很快就要噴發。"],["guide-114-24","Xiaoyoukeng, located in Yangmingshan National Park, is probably one of the best places to feel the pulsation of the \u0001volcano\u0002 under your feet.","位於陽明山國家公園的小油坑,大概是最能感受腳下火山脈動的地方之一。"]],"wheelchair (n.)":[["leader-112-67","My ankle was sprained, so walking was quite hard. I think I may need a \u0001wheelchair\u0002 for assistance at the airport.","我的腳踝扭傷了,走路很吃力。我想在機場可能需要輪椅協助。"],["leader-110-31","To provide a disabled-friendly lodging environment, the features of a guest room for people in a \u0001wheelchair\u0002 include lower cloth rails, an adjustable bed, a shower chair, and a raised toilet.","為提供身障友善的住宿環境,供輪椅使用者的客房設計特徵包括較低的掛桿、可調式床、淋浴椅和加高馬桶。"]],"accommodate (v.)":[["guide-113-16","Due to increased demand, the national park started issuing more permits for overnight camping to \u0001accommodate\u0002 more hikers.","由於需求增加,國家公園開始發放更多過夜露營許可證,以容納更多登山客。"],["guide-112-51","Designed by British architects, the hotel can \u0001accommodate\u0002 more than 700 people.","這家由英國建築師設計的飯店可容納超過 700 人。"]],"aircraft (n.)":[["leader-112-4","Please remain seated until the \"fasten seat belt\" sign is switched off and the \u0001aircraft\u0002 has come to a complete stop.","請保持坐著,直到「繫安全帶」燈號熄滅且飛機完全停妥。"],["leader-112-44","This is a non-smoking flight. Please be aware that smoking is prohibited on the entire \u0001aircraft\u0002.","本班機為禁菸航班。請注意,全機禁止吸菸。"]],"allergic (adj.)":[["guide-113-60","Many people are \u0001allergic\u0002 to pollen, and they experience symptoms like sneezing and itchy eyes during spring.","許多人對花粉過敏,他們在春天會出現打噴嚏、眼睛癢等症狀。"],["leader-112-66","B: Doctor, it seems I am \u0001allergic\u0002 to seafood.",""]],"architect (n.)":[["guide-112-51","Designed by British \u0001architects\u0002, the hotel can accommodate more than 700 people.","這家由英國建築師設計的飯店可容納超過 700 人。"],["leader-111-17","In 1666, the Great Fire burnt for three days and destroyed most buildings in London. The famous \u0001architect\u0002, Christopher Wren, designed many buildings after the Great Fire.","1666 年倫敦大火燒了三天,摧毀多數建築。著名建築師 Christopher Wren 在大火後設計了許多建築。"]],"arrange (v.)":[["guide-112-61","A concierge is someone who is employed in a hotel to help guests \u0001arrange\u0002 things, such as local tours, theatre tickets and restaurant reservations.","禮賓員是飯店雇用來協助客人安排事務(如當地旅遊、劇院票券和餐廳訂位)的人。"],["guide-111-66","A: Can I pick up the car at the airport? B: No, but we can \u0001arrange\u0002 for transportation to our lot.","A:我可以在機場取車嗎? B:不行,但我們可以安排交通接送到我們的租車場。"]],"booking (n.)":[["leader-107-63","Many airlines operate overbooking policies because a small number of passengers, having made their \u0001bookings\u0002, do not turn up for their flights.","許多航空公司採超額訂位政策,因為少數已訂位的乘客最後沒現身搭機。"],["leader-106-15","If you want to change your \u0001booking\u0002, we will try to help you, but we cannot guarantee that we will be able to do this.","如果你想改訂位,我們會盡力協助,但我們不能保證一定辦得到。"]],"boutique (n.)":[["leader-115-56","In the areas around this lake, you can find many \u0001boutiques\u0002 selling refined clothes and local handicrafts.","在這座湖周邊,你可以找到許多販售精緻服飾和當地手工藝品的精品店。"],["guide-115-15","In Taiwan, in addition to old-fashioned shopping streets, there are also lavish department stores with designer \u0001boutiques\u0002.","在台灣,除了老式商店街,也有奢華百貨公司,裡面有設計師精品店。"]],"carousel (n.)":[["leader-113-24","I couldn't find it on the \u0001carousel\u0002.",""],["leader-112-8","Normally, checked baggage will be delivered to the \u0001carousel\u0002 after the flight arrives, depending on the priority and the position of baggage.","通常班機抵達後,託運行李會送到行李轉盤,順序視優先級和行李位置而定。"]],"charge (v.)":[["leader-112-47","Changing money at the airport is convenient to get local currency, but you may be \u0001charged\u0002 some service fees.","在機場換錢方便取得當地貨幣,但可能被收手續費。"],["leader-111-20","International calls to mobile phones registered in another country are \u0001charged\u0002 higher rates. The first zero of an international number must be deleted since it is a \"trunk prefix\" only for domestic calls within many countries.","打到在他國註冊的手機的國際電話會被收取較高費率。國際號碼開頭的 0 須刪去,因它是在許多國家只供國內電話使用的「長途字冠」。"]],"chewy (adj.)":[["guide-115-21","Many people in Taiwan like drinking Pearl Milk Tea which usually consists of sweetened tea with milk and \u0001chewy\u0002 tapioca balls.","許多台灣人喜歡喝珍珠奶茶,通常是加了牛奶和有嚼勁粉圓(珍珠)的甜茶。"],["leader-112-30","Bubble tea most commonly consists of tea accompanied by \u0001chewy\u0002 tapioca balls (\"boba\" or \"pearls\").","珍珠奶茶最常見是茶加上有嚼勁的木薯(粉圓)球(即「波霸」或「珍珠」)。"]],"claim (v.)":[["leader-113-62","To \u0001claim\u0002 the tax refund, foreign travelers must apply at the port of their departure from Taiwan within a limited time of their purchase.","要申請退稅,外國旅客須在購買後限定時間內,於離台口岸辦理。"],["leader-112-6","A: Excuse me, I can't find my baggage. B: Do you have your \u0001claim\u0002 tag?","A:不好意思,我找不到行李。 B:你有行李領取牌嗎?"]],"collection (n.)":[["guide-115-62","The National Palace Museum houses the world's largest \u0001collection\u0002 of priceless Chinese art treasures.","故宮博物院收藏著全世界最大的無價中華藝術珍寶典藏。"],["leader-110-77","The decision to turn the Louvre into a massive repository of the world's greatest fine art \u0001collection\u0002 was proposed in 1981 by the French President François Mitterrand.","",4]],"conservation (n.)":[["guide-113-15","The \u0001conservation\u0002 of jungles and rainforests is critical to the survival of many species.","叢林與雨林的保育對許多物種的生存至關重要。"],["guide-113-46","More and more governments are making commitments to sustainable tourism by providing eco-friendly accommodations, \u0001conservation\u0002 efforts, and community engagement initiatives.","越來越多政府承諾推動永續觀光,提供環保住宿、保育行動與社區參與計畫。"]],"conserve (v.)":[["leader-113-33","The Geopark employs various methods to \u0001conserve\u0002 water, including rainwater harvesting and a closed-loop filtration system, while also replacing groundwater with recharge wells.","地質公園採用多種節水方法,包括雨水收集與閉迴路過濾系統,同時也用回補井取代地下水。"],["guide-112-29","Much of Taiwan's natural beauty and wealth are \u0001conserved\u0002 on the east coast of the island.","台灣大部分的自然美景與資源都保存在島嶼東海岸。"]],"consume (v.)":[["guide-110-8","A report indicates that Taiwanese people \u0001consume\u0002 almost 7.9 kilograms of apples per person every year, comparable to the quantity of bananas a Taiwanese has a year.","一份報告指出,台灣人每人每年食用將近 7.9 公斤蘋果,和台灣人一年吃的香蕉量相當。"],["leader-108-72","As a result, the imbalance between what nature replenishes and humans \u0001consume\u0002 will probably continue to grow.","",4]],"cost (n.)":[["leader-114-29","Medical tourism refers to traveling for medical treatment in other countries, often for better services or lower \u0001costs\u0002.","醫療旅遊指的是到其他國家接受醫療治療,通常是為了更好的服務或更低的費用。"],["leader-107-35","Weddings can be expensive. In this week's News Report you can hear about a way to cut the \u0001cost\u0002 of your wedding by 50%.","婚禮可能很花錢。本週新聞報導會告訴你把婚禮費用削減 50% 的方法。"]],"crowded (adj.)":[["guide-113-59","During the tour, the guide highlighted the assembly point in case the group got separated in the \u0001crowded\u0002 area.","導覽途中,導遊特別說明了集合點,以防團體在擁擠處走散。"],["guide-110-3","Telluride, a Victorian-era mining town in Colorado, is a winter paradise offering plenty to do and isn't as \u0001crowded\u0002 as some of Colorado's other destinations.","泰勒瑞德是科羅拉多州一座維多利亞時代的礦業小鎮,是個冬季天堂,有很多活動,也不像科羅拉多其他景點那麼擁擠。"]],"cruise (v.)":[["leader-113-58","\u0001Cruising\u0002 through the Caribbean, passengers enjoyed the warm sea breeze and crystal-clear waters.","搭郵輪航行加勒比海時,乘客享受溫暖海風和清澈海水。"],["leader-110-43","We are currently \u0001cruising\u0002 at an altitude of 3,300 feet at an airspeed of 400 miles per hour.",""]],"deposit (n.)":[["guide-112-41","Sir, we need your \u0001deposit\u0002 for a confirmed and guaranteed reservation.","先生,我們需要您的訂金來完成確認並保證的訂位。"],["leader-111-51","You pay a \u0001deposit\u0002 in advance to secure the reservation.",""]],"device (n.)":[["leader-109-79","Plastics revolutionized medicine with life-saving \u0001devices\u0002, made space travel possible, lightened cars and jets—saving fuel and pollution—and saved lives with helmets, incubators, and equipment for clean drinking water.","",4],["leader-108-10","Captain: Laptop computers and other electronic \u0001devices\u0002 cannot be used until 15 minutes after take-off, or after the seat belt sign has been turned on prior to landing.","機長:筆電和其他電子裝置,須在起飛 15 分鐘後、或降落前安全帶燈亮起後才不能使用。"]],"disrupt (v.)":[["guide-115-76","New findings from Lux Research suggest that while autonomous robotaxis will further \u0001disrupt\u0002 the conventional taxi and ride sharing spaces, car ownership will not be affected.","",1],["leader-114-19","Common sense tells us that behavior that \u0001disrupts\u0002 a classroom and disrupts the learning of others is not acceptable.","常識告訴我們,擾亂課堂、妨礙他人學習的行為是不可接受的。"]],"eligible (adj.)":[["guide-114-14","Foreign travelers who make purchases of at least NT$2,000 on the same day from the same designated stores with the “Taiwan Tax Refund”-label are \u0001eligible\u0002 to request the refund.","外國旅客在同一天於同一貼有「Taiwan Tax Refund」標誌的指定商店消費滿新台幣 2,000 元,即有資格申請退稅。"],["guide-113-36","You just need to find out if your country is \u0001eligible\u0002 for visa-free entry.",""]],"emission (n.)":[["guide-112-71","Unfortunately, airplanes are predicted to triple their CO2 \u0001emissions\u0002 by 2050 if left unchecked now.","",1],["leader-111-63","Many factors contribute to increased level of toxic gases and one factor which is often ignored by people is the \u0001emissions\u0002 of the public transportation.","許多因素導致有毒氣體增加,其中常被人們忽略的一項是大眾運輸的排放。"]],"erupt (v.)":[["guide-115-40","The volcano on the island has been unusually active over the past few days; many residents are afraid that it is going to \u0001erupt\u0002 in no time.","島上的火山過去幾天異常活躍;許多居民擔心它很快就要噴發。"],["leader-113-11","The geyser \u0001erupts\u0002 more frequently than any of the other big ones and is still as spectacular as it was a century ago.","這座間歇泉噴發比其他大型間歇泉更頻繁,至今仍和一世紀前一樣壯觀。"]],"essential (adj.)":[["leader-113-65","Before you undertake a journey through the Amazon rainforest, it's \u0001essential\u0002 to be well-prepared and informed.","在你展開穿越亞馬遜雨林的旅程前,充分準備和了解資訊至關重要。"],["guide-111-20","Shopping has converted into an \u0001essential\u0002 factor for many tourists when choosing a travel destination.","對許多遊客而言,購物已轉變成選擇旅遊目的地時的重要因素。"]],"exhibit (n.)":[["leader-115-60","In many museums, touching the \u0001exhibited\u0002 items is a behavior that is absolutely prohibited.","在許多博物館,觸摸展示品是絕對被禁止的行為。"],["guide-113-30","The controversial art \u0001exhibit\u0002 was designed to provoke thought and discussion among its viewers.","這場具爭議的藝術展旨在激發觀眾的思考與討論。"]],"expire (v.)":[["guide-114-70","In international practice, most countries and territories may refuse entry to a foreign visitor if their passport will \u0001expire\u0002 less than six months after the date of arrival.","依國際慣例,若外國旅客的護照在抵達日後不到六個月就到期,多數國家與地區可能拒絕其入境。"],["guide-112-44","Only when David was stopped by a policeman for drunk driving did he realize that his passport had \u0001expired\u0002 and he was forced to return home.","直到 David 因酒駕被警察攔下,他才意識到護照已過期,並被迫返國。"]],"habitat (n.)":[["guide-115-42","The rich topographic features and diverse vegetation of Taroko National Park bring about a variety of \u0001habitats\u0002 in which many life forms thrive.","太魯閣國家公園豐富的地形與多樣的植被,孕育出各種棲地,眾多生命形式在其中繁衍。"],["guide-114-68","The lowlands of Taiwan, especially the coasts, are important \u0001habitats\u0002 for seabirds and for wildlife associated with the few remaining undisturbed patches of tropical strand or mangrove trees.","台灣的低地,尤其是海岸,是海鳥及與少數僅存未受干擾的熱帶海濱林或紅樹林相關野生動物的重要棲地。"]],"inexpensive (adj.)":[["leader-113-60","In Europe, where travel distances are often short, it is usually more convenient and \u0001inexpensive\u0002 to travel by train than by airplane.","在歐洲,由於旅行距離常常很短,搭火車通常比搭飛機更方便且便宜。"],["guide-113-61","In Taiwan, you don't need to worry about traveling far to find eateries that offer \u0001inexpensive\u0002 food.","在台灣,你不用擔心要跑很遠才能找到提供便宜食物的餐館。"]],"insurance (n.)":[["guide-114-52","If you do not have appropriate \u0001insurance\u0002 before you travel, you could be liable for emergency expenses.","如果你在旅行前沒有適當的保險,可能需要自行負擔緊急費用。"],["leader-111-57","If you are sick when travelling, you could call the hospital and schedule an appointment. When you visit the hospital, you need to bring your health \u0001insurance\u0002 policy documents.","旅途中生病,可打電話給醫院預約。看診時要帶健康保險保單文件。"]],"issue (v.)":[["guide-113-16","Due to increased demand, the national park started \u0001issuing\u0002 more permits for overnight camping to accommodate more hikers.","由於需求增加,國家公園開始發放更多過夜露營許可證,以容納更多登山客。"],["leader-111-13","They can't be easily cashed, even at the banks that \u0001issued\u0002 them.",""]],"lantern (n.)":[["leader-115-11","The view gets even more romantic at night as cherry trees along the river are lighted up by charming paper \u0001lanterns\u0002.","夜裡景色更浪漫,沿河的櫻花樹被迷人的紙燈籠點亮。"],["guide-114-28","The Pingxi \u0001Lantern\u0002 Festival in New Taipei City is known as one of the best festivals in Taiwan. Thousands of lanterns are sent into the air as a form of prayer for good luck and blessings.","新北市的平溪天燈節是台灣最棒的節慶之一。成千上萬的天燈升空,作為祈求好運與祝福的一種方式。"]],"meal (n.)":[["guide-112-63","If you are not hungry, we can order one \u0001meal\u0002 and share it. The portions are very big.","如果你不餓,我們可以點一份餐一起分。這裡的份量很大。"],["leader-108-36","Do not undertake hard exercise for a few hours after a \u0001meal\u0002 to allow food to digest.","飯後幾小時內不要做劇烈運動,好讓食物消化。"]],"missing (adj.)":[["leader-113-24","I'm reporting a \u0001missing\u0002 suitcase.",""],["leader-112-31","You can go to the Lost and Found Service Center for your \u0001missing\u0002 items.","你可以到失物招領中心找你遺失的物品。"]],"operate (v.)":[["guide-115-60","Before departure, please check the airline's official website to confirm that your flight is \u0001operating\u0002 normally.","出發前,請查看航空公司官方網站,確認你的航班正常運作。"],["leader-111-45","Passenger: Could you show me how to \u0001operate\u0002 the in-flight entertainment?",""]],"operator (n.)":[["guide-114-44","The travel business has shown clearly that the largest setbacks came among the relatively cheap package tour \u0001operators\u0002, and especially with tours that have a low foreign currency content.","旅遊業已清楚顯示,最大的挫敗(衰退)發生在相對便宜的套裝行程業者身上,尤其是外幣占比低的行程。"],["leader-111-38","Guest: Please transfer my call to an international \u0001operator\u0002.",""]],"option (n.)":[["leader-114-80","Unlike traditional vacation cruises, the Odyssey offers a new growing trend: cruises are a new living \u0001option\u0002 for the rich.","",4],["guide-112-19","While beef may seem like a great choice for holidays and other special occasions, some research suggests it may not be the healthiest \u0001option\u0002.","雖然牛肉在節慶和其他特殊場合看似是絕佳選擇,但有些研究指出它可能不是最健康的選項。"]],"pandemic (n.)":[["guide-110-6","Despite global restrictions on travel due to the coronavirus \u0001pandemic\u0002, travel between the United States and Mexico has continued relatively unchecked through 2020.","儘管因新冠疫情全球對旅行實施限制,美墨之間的旅行在整個 2020 年仍相對不受阻礙地持續著。"],["guide-110-7","Air travel in the US took its biggest dive since World War II at the beginning of the \u0001pandemic\u0002 in 2020.",""]],"pharmacy (n.)":[["leader-114-35","Kate: Could you please tell me where the \u0001pharmacy\u0002 is?",""],["guide-113-57","The \u0001pharmacy\u0002 is where you can fill your prescriptions and purchase over-the-counter medications and health-related products.","藥局是你可以領處方藥、購買成藥與健康相關產品的地方。"]],"preference (n.)":[["leader-114-47","Wilson: Before we leave for the trip, can you fill out this questionnaire about your \u0001preferences\u0002?",""],["leader-114-71","Most travelers have a \u0001preference\u0002 for window or aisle seats when it comes to air travel, but have you ever given thought to which side of the plane you should sit on?","",4]],"preserve (v.)":[["guide-114-5","The historical value of the museum lies in its exterior design which \u0001preserves\u0002 the architectural trends of the early 20th century.","博物館的歷史價值在於其外觀設計保留了 20 世紀初的建築風潮。"],["leader-113-68","Tourists should always abide by the rules and regulations of the national parks they visit to \u0001preserve\u0002 the natural environment.","遊客應始終遵守所造訪國家公園的規章,以保護自然環境。"]],"promote (v.)":[["leader-111-54","Visitor Information Center could \u0001promote\u0002 regional tourism since it provides free information and encourages tourists to participate in local events and visit local attractions.","遊客服務中心能促進區域觀光,因它提供免費資訊,鼓勵遊客參與在地活動、造訪當地景點。"],["guide-111-15","Tourism is vital to the economy of a country; as a result, the National Tourism Authorities always try to \u0001promote\u0002 its national brand image.","觀光對一國經濟至關重要;因此,國家觀光機關總是努力推廣其國家品牌形象。"]],"purchase (n.)":[["guide-111-55","You can make big \u0001purchases\u0002 with your credit card. That way, you don't have to carry large amounts of cash.","你可以用信用卡進行大額消費(購物)。這樣就不必攜帶大量現金。"],["leader-110-21","That sign on the wall says 20 percent off on all \u0001purchases\u0002.",""]],"receptionist (n.)":[["leader-113-12","The \u0001receptionist\u0002 of a hotel is responsible for politely completing the check-in procedure and introducing the facilities and services the hotel provides.","飯店櫃台負責禮貌地完成入住手續,並介紹飯店提供的設施和服務。"],["leader-110-49","Traveler: May I have a local map? \u0001Receptionist\u0002: Sure, here you go.","旅客:能給我一張當地地圖嗎? 櫃台:當然,拿去吧。"]],"regulation (n.)":[["guide-114-9","Tour guides should be well-versed in the local history, landmarks, culture, and \u0001regulations\u0002.","導遊應對當地歷史、地標、文化與法規十分熟稔。"],["leader-113-68","Tourists should always abide by the rules and \u0001regulations\u0002 of the national parks they visit to preserve the natural environment.","遊客應始終遵守所造訪國家公園的規章,以保護自然環境。"]],"resident (n.)":[["leader-114-78","Also, wealthy \u0001residents\u0002 do not want to share their space with tourists.","",4],["leader-112-78","In Taiwan, Xiaoliuqiu (also called Little Liuqiu or Liuqiu), an island belonging to Pingtung County in Taiwan has a high number of sea turtles, and the majority of the \u0001residents\u0002 there have been aware of the importance of protecting sea turtles.","",4]],"restore (v.)":[["guide-113-71","Which of the following is closest in meaning to the word “\u0001restored\u0002” in the first paragraph?","下列何者與第一段的 restored 意思最接近?"],["guide-113-71","Due to natural disaster and damages caused by humans, the temple has been \u0001restored\u0002 several times.","",1]],"return (v.)":[["leader-113-41","Customer: I'd like to \u0001return\u0002 this blender.",""],["guide-112-46","If you are not completely satisfied with our product, you can \u0001return\u0002 it for a full refund.","如果你對我們的產品不完全滿意,可以退貨並獲得全額退款。"]],"ride (n.)":[["guide-114-29","Now many tourists come here to experience the \u0001ride\u0002.",""],["guide-113-6","It'll be about a 20-minute \u0001ride\u0002 to the hotel.",""]],"skyscraper (n.)":[["guide-115-65","Designed to look like a pole of bamboo, this \u0001skyscraper\u0002 is the tallest and most iconic landmark of the city.","這棟以竹節造型設計的摩天大樓(台北 101),是該市最高、最具代表性的地標。"],["leader-108-28","The Burj Khalifa is a \u0001skyscraper\u0002 in Dubai and has been the tallest building in the world since 2008.","哈里發塔是杜拜的一座摩天大樓,自 2008 年以來一直是世界最高的建築。"]],"snorkeling (n.)":[["guide-114-25","If you are staying near the coast in Taiwan, some homestays might offer activities like \u0001snorkeling\u0002 in the sea.","如果你在台灣海邊住宿,有些民宿可能提供像浮潛這類的海上活動。"],["leader-112-76","They come for scuba diving, SUP (stand-up paddling), \u0001snorkeling\u0002, and so on.","",1]],"steak (n.)":[["guide-113-4","Waitress: How would you like your \u0001steak\u0002?",""],["guide-113-54","Tour Leader: One of our guests absolutely loved the \u0001steak\u0002 tonight.",""]],"takeoff (n.)":[["leader-114-53","Before \u0001takeoff\u0002 and landing, flight attendants instruct passengers to place their seats in the upright position.","起飛和降落前,空服員指示乘客把座椅調到直立位置。"],["leader-113-61","All mobile phones must be switched to flight mode before \u0001takeoff\u0002 and landing.","所有手機在起飛和降落前必須切換到飛航模式。"]],"temple (n.)":[["leader-115-37","Tourist: Can we take photos inside the \u0001temple\u0002? Tour Guide: Yes, but please turn off the camera flash.","遊客:我們可以在寺廟內拍照嗎? 導遊:可以,但請關閉相機閃光燈。"],["guide-115-31","Longshan \u0001Temple\u0002, located in Wanhua, is one of Taipei's finest examples of Taiwan's architectural and historical heritage.","位於萬華的龍山寺,是台灣建築與歷史遺產的最佳範例之一。"]],"tip (n.)":[["leader-115-46","These essential travel \u0001tips\u0002 will help you avoid common travel mistakes and make the most of your journey.","這些必備的旅遊訣竅能幫你避免常見的旅行錯誤,充分享受旅程。"],["guide-109-21","When you tell the driver to “keep the change,” you are giving the change as a \u0001tip\u0002.","當你跟司機說「不用找了」,你是把找的零錢當小費給他。"]],"trail (n.)":[["guide-115-22","The \u0001trail\u0002 around Sun Moon Lake in Nantou is listed as one of the 10 best cycling routes in the world by CNN.","南投日月潭的環湖步道被 CNN 列為全球十大最佳自行車路線之一。"],["leader-114-11","Many national parks have \u0001trails\u0002 and reachable adventures, allowing everyone to enjoy the beauty of America's protected spaces.","許多國家公園有步道和可及的探險活動,讓每個人都能享受美國受保護空間之美。"]],"transportation (n.)":[["leader-115-14","To make getting around the city easier, the tour leader suggested that everyone buy a \u0001transportation\u0002 pass, which allows unlimited travel on buses and trains for a set period.","為了方便在市區移動,領隊建議大家買一張交通票券,可在一段期間內無限搭乘公車和火車。"],["leader-111-11","Receptionist: Our one-day package tour includes a guided tour of the city and free \u0001transportation\u0002. Guest: That sounds perfect.","櫃台:我們的一日套裝行程含城市導覽和免費接送(交通)。 客人:聽起來很完美。"]],"validity (n.)":[["leader-115-64","It is common sense that before booking your international flight, you should always check the \u0001validity\u0002 of your passport to ensure it meets the entry requirements for your destination country.","常識是,預訂國際航班前,你應該先檢查護照的有效性(效期),以確保符合目的地國的入境要求。"],["leader-113-76","First, the \u0001validity\u0002 of your passport can be an easy oversight.","",1]],"viable (adj.)":[["guide-115-19","If your goal is to catch an early High-Speed Rail (HSR) train to Taichung, the 6:00 A.M. MRT is the earliest \u0001viable\u0002 option from the airport.","如果你的目標是搭早班高鐵到台中,清晨 6 點的捷運是從機場出發最早、可行的選擇。"],["leader-114-80","What does the word \"\u0001viable\u0002\" (in the last paragraph) mean?","(最後一段中)「viable」一字的意思是?"]],"visa (n.)":[["leader-115-32","Officers at immigration check all passports and \u0001visas\u0002 before travelers can enter the country.","入境查驗處的官員會查驗所有護照和簽證,旅客才能入境。"],["leader-115-62","Aliens who overstay their \u0001visas\u0002 would be deported back to their country of birth.","逾期居留簽證的外國人會被遣返回其出生國。"]],"access (n.)":[["leader-115-67","That museum is very old and not friendly to tourists who need elevator \u0001access\u0002.","那間博物館很老舊,對需要電梯通道(使用)的遊客不太友善。"],["guide-115-39","In Taiwan, special rental places such as \"whole-house lodging\" can be found. You can rent a whole house just for your party and have \u0001access\u0002 to your own private facilities.","在台灣可找到「整棟出租(包棟民宿)」這類特別的租宿。你可以只為自己的團體租下整棟房子,擁有使用自己專屬設施的權利。"]],"accident (n.)":[["leader-112-20","We missed the warning signs and that's why the car \u0001accident\u0002 happened.","我們錯過了警告標誌,所以才發生車禍。"],["leader-111-16","Tourist: Sir, a car \u0001accident\u0002 just happened across the street.",""]],"accompany (v.)":[["leader-110-14","Fresh herbs such as chives and parsley are essential ingredients in the sauces that \u0001accompany\u0002 most French savory dishes.","細香蔥、巴西里等新鮮香草是醬汁的必要食材,這些醬汁搭配多數法式鹹食。"],["guide-109-52","Let me remind you that all children must be \u0001accompanied\u0002 by an adult in the art center.","提醒你,在藝術中心所有孩童都必須有大人陪同。"]],"account (n.)":[["leader-111-64","At public places such as libraries, hotels, and airports, free Wi-Fi is very convenient but not secure. Travelers should avoid logging into bank \u0001accounts\u0002 and entering passwords at these public areas because someone else might see them.","在圖書館、飯店、機場等公共場所,免費 Wi-Fi 很方便但不安全。旅客應避免在這些公共區域登入銀行帳戶或輸入密碼,以免被他人看到。"],["leader-107-60","When you are traveling, try to avoid logging into bank \u0001accounts\u0002 or entering any passwords while using free public WiFi at a place like an airport.","旅行時,在機場等地用免費公共 WiFi,盡量避免登入銀行帳戶或輸入任何密碼。"]],"achieve (v.)":[["leader-115-58","Find out why customers have come on holidays, what they want to do, and then help them to \u0001achieve\u0002 their dream.","找出顧客為何來度假、他們想做什麼,然後幫他們實現夢想。"],["leader-115-80","According to the text, which of the following is necessary to \u0001achieve\u0002 net zero before 2050?","根據本文,下列何者是 2050 年前達成淨零的必要條件?"]],"affordable (adj.)":[["leader-112-40","Taiwan has become more and more popular among foreign tourists because it is quite \u0001affordable\u0002 and friendly.","台灣越來越受外國旅客歡迎,因為它相當物價實惠又友善。"],["guide-112-7","She is now looking for \u0001affordable\u0002 airline tickets in order to return to her homeland soon.","她現在正在找負擔得起的機票,以便盡快返回家鄉。"]],"airsickness (n.)":[["leader-112-10","Flight attendant: You seem to have some \u0001airsickness\u0002. B: Yes, do you have medicine for that?","空服員:您似乎有點暈機。 乘客:是的,你們有暈機藥嗎?"],["leader-112-45","Here is the \u0001airsickness\u0002 bag, right in front of your seat pocket.",""]],"amenity (n.)":[["guide-113-27","The new luxury hotel boasts a capacity of 500 guests, offering them unparalleled comfort and \u0001amenities\u0002.","這家新的豪華飯店以可容納 500 位客人的容量自豪,為他們提供無與倫比的舒適與設施。"],["guide-112-12","Most premium airlines provide passengers with superior levels of comfort, seats, \u0001amenities\u0002, and luggage management.","大多數高級航空公司為乘客提供更優越的舒適度、座椅、設施與行李管理。"]],"apologize (v.)":[["leader-114-27","I \u0001apologize\u0002 on behalf of the company for our waitress's error, and we will cover the cost of dry cleaning.","我代表公司為我們服務生的錯誤道歉,我們會負擔乾洗費用。"],["leader-113-19","This is your captain speaking. We \u0001apologize\u0002 for our late departure, but as is sometimes the case at San Francisco, the fog was too thick for taking off.","我是機長。我們為延遲起飛道歉,但如舊金山常有的情況,霧太濃無法起飛。"]],"appetizer (n.)":[["guide-113-44","The restaurant's \u0001appetizers\u0002, including crispy calamari, stuffed mushrooms, and savory sliders, left us eagerly anticipating the main course.","這家餐廳的開胃菜,包括酥炸花枝、鑲蘑菇和美味小漢堡,讓我們熱切期待主餐。"],["leader-107-18","We ordered two \u0001appetizers\u0002, chicken wings and Mozzarella sticks, salad and soup before the main dish.","我們在主菜前點了兩道開胃菜——雞翅和莫札瑞拉起司條、沙拉和湯。"]],"appliance (n.)":[["guide-115-57","Taiwan uses electric current of 110 volts at 60 cycles; \u0001appliances\u0002 from Europe, Australia, or South-East Asia will need a(n) converter or transformer.","台灣使用 110 伏特、60 赫茲的電流;來自歐洲、澳洲或東南亞的電器會需要轉換器或變壓器。"],["guide-114-15","Taiwan uses electric current of 110 volts at 60 cycles, so \u0001appliances\u0002 from Europe, Australia or South-East Asia will need an adapter or transformer.","台灣使用 110 伏特、60 赫茲的電流,所以來自歐洲、澳洲或東南亞的電器會需要轉接器或變壓器。"]],"application (n.)":[["guide-115-47","It takes approximately five working days (excluding weekends and national holidays) to process passport \u0001applications\u0002.","護照申請的辦理大約需要五個工作天(不含週末與國定假日)。"],["leader-112-12","To maintain your rights, please arrive at the airport three hours prior to your departure time for tax refund \u0001application\u0002.","為保障權益,請於出發前三小時抵達機場辦理退稅申請。"]],"architecture (n.)":[["leader-115-68","The \u0001architecture\u0002 of this building is typical of the Renaissance age, and many tourists enjoy visiting this place.","這棟建築的建築(風格)是文藝復興時期的典型,許多遊客喜歡來參觀。"],["guide-114-32","The \u0001architecture\u0002 of the Old Taichung Train Station is a mix of traditional Japanese and late Renaissance themes. It is now listed as a national monument.","台中舊火車站的建築融合了傳統日式與晚期文藝復興的風格。它現在被列為國定古蹟。"]],"arrival (n.)":[["leader-115-34","The crowd waited anxiously at the terminal for the \u0001arrival\u0002 of the VIP guests.","群眾在航廈焦急地等待貴賓的到來。"],["guide-109-68","If you find your baggage damaged after the \u0001arrival\u0002 of your flight, report to the Airport Service Office immediately.","若你在班機抵達後發現行李受損,請立刻向機場服務處通報。"]],"artifact (n.)":[["leader-114-55","The team made an incredible discovery at the archaeological site, uncovering \u0001artifacts\u0002 that were thousands of years old.","團隊在考古遺址有驚人發現,挖掘出數千年前的文物。"],["guide-114-33","The National Palace Museum is home to hundreds of thousands of ancient Chinese \u0001artifacts\u0002 and artwork, which are of great historical value.","故宮博物院收藏著數十萬件古代中華文物與藝術品,深具歷史價值。"]],"atmosphere (n.)":[["leader-115-10","This ancient city is a must-visit destination for every tourist to experience the traditional culture and old town \u0001atmosphere\u0002.","這座古城是每位遊客必訪的目的地,可體驗傳統文化與老城氛圍。"],["leader-109-24","Natalie: I like the \u0001atmosphere\u0002 in your restaurant.",""]],"authorities (n.)":[["leader-113-14","The \u0001authorities\u0002 have touted their efforts in protecting the environment during the $2 billion project.","當局在這 20 億美元的計畫中大力標榜他們保護環境的努力。"],["guide-113-31","In the unfortunate event of a group member's accidental demise during a foreign trip, it is necessary to obtain an official death certificate from local \u0001authorities\u0002.",""]],"aviation (n.)":[["guide-112-73","The \u0001aviation\u0002 sector has released huge amounts of carbon dioxide (CO2) into the atmosphere every year.","",4],["leader-111-69","Pilots and air traffic controllers are all proficient in \u0001aviation\u0002 English as well as everyday English.","機師和航管人員都精通航空英語和日常英語。"]],"baggage (n.)":[["guide-113-21","First, your \u0001baggage\u0002 pick-up time is 9:00 a.m. tomorrow morning, and please have all your baggage ready and put them outside your room by 9:00 a.m.",""],["leader-112-6","A: Excuse me, I can't find my \u0001baggage\u0002. B: Do you have your claim tag?","A:不好意思,我找不到行李。 B:你有行李領取牌嗎?"]],"ban (v.)":[["guide-110-4","Taiwan has become the first country in Asia to totally \u0001ban\u0002 the eating of dog and cat meat, and violating the rule is punishable by up to $8,000 in fines.","台灣成為亞洲第一個完全禁止食用貓狗肉的國家,違規者最高可罰 8,000 元。"],["guide-110-52","The temple is unique in that the burning of incense is \u0001banned\u0002 in the interest of the environment.","這座廟宇獨特之處在於,為了環境,禁止燒香。"]],"bargain (n.)":[["leader-111-24","It is already a real \u0001bargain\u0002.",""],["guide-109-56","I heard books are on sale in the store this month. Maybe we can get a good \u0001bargain\u0002 there.","我聽說這個月書店特價,也許我們能在那撿到划算貨。"]],"beverage (n.)":[["guide-114-35","Drink stores can be found practically anywhere in built-up areas in Taiwan. Most of the \u0001beverages\u0002 at these places involve tea.","在台灣的鬧區幾乎到處都能找到飲料店。這些店裡大部分的飲料都含茶。"],["leader-109-46","Non-alcoholic \u0001beverages\u0002 are complimentary on all the flights. You don't have to pay for them.","所有航班上的無酒精飲料都是免費招待的,你不用付錢。"]],"bicycle (n.)":[["leader-109-66","This is a city for \u0001bicycles\u0002 and more tourists are adopting this way of exploring the city.","這是座適合單車的城市,越來越多遊客採用這種探索城市的方式。"],["guide-108-33","On the MRT of Taiwan, visitors carrying \u0001bicycles\u0002 can get on and off the train only at designated stations.","在台灣捷運,攜帶單車的旅客只能在指定車站上下車。"]],"biodiversity (n.)":[["guide-115-71","Drawing on Alishan's ecological treasures, the train blends striking design with the experience of exploring Alishan's rich \u0001biodiversity\u0002, making the Vivid Express a truly unique journey.","",1],["leader-113-45","Ecological tourism encourages sustainable travel, fostering appreciation for natural wonders while promoting conservation efforts crucial for preserving our planet's \u0001biodiversity\u0002.","生態旅遊鼓勵永續旅行,培養對自然奇景的欣賞,同時推動對保護地球生物多樣性至關重要的保育工作。"]],"block (n.)":[["leader-114-35","When you leave the hotel, turn left and go straight for two \u0001blocks\u0002 until you get to the intersection.",""],["leader-113-38","You need to head down this street, and it's just a few \u0001blocks\u0002 that way.",""]],"board (v.)":[["guide-115-58","You need a passport to \u0001board\u0002 an international flight and to enter a country.","你需要護照才能登上國際航班並進入一個國家。"],["leader-110-46","Flight attendants can help travelers with young kids to \u0001board\u0002 earlier for their convenience.","空服員可協助帶幼童的旅客提早登機,以方便他們。"]],"border (n.)":[["leader-114-70","The inspector expressed his concerns about the lack of an adequate effort to enforce customs laws along the \u0001border\u0002.","稽查員表達他對邊境缺乏足夠努力執行海關法規的擔憂。"],["leader-110-61","Due to the influences of the COVID-19, our \u0001border\u0002 has been closed since last March.","由於 COVID-19 的影響,我們的國界自去年三月起關閉。"]],"browse (v.)":[["leader-109-52","Clerk: Can I help you find anything? Customer: I'm just \u0001browsing\u0002.","店員:需要我幫你找什麼嗎? 顧客:我只是隨便看看。"],["guide-108-52","For some passengers, \u0001browsing\u0002 the duty-free catalogue during the flight is a highlight of the journey.","對某些旅客來說,飛行中瀏覽免稅商品目錄是旅程的一大亮點。"]],"budget (adj.)":[["guide-115-43","By using a variety of cost-cutting strategies, from charging for extras like checked baggage and meals to operating more efficient aircraft, \u0001budget\u0002 airlines have revolutionized air travel, making it accessible to millions.","透過各種削減成本的策略——從托運行李、餐點等額外收費,到操作更省油的飛機——平價航空公司(廉航)徹底革新了航空旅行,讓數百萬人都能負擔。"],["guide-113-62","Hotels operated by chains normally provide accommodations ranging from \u0001budget\u0002 to luxurious ones. However, there are still many privately owned inns and hotels that provide much less expensive rooms and meals than chain hotels.","連鎖經營的飯店通常提供從平價到豪華不等的住宿。然而,仍有許多私人經營的旅館提供比連鎖飯店便宜許多的房間與餐點。"]],"cabin (n.)":[["leader-114-76","Passengers can purchase or rent \u0001cabins\u0002 for up to 15 years.","",1],["leader-112-2","When the pressure drops in the \u0001cabin\u0002, oxygen masks will fall.","當機艙壓力下降時,氧氣面罩會落下。"]],"cash (n.)":[["leader-111-30","Customs officer: Do you have anything to declare? Traveler: Yes, I have NT$100,000 dollars in \u0001cash\u0002 with me.","海關人員:你有任何東西要申報嗎? 旅客:有,我帶了 10 萬元台幣現金。"],["guide-111-55","You can make big purchases with your credit card. That way, you don't have to carry large amounts of \u0001cash\u0002.","你可以用信用卡進行大額消費(購物)。這樣就不必攜帶大量現金。"]],"certificate (n.)":[["leader-111-40","If your passport is lost or stolen abroad, and you need to return to Taiwan right away, you may apply for a(n) \"Entry \u0001Certificate\u0002 for the Republic of China Nationals.\"","若你在國外遺失或被竊護照,又需立刻返台,可申請「中華民國國民入國證明書」。"],["leader-108-65","A marriage \u0001certificate\u0002 is an official statement that two people are married. In most countries, it is issued by a government official only after the civil registration of the marriage.","結婚證書是兩人已婚的官方證明;在多數國家,須待婚姻完成民事登記後,才由政府官員核發。"]],"check-in (n.)":[["guide-114-49","Make sure that your luggage has successfully passed through X-ray inspection before you leave the \u0001check-in\u0002 area.","離開報到區前,請確認你的行李已順利通過 X 光檢查。"],["leader-113-12","The receptionist of a hotel is responsible for politely completing the \u0001check-in\u0002 procedure and introducing the facilities and services the hotel provides.","飯店櫃台負責禮貌地完成入住手續,並介紹飯店提供的設施和服務。"]],"cliff (n.)":[["leader-115-33","Please keep a safe distance between yourself and the \u0001cliff\u0002 edge while taking photos.","拍照時請與懸崖邊緣保持安全距離。"],["guide-115-64","People come to Taroko National Park for its natural wonders. It features majestic \u0001cliffs\u0002, waterfalls, and blue streams.","人們來太魯閣國家公園是為了它的自然奇景。它以雄偉的峭壁、瀑布與湛藍溪流著稱。"]],"coastal (adj.)":[["guide-115-26","Taking up the entire southern tip of Taiwan, Kenting is a \u0001coastal\u0002 playground that lends itself to everything from diving and windsurfing to a growing surfing scene.","佔據台灣最南端的墾丁是個海濱樂園,從潛水、風浪板到日益興盛的衝浪都很適合。"],["guide-113-9","The park's landscape features unique \u0001coastal\u0002 rock formations shaped by natural forces over several million years.","這座公園的地景以…為特色,擁有由自然力量歷經數百萬年塑造的獨特海岸岩層。"]],"commission (n.)":[["guide-112-24","Most tour guides earn \u0001commission\u0002 on sales in addition to their base salary.","大多數導遊除了底薪外,還從銷售中賺取佣金。"],["guide-108-55","If you want to cash your traveler's checks, you must pay a handling charge. We charge a 2% \u0001commission\u0002 on each check.","若你想兌現旅行支票,必須付手續費。我們每張收 2% 佣金。"]],"complaint (n.)":[["leader-109-28","The clerk couldn't deal with the guest's \u0001complaint\u0002, so he asked the manager for help to sort out the problem.","店員無法處理客人的抱怨,所以找經理幫忙解決問題。"],["guide-107-60","One tip for dealing with difficult customers is to put your emotions aside when listening to their \u0001complaints\u0002 or concerns and sincerely thank them for sharing.","應對難纏客人的一個訣竅是:傾聽他們的抱怨或疑慮時放下情緒,並真誠感謝他們分享。"]],"concern (n.)":[["leader-114-15","Scientists found harmful particles in dolphins' breath off Florida, raising \u0001concerns\u0002 for their health and the environment.","科學家在佛州外海海豚的呼吸中發現有害微粒,引發對牠們健康和環境的擔憂。"],["leader-112-75","What is one of the causes that raise people's environmental \u0001concerns\u0002?","引起人們環境關切的原因之一是什麼?"]],"concert (n.)":[["leader-113-22","I have got two complimentary tickets for the \u0001concert\u0002 on next Saturday evening from my boss.",""],["leader-108-39","Many people are queuing up outside the hall for tickets to the \u0001concert\u0002 featuring a talented pianist.","許多人在會堂外排隊買這場才華洋溢鋼琴家演奏會的票。"]],"confiscate (v.)":[["leader-114-46","The security officer had to \u0001confiscate\u0002 the prohibited items from the passenger's luggage.","安檢人員必須從乘客行李中沒收違禁品。"],["leader-113-54","Customs Officer: I'm sorry, sir, but we need to \u0001confiscate\u0002 the fruits in your luggage.",""]],"conflict (n.)":[["guide-113-12","When you are faced with a \u0001conflict\u0002, raising your voice is never a successful way to settle the disagreement.","當你面臨衝突時,提高音量絕不是解決歧見的成功方法。"],["guide-108-62","Since the cessation of the \u0001conflict\u0002 over two decades ago, many people have visited Kinmen, which boasts famous specialties and souvenirs.","自從二十多年前衝突停止以來,許多人造訪金門,那裡以名產與伴手禮聞名。"]],"congestion (n.)":[["guide-114-30","Taiwan's metro system has been praised by locals for its effectiveness in relieving growing traffic \u0001congestion\u0002 in Taipei and its surrounding satellite towns.","台灣的捷運系統因有效紓解台北及周邊衛星城鎮日益嚴重的交通壅塞,而受到當地人稱讚。"],["leader-108-35","Since traffic \u0001congestion\u0002 around the airport is expected during the holidays, travelers should leave home early.","由於假期機場周邊預計會塞車,旅客應提早出門。"]],"connect (v.)":[["leader-115-44","Passenger: Is there Wi-Fi available on this flight? Flight Attendant: Yes, you can \u0001connect\u0002 after takeoff using the instructions provided.","乘客:這班機有 Wi-Fi 嗎? 空服員:有,起飛後你可以依照提供的說明連線。"],["guide-113-77","People are more eager than ever to \u0001connect\u0002 with the real roots of their visiting places.","",4]],"convert (v.)":[["guide-114-43","An interpreter is a person who \u0001converts\u0002 a thought or expression of a source language into an expression with a comparable meaning in a target language.","口譯員是把來源語言的想法或表達轉換成目標語言中意義相當之表達的人。"],["guide-112-8","When traveling abroad, you should carefully choose the money changers to \u0001convert\u0002 currencies.","出國旅行時,你應謹慎選擇換匯處來兌換貨幣。"]],"coupon (n.)":[["guide-112-47","In the travel brochures, you'll find information about tours, itineraries, maps, discounts and \u0001coupons\u0002, or package holidays.","在旅遊簡介手冊裡,你會找到關於行程、路線、地圖、折扣與優惠券,或套裝假期的資訊。"],["leader-109-31","Helen treated everyone from the office to that restaurant because she had a \u0001coupon\u0002 for 30% off.","Helen 請全辦公室的人去那間餐廳,因為她有一張 7 折折價券。"]],"crowd (n.)":[["leader-114-22","At the large, unruly gathering, glass bottles and cans were thrown at police officers as they tried to break up the \u0001crowd\u0002.","在那場大型失序的聚集中,玻璃瓶和罐子被扔向警察,警察試圖驅散人群。"],["guide-109-78","“Bunches of selfie sticks” is an indication of tourist \u0001crowd\u0002.","「成堆的自拍棒」代表什麼?"]],"cruise (n.)":[["leader-114-76","During the pandemic, the \u0001cruise\u0002 industry faced many challenges and financial losses.","",1],["leader-113-9","A: Why do you opt for a \u0001cruise\u0002 holiday? B: Well, I choose it because it offers fully inclusive holidays, which cover meals, entertainment, and tours ashore.","A:你為何選郵輪假期? B:因為它提供全包式假期,含餐點、娛樂和岸上觀光。"]],"customary (adj.)":[["guide-112-21","In many countries, it is \u0001customary\u0002 to leave a gratuity while dining out.","在許多國家,外出用餐時留小費是慣例。"],["guide-108-14","It is \u0001customary\u0002 to leave a tip for your maid.","給房務員留小費是慣例。"]],"delay (n.)":[["leader-114-39","The airline made an announcement over the loudspeaker, informing passengers of a \u0001delay\u0002 due to weather conditions.","航空公司透過廣播系統做了宣布/廣播,告知乘客因天候因素延誤。"],["leader-110-35","We are truly sorry for the \u0001delay\u0002.",""]],"delicacy (n.)":[["guide-115-52","Changhua is noted for its many temples as well as its unique local \u0001delicacies\u0002, such as ba-wan, mao-shu noodle, and braised pork with rice.","彰化以眾多廟宇聞名,也以獨特的在地美食著稱,例如肉圓、貓鼠麵與滷肉飯。"],["guide-110-71","From local \u0001delicacies\u0002 to exotic culinary delights, Taiwan offers a whole array of food choices that cater to all tastes.","",1]],"deliver (v.)":[["leader-106-71","In Hindi, the word dabba refers to lunch box and walla means carrier or \u0001deliver\u0002 man.","",4]],"depart (v.)":[["guide-115-56","Normally, the earliest Airport MRT from Taoyuan International Airport to the Taoyuan HSR Station \u0001departs\u0002 at 6:02 A.M.","通常,從桃園國際機場到桃園高鐵站最早的機場捷運在早上 6:02 發車。"],["guide-111-39","Before going abroad, make sure that your passport must be valid for another six months before you \u0001depart\u0002 for international travel.","出國前,務必確認你的護照在出發做國際旅行前還有至少六個月的有效期。"]],"design (v.)":[["guide-112-51","\u0001Designed\u0002 by British architects, the hotel can accommodate more than 700 people.","這家由英國建築師設計的飯店可容納超過 700 人。"],["leader-111-17","In 1666, the Great Fire burnt for three days and destroyed most buildings in London. The famous architect, Christopher Wren, \u0001designed\u0002 many buildings after the Great Fire.","1666 年倫敦大火燒了三天,摧毀多數建築。著名建築師 Christopher Wren 在大火後設計了許多建築。"]],"detour (n.)":[["leader-112-56","I am afraid that part of the highway to the airport is under construction, so you may need to take a \u0001detour\u0002.","恐怕往機場的部分公路正在施工,所以你可能得繞道。"],["guide-106-5","On multi-lane highways, traffic shifts can be utilized in lieu of a \u0001detour\u0002 as turn lanes can often be congested with detours.","在多線道公路上,可用車道調撥取代改道,因為轉彎車道常因改道而壅塞。"]],"dial (v.)":[["guide-112-13","Do I need to \u0001dial\u0002 the international area code while making a call abroad?","打國際電話時,我需要撥國際區碼嗎?"],["leader-111-14","Foreign guest: How could I use this public phone to make a collect call? Tour leader: Please \u0001dial\u0002 108.","外國客人:我怎麼用這支公共電話打對方付費電話? 領隊:請撥 108。"]],"dimension (n.)":[["leader-112-36","Hand luggage carried aboard aircraft by passengers must be within the following \u0001dimensions\u0002: length 56 cm, width 36 cm, height 23 cm.","乘客帶上機的手提行李須在下列尺寸內:長 56 公分、寬 36 公分、高 23 公分。"]],"diverse (adj.)":[["guide-115-42","The rich topographic features and \u0001diverse\u0002 vegetation of Taroko National Park bring about a variety of habitats in which many life forms thrive.","太魯閣國家公園豐富的地形與多樣的植被,孕育出各種棲地,眾多生命形式在其中繁衍。"],["guide-110-74","As you make your way through different destinations, you are bound to encounter a cultural mosaic of \u0001diverse\u0002 highlights, traditions, and events.","",4]],"dormant (adj.)":[["guide-115-8","Right on Taipei's doorstep, the easy-to-reach national park of Yangmingshan is a geological haven to hiking trails, bubbling hot springs, some challenging cycling routes and several \u0001dormant\u0002 volcanoes.","陽明山國家公園近在台北門口、交通便利,是地質天堂,有步道、沸騰溫泉、具挑戰性的自行車路線和數座休眠火山。"],["leader-113-27","A volcano which has been \u0001dormant\u0002 for nearly two centuries erupted in Iceland last week.","一座休眠近兩世紀的火山上週在冰島噴發。"]],"edge (n.)":[["leader-115-33","Please keep a safe distance between yourself and the cliff \u0001edge\u0002 while taking photos.","拍照時請與懸崖邊緣保持安全距離。"],["leader-111-79","What does the author mean \"Virtual reality can give you an \u0001edge\u0002 over rivals who have not yet adopted it\"?","作者說「VR 能讓你贏過尚未採用它的對手」是什麼意思?"]],"employee (n.)":[["leader-111-74","It is then picked up by an Alibaba \u0001employee\u0002 and carried the rest of the way.","",4],["leader-106-24","An \u0001employee\u0002 who can do business in more than one language is a valuable asset to most companies.","能用多種語言做生意的員工,對多數公司是寶貴的資產。"]],"endangered (adj.)":[["guide-112-76","In my experience, seeing iconic and \u0001endangered\u0002 animals like lions, elephants, and gorillas in their natural habitats is expected to be a staple of a safari vacation.","",1],["guide-111-26","The Formosan black bear is a species indigenous to Taiwan and currently listed as “\u0001endangered\u0002” under Taiwan's Wildlife Conservation Act.","台灣黑熊是原生於台灣的物種,目前依《野生動物保育法》被列為「瀕危」。"]],"enhance (v.)":[["leader-114-49","A nicer room would really \u0001enhance\u0002 our stay.",""],["guide-114-11","An important part of guiding is building rapport with tourists to \u0001enhance\u0002 their experience.","帶團的重要一環是與遊客建立融洽關係,以提升他們的體驗。"]],"erosion (n.)":[["guide-114-65","Uplifting, followed by \u0001erosion\u0002 by rivers, caused the formation of most of the geological features of Taroko Gorge.","地殼抬升,加上河流的侵蝕,造就了太魯閣峽谷大部分的地質特徵。"],["leader-108-75","In West Virginia (USA), for example, loggers in certified forests must receive special training to avoid causing soil \u0001erosion\u0002.","",4]],"escalator (n.)":[["guide-111-12","You can get to Baggage Claim by going down the \u0001escalator\u0002 and following the signs.","你可以下手扶梯後照著標示走到行李提領處。"],["guide-110-48","In case of emergency, open the transparent plastic cover and press the red button to stop the \u0001escalator\u0002.","緊急情況時,打開透明塑膠蓋並按紅色按鈕停止手扶梯。"]],"estimate (v.)":[["guide-113-56","Captain: We're thrilled to have you with us today and hope you're as excited as we are for this journey ahead. Our flight time today is \u0001estimated\u0002 to be approximately five hours.","機長:今天很高興有您同行,希望您和我們一樣期待這趟旅程。今天的飛行時間預估約五小時。"],["guide-113-68","Women are more attracted by spa holidays than men. While spa usage among men is increasing, it was \u0001estimated\u0002 that over 65% of spa customers are female.","女性比男性更受水療假期吸引。雖然男性使用水療的比例在增加,但據估計超過 65% 的水療顧客是女性。"]],"excursion (n.)":[["leader-113-44","During our exciting \u0001excursion\u0002, we explored ancient ruins, savored exotic cuisine, and connected with locals, making our travel unforgettable.","在這趟刺激的短程旅遊中,我們探索古蹟、品嚐異國料理、與當地人交流,讓旅程難忘。"],["guide-111-76","Off-train \u0001excursions\u0002 include a stop in Kimberley, a historical diamond-rush town.","",1]],"exotic (adj.)":[["leader-115-5","If you plan to try some \u0001exotic\u0002 dishes when traveling to a different country, please do some research about what those dishes are.","如果你到不同國家想嘗試一些異國風味的菜,請先研究一下那些是什麼菜。"],["leader-113-44","During our exciting excursion, we explored ancient ruins, savored \u0001exotic\u0002 cuisine, and connected with locals, making our travel unforgettable.","在這趟刺激的短程旅遊中,我們探索古蹟、品嚐異國料理、與當地人交流,讓旅程難忘。"]],"experience (n.)":[["leader-110-3","Tom: Do not go into it for money. The most rewarding aspect of my job is that I go to different places and talk about my own travel \u0001experiences\u0002.","Tom:別為錢入這行。我工作最有成就感的部分,是能到不同地方、分享自己的旅遊經驗。"],["leader-106-28","Anybody looking for a truly heavenly \u0001experience\u0002 will think that they have walked into paradise at the Chocolate Show in New York.","任何想尋求極致美妙體驗的人,到紐約巧克力展會覺得自己彷彿走進了天堂。"]],"feature (n.)":[["leader-114-76","According to the passage, what is the main \u0001feature\u0002 of the Odyssey?","根據本文,Odyssey 的主要特色是什麼?"],["leader-112-74","Which \u0001feature\u0002 are green products known for?","綠色產品以什麼特色聞名?"]],"fee (n.)":[["guide-113-47","A: Is there a complimentary meal on the flight? B: No, but there's a selection of refreshments available for a small \u0001fee\u0002.","A:飛機上有免費餐點嗎? B:沒有,但有一些點心可付少許費用購買。"],["guide-111-13","The last thing you want on a vacation is to find out hidden \u0001fees\u0002 that you must pay.","度假時你最不想遇到的,就是發現隱藏的費用得付。"]],"fermented (adj.)":[["leader-108-8","Tom: What's the signature dish of your restaurant? Attendant: Clay pot chicken in \u0001fermented\u0002 red rice wine.","Tom:你們餐廳的招牌菜是什麼? 服務員:紅糟醃雞煲。"],["guide-108-61","The tofu is left in \u0001fermented\u0002 milk and some ingredients for months, making it pungent and tasty.","豆腐浸在發酵的滷汁與一些原料中數月,讓它變得氣味濃烈又美味(臭豆腐)。"]],"firecracker (n.)":[["guide-114-66","Yenshui Fireworks Festival originated in the past when people would ask the gods for help to get rid of the epidemic in Yenshui, and they would set off \u0001firecrackers\u0002 to welcome the arrival of the gods.","鹽水蜂炮節起源於過去,當時鹽水人祈求神明協助驅除瘟疫,並施放鞭炮迎接神明降臨。"],["guide-109-13","People decorate their homes with plastic \u0001firecrackers\u0002 to ward off bad luck.","人們用塑膠鞭炮裝飾家裡,以驅趕厄運。"]],"flood (n.)":[["guide-113-10","The city was struck by an exceptional high tide, which caused severe \u0001flood\u0002 damage to bridges and roadways.","這座城市遭異常大潮侵襲,造成橋樑與道路嚴重的水患損害。"],["guide-106-16","Tourist deaths have been linked to altitude sickness, \u0001floods\u0002, and hiking accidents over the past decades at Machu Picchu.","過去數十年,馬丘比丘的旅客死亡與高山症、洪水及健行意外有關。"]],"gate (n.)":[["leader-115-30","Mary: John, do you know when boarding will start for our flight? John: Yes, it begins at 9:15 A.M. at \u0001Gate\u0002 7.","Mary:John,你知道我們班機什麼時候開始登機嗎? John:知道,上午 9:15 在 7 號登機門開始。"],["leader-110-44","Clerk: This is the final boarding call for John and Mary Smith booked on flight 321C to Salt Lake City. Please proceed to \u0001gate\u0002 3 immediately.","地勤:這是已訂位飛往鹽湖城 321C 班機的 John 和 Mary Smith 最後登機廣播,請立刻前往 3 號登機門。"]],"geopark (n.)":[["guide-115-54","Along Taiwan's northern coast, the wonders made by nature can be seen at Yehliu \u0001Geopark\u0002. Wind and waves have transformed rocks into various shapes, including a queen with a beautiful, thin neck.","在台灣北部海岸,野柳地質公園可見大自然的鬼斧神工。風與海浪把岩石雕塑成各種形狀,包括有著美麗細頸的女王頭。"],["guide-115-61","The \"Yehliu \u0001Geopark\u0002\" is one of the most famous landmarks of Taiwan.","「野柳地質公園」是台灣最著名的地標之一。"]],"gorge (n.)":[["guide-115-69","The island boasts towering mountains interwoven with \u0001gorges\u0002 and valleys carved out by countless rivers and streams.","這座島擁有高聳的山脈,與無數河流溪水切割出的峽谷、山谷交織在一起。"],["guide-114-65","Uplifting, followed by erosion by rivers, caused the formation of most of the geological features of Taroko \u0001Gorge\u0002.","地殼抬升,加上河流的侵蝕,造就了太魯閣峽谷大部分的地質特徵。"]],"gourmet (adj.)":[["leader-111-59","In a Japanese restaurant, your personal chef brings in the ingredients and cooks the food in front of you. He then serves the steaming hot \u0001gourmet\u0002 dish.","在日式餐廳,你的專屬主廚會端上食材並在你面前烹調,接著上熱騰騰的美食。"],["guide-108-5","First class passengers can enjoy \u0001gourmet\u0002 food.","頭等艙旅客可享用美饌。"]],"gym (n.)":[["guide-112-70","Hotel clerk: We have a bar, a \u0001gym\u0002, a swimming pool, tennis courts and a buffet restaurant.",""],["leader-110-41","Lisa: Do you have any exercise facilities? Hotel clerk: You can go to the 15th floor where our \u0001gym\u0002 is and as long as you have running shoes with you, you can use all of our equipment with no extra charge.","Lisa:你們有健身設施嗎? 櫃台:可以到 15 樓的健身房,只要隨身帶著跑鞋,所有器材都能免費使用。"]],"hospitality (n.)":[["guide-114-76","In the fast-paced and highly competitive world of \u0001hospitality\u0002, where customer expectations are sky-high, the industry faces a multitude of challenges.","",1],["guide-113-42","The politician proposed the loosening of restrictions on foreigners serving in the \u0001hospitality\u0002 and logistics sectors.","這位政治人物提議放寬對在餐旅與物流業工作之外國人的限制。"]],"illegal (adj.)":[["leader-113-79","For instance, chewing gum is \u0001illegal\u0002 in Singapore, feeding pigeons is prohibited in Venice, and riding a cow while intoxicated is not allowed in Scotland.","",4],["leader-113-80","Which of the following is mentioned as an \u0001illegal\u0002 activity in a foreign country?","下列何者被提到是某外國的違法行為?"]],"incentive (n.)":[["leader-114-30","To bring more tourists to Taiwan, the government should offer attractive \u0001incentive\u0002 like discounts and special deals.","為了吸引更多遊客來台灣,政府應提供有吸引力的誘因,例如折扣和特別優惠。"],["leader-111-75","According to the passage, what may not be the \u0001incentive\u0002 for people to use the service of Ele.me food delivery?","根據本文,下列何者可能不是人們使用 Ele.me 外送的誘因?"]],"ingredient (n.)":[["guide-114-26","Common \u0001ingredients\u0002 of Taiwanese cuisine are pork, seafood, rice, soy, and chicken.","台灣料理常見的食材有豬肉、海鮮、米、大豆和雞肉。"],["leader-111-59","In a Japanese restaurant, your personal chef brings in the \u0001ingredients\u0002 and cooks the food in front of you. He then serves the steaming hot gourmet dish.","在日式餐廳,你的專屬主廚會端上食材並在你面前烹調,接著上熱騰騰的美食。"]],"inspection (n.)":[["leader-115-3","Before entering the country, each visitor must have a valid passport ready for \u0001inspection\u0002.","入境前,每位旅客都必須備妥有效護照以供查驗。"],["guide-114-49","Make sure that your luggage has successfully passed through X-ray \u0001inspection\u0002 before you leave the check-in area.","離開報到區前,請確認你的行李已順利通過 X 光檢查。"]],"instruction (n.)":[["leader-115-44","Passenger: Is there Wi-Fi available on this flight? Flight Attendant: Yes, you can connect after takeoff using the \u0001instructions\u0002 provided.","乘客:這班機有 Wi-Fi 嗎? 空服員:有,起飛後你可以依照提供的說明連線。"],["guide-114-16","Abide by all safety rules when enjoying theme-park facilities. To stay safe, listen to what staff members say and follow their \u0001instructions\u0002.","玩主題樂園設施時,請遵守所有安全規定。為了安全,聽從工作人員的話並遵循指示。"]],"issue (n.)":[["leader-112-73","Green consumers are those who are aware of and interested in environmental \u0001issues\u0002.","",4],["guide-112-36","A: Have you had any \u0001issues\u0002 renewing your visa? B: Not yet.","A:你續簽簽證有遇到什麼問題嗎? B:還沒有。"]],"item (n.)":[["leader-112-31","You can go to the Lost and Found Service Center for your missing \u0001items\u0002.","你可以到失物招領中心找你遺失的物品。"],["guide-111-67","I couldn't return this \u0001item\u0002 because I had lost the receipt.","我沒辦法退這件商品,因為我把收據弄丟了。"]],"landing (n.)":[["leader-112-15","Ladies and gentlemen, please fasten your seat belts for \u0001landing\u0002.","各位女士先生,降落前請繫好安全帶。"],["leader-111-31","A cellphone parking lot is a parking lot where people wait for their friends to complete their \u0001landing\u0002 procedures.","「手機停車場」是人們等候朋友完成降落(入境)手續的停車場。"]],"layer (n.)":[["leader-114-25","Remember to wear several \u0001layers\u0002 of clothes to stay warm during travel to protect yourself from the cold.","記得旅行時穿好幾層衣服保暖,保護自己不受寒。"],["guide-107-72","What does the title “A New \u0001Layer\u0002” refer to?","展覽名稱「A New Layer(新的一層)」指的是什麼?"]],"lift (v.)":[["leader-115-57","Passenger: Could you help me place my bag overhead? Flight Attendant: Absolutely, let me \u0001lift\u0002 it for you safely.","乘客:可以幫我把包包放到上方置物櫃嗎? 空服員:當然,我幫你安全抬上去。"],["leader-112-25","Effective from October 13, 2022, Taiwan has \u0001lifted\u0002 the quarantine requirement for all arrivals, so arriving travelers will no longer be required to quarantine.","自 2022 年 10 月 13 日起,台灣取消所有入境者的隔離要求,入境旅客不再須隔離。"]],"luxury (n.)":[["guide-110-71","Traveling in Taiwan is a \u0001luxury\u0002 that anyone can enjoy without spending a fortune.","",1],["guide-106-71","The Tour de France has cycling on many people's minds, and for \u0001luxury\u0002 travelers, there has never been a better time to tour the world on two wheels.","",4]],"medicine (n.)":[["leader-112-10","Flight attendant: You seem to have some airsickness. B: Yes, do you have \u0001medicine\u0002 for that?","空服員:您似乎有點暈機。 乘客:是的,你們有暈機藥嗎?"],["leader-109-14","Many \u0001medicines\u0002 must be prescribed by a doctor. You cannot buy them at the pharmacy.","許多藥物必須由醫生開立處方,你無法在藥局直接買。"]],"migration (n.)":[["leader-114-10","Leaders of European Union countries arrived in Brussels for a summit, where \u0001migration\u0002 is an urgent topic.","歐盟各國領袖抵達布魯塞爾參加高峰會,移民是緊急議題。"],["leader-112-76","The team observes the life of sea turtles, keeping records of their \u0001migration\u0002 behaviors.","",1]],"monument (n.)":[["guide-114-32","The architecture of the Old Taichung Train Station is a mix of traditional Japanese and late Renaissance themes. It is now listed as a national \u0001monument\u0002.","台中舊火車站的建築融合了傳統日式與晚期文藝復興的風格。它現在被列為國定古蹟。"],["leader-112-59","We can take the subway to the \u0001monument\u0002.",""]],"nostalgia (n.)":[["guide-109-33","Taiwan Railways offers \u0001nostalgia\u0002 bento, transporting memories, __BLANK2__ for home, and tales of goodness.","台鐵推出懷舊便當,承載回憶、思鄉之情與美好故事。"],["guide-107-79","Which is closest in meaning to the word “\u0001nostalgia\u0002” in the second paragraph?","第二段中的「nostalgia」一詞意思最接近下列何者?"]],"offer (v.)":[["guide-113-61","In Taiwan, you don't need to worry about traveling far to find eateries that \u0001offer\u0002 inexpensive food.","在台灣,你不用擔心要跑很遠才能找到提供便宜食物的餐館。"],["leader-112-19","The hotel \u0001offers\u0002 easy access to the National Palace Museum.","這間飯店可輕鬆前往國立故宮博物院。"]],"overcharge (v.)":[["leader-110-36","I only bought a pair of blue jeans at US$20, but here it says US$40. You seem to have \u0001overcharged\u0002 me.","我只買一條 20 美元的牛仔褲,但這裡寫 40 美元。你好像多收我錢了。"],["leader-109-40","Front desk clerk: What seems to be the problem with your invoice? Hotel Guest: I think I have been \u0001overcharged\u0002.","櫃台:你的帳單有什麼問題嗎? 飯店客人:我覺得我被多收費了。"]],"overweight (adj.)":[["leader-110-58","Clerk: Your luggage seems \u0001overweight\u0002. I will suggest you to find a scale to measure its weight.","櫃台:你的行李好像超重了。我建議你找個磅秤量一下重量。"],["leader-108-4","Please put your suitcase on the scale. Oh, it is \u0001overweight\u0002.","請把行李箱放上磅秤。喔,它超重了。"]],"paradise (n.)":[["guide-110-3","Telluride, a Victorian-era mining town in Colorado, is a winter \u0001paradise\u0002 offering plenty to do and isn't as crowded as some of Colorado's other destinations.","泰勒瑞德是科羅拉多州一座維多利亞時代的礦業小鎮,是個冬季天堂,有很多活動,也不像科羅拉多其他景點那麼擁擠。"],["guide-108-24","An earthly \u0001paradise\u0002 awaits you in the alpine forests of Shei-Pa National Park.","雪霸國家公園的高山森林裡,有人間天堂等著你。"]],"patience (n.)":[["guide-107-77","We are always on the move, and we don't have much \u0001patience\u0002 with slow systems of transportation.","",4],["guide-106-46","Not knowing when the flight was going to take off, some tourists had lost their \u0001patience\u0002 and started yelling at the ground staff.","不知班機何時起飛,有些旅客失去耐心,開始對地勤大吼。"]],"pedestrian (n.)":[["guide-115-35","The buildings are built very close to each other to provide shade for \u0001pedestrians\u0002 walking in the city.","建築物彼此蓋得很近,為在城市中行走的行人提供遮蔭。"],["leader-113-6","Elevated wood-plank bridges are used to separate \u0001pedestrian\u0002 and vehicle traffic, and to provide beautiful views of the treetops.","架高的木棧橋用來區隔行人和車輛,並提供樹梢的美景。"]],"platform (n.)":[["guide-113-65","Clerk: Please mind the gap between the train and the \u0001platform\u0002 when leaving the train.","站務員:下車時請留意火車與月台之間的間隙。"],["leader-109-68","This \u0001platform\u0002 is for southbound trains. Uptown service is on the other side of the tracks.","這個月台是往南的列車。往市區(北)的班車在鐵軌另一側。"]],"pollution (n.)":[["leader-114-21","The global scientific community comes together and calls for immediate action on the urgent global problem—air \u0001pollution\u0002.","全球科學界團結起來,呼籲對空氣污染這個緊急全球問題採取立即行動。"],["guide-113-2","To protect the houses from air \u0001pollution\u0002, a special coating was applied on the exterior surface of the walls for all the houses in the town.","為保護房屋免受空氣污染,鎮上所有房屋的牆面外表都塗上了特殊塗層。"]],"primary (adj.)":[["leader-113-76","What is the \u0001primary\u0002 focus of this passage?","本文的主要焦點為何?"],["guide-110-28","Tour guides' \u0001primary\u0002 responsibility is to make sure the tour is safe for the group of tourists.","導遊的首要責任是確保旅程對整團遊客而言是安全的。"]],"procession (n.)":[["guide-111-27","The annual Dajia Matsu Pilgrimage \u0001procession\u0002 went off without a hitch this year!","今年大甲媽祖遶境進香隊伍順利無阻地完成了!"],["guide-109-35","The \u0001procession\u0002 for the goddess Mazu is a century-old tradition that embodies the collective memories of Taiwanese people.","媽祖遶境是有百年歷史的傳統,體現了台灣人的集體記憶。"]],"prohibit (v.)":[["guide-111-9","Federal law \u0001prohibits\u0002 disabling any smoke detector installed in any airplane lavatory.","聯邦法律禁止停用任何裝在飛機廁所的煙霧偵測器。"],["guide-109-15","Inside the museum, flash photography is strictly \u0001prohibited\u0002.","在博物館內,嚴格禁止使用閃光燈拍照。"]],"provide (v.)":[["leader-111-6","I prefer to pack light. Does your hotel \u0001provide\u0002 free toiletries?","我喜歡輕便打包。你們飯店有提供免費盥洗用品嗎?"],["leader-108-5","The hotel \u0001provides\u0002 two complimentary bottles of water in your fridge.","飯店在你的冰箱裡提供兩瓶免費招待的水。"]],"reception (n.)":[["leader-115-2","Guests checked in at the hotel \u0001reception\u0002 before going to their rooms.","客人先在飯店接待櫃台辦理入住,然後才進房間。"],["guide-108-50","At wedding \u0001receptions\u0002, guests bless the newlyweds by giving them red envelopes filled with money.","在婚宴上,賓客用裝了錢的紅包祝福新人。"]],"recommend (v.)":[["leader-107-43","Tourist: I am looking for a room that would be nice for a romantic weekend. What would you \u0001recommend\u0002?","遊客:我在找適合浪漫週末的房間,你會推薦什麼?"],["guide-107-1","The traveling office \u0001recommended\u0002 10 locations to offer people multiple choices to enjoy the magnificent sunsets in a relaxing way.","這個行動辦公室推薦了 10 個地點,讓人們有多種選擇,悠閒地欣賞壯麗的夕陽。"]],"rehabilitation (n.)":[["leader-113-46","After a severe injury, Hanna underwent intensive \u0001rehabilitation\u0002, working tirelessly to regain her strength, mobility, and independence, ultimately recovering well.","嚴重受傷後,Hanna 接受密集復健,不懈努力以恢復力量、行動力和獨立,最終復原良好。"],["guide-108-73","People can combine hot springs with natural and human resources for relieving stress, \u0001rehabilitation\u0002, and recuperation.","",4]],"renowned (adj.)":[["guide-113-8","The spiritual center of Japan's culture and heritage, Kyoto is \u0001renowned\u0002 for its abundance of green tea.","京都是日本文化與傳統遺產的精神中心,以盛產綠茶聞名。"],["guide-112-17","Yingge District in New Taipei City has been \u0001renowned\u0002 for its pottery for a long time, but recently, tourists have realized that this area offers so much more.","新北市鶯歌區長久以來以陶瓷聞名,但最近遊客發現這個地區能提供的遠不止於此。"]],"represent (v.)":[["leader-115-48","On the city tour, the guide asked everyone to take a photo in front of the famous landmark that \u0001represents\u0002 the history of the area.","市區觀光時,導遊請大家在代表當地歷史的著名地標前拍照。"],["guide-108-2","Embassy is the office that \u0001represents\u0002 your country to a foreign government.","大使館是代表你的國家對外國政府的辦事處。"]],"resemble (v.)":[["leader-114-36","Ground Staff: Can you identify which one \u0001resembles\u0002 your luggage? (Showing a card with various types of luggage.) Amy: Mine looks similar to Type D.","地勤:你能辨認出哪一個像你的行李嗎?(出示各種行李款式的卡片) Amy:我的很像 D 型。"],["guide-112-5","Guabao, a steamed sandwich, \u0001resembles\u0002 a hamburger that has a soft white bun filled with braised pork, pickled vegetables, peanut powder, and cilantro.","刈包是一種蒸的三明治,類似漢堡,有柔軟的白麵皮,夾著滷肉、酸菜、花生粉和香菜。"]],"resilience (n.)":[["guide-114-50","\u0001Resilience\u0002 refers to the ability to successfully adapt to stressors, maintaining psychological well-being in the face of adversity.","韌性(心理復原力)指的是成功適應壓力源、在逆境中維持心理健康的能力。"],["guide-110-78","Indeed, in this ongoing war against the pandemic, we have seen the \u0001resilience\u0002 and power of mankind.","",4]],"responsible (adj.)":[["guide-115-28","With a growing focus on \u0001responsible\u0002 and ethical tourism, sustainable tourism is becoming an increasingly important industry worldwide.","隨著對負責任且合乎道德的觀光日益重視,永續觀光正成為全球日益重要的產業。"],["leader-113-4","\u0001Responsible\u0002 tourists travel with reusable bags and water bottles, with which less trash is created.","負責任的旅客攜帶可重複使用的袋子和水瓶,以減少垃圾。"]],"ritual (n.)":[["leader-115-59","When our group visited a church this morning, we got a glimpse of how the priest performed a local \u0001ritual\u0002.","今早我們團體參觀一間教堂時,得以一瞥神父如何進行當地的儀式。"],["guide-107-13","Wang Ye and Matsu are two of the most common gods in Taiwan, but the \u0001rituals\u0002 of worshipping these gods differ.","王爺與媽祖是台灣民間信仰中最常見的兩位神明,但祭拜這些神明的儀式各有不同。"]],"sanctuary (n.)":[["guide-112-76","Safaris sometimes involve more than just visits to zoos and \u0001sanctuaries\u0002 to see animals; they often provide opportunities for hiking, birdwatching, and cultural immersion.","",1],["guide-111-77","The Koala Gardens, the Australian Butterfly \u0001Sanctuary\u0002, and Bird World Kuranda are among the many attractions in this picturesque village.","",4]],"scale (n.)":[["leader-110-58","Clerk: Your luggage seems overweight. I will suggest you to find a \u0001scale\u0002 to measure its weight.","櫃台:你的行李好像超重了。我建議你找個磅秤量一下重量。"],["leader-108-4","Please put your suitcase on the \u0001scale\u0002. Oh, it is overweight.","請把行李箱放上磅秤。喔,它超重了。"]],"scenery (n.)":[["leader-107-14","We headed to the countryside, rich with gorgeous hills and lakes. The \u0001scenery\u0002 there was breathtaking.","我們前往鄉間,那裡有壯麗的山丘與湖泊。當地景色令人屏息。"],["leader-107-22","There are many different types of \u0001scenery\u0002 in the park. The best way to see them is to go on foot.","公園裡有許多不同的景緻。看它們最好的方式就是步行。"]],"seafood (n.)":[["leader-110-32","I would like a \u0001seafood\u0002 fried rice. Please make it to takeaway.","我要一份海鮮炒飯,請做成外帶。"],["leader-110-42","Mary: I love \u0001seafood\u0002.",""]],"settle (v.)":[["guide-113-12","When you are faced with a conflict, raising your voice is never a successful way to \u0001settle\u0002 the disagreement.","當你面臨衝突時,提高音量絕不是解決歧見的成功方法。"],["guide-111-47","I'd like to leave early tomorrow morning. Can I \u0001settle\u0002 my bill now?","我明天一早想離開。我可以現在結帳嗎?"]],"snack (n.)":[["leader-114-26","The vending machines offer everything you might need, ranging from \u0001snacks\u0002 to pajamas.","自動販賣機提供你可能需要的一切,從零食到睡衣。"],["guide-114-53","Pig's blood cake is a popular Taiwanese street food \u0001snack\u0002 made with pork blood congealed with sticky rice.","豬血糕是受歡迎的台灣街頭小吃,由豬血凝結糯米製成。"]],"statue (n.)":[["leader-113-3","This church dates back to the mid-fourteenth century and houses a large number of remarkable \u0001statues\u0002 and wall paintings.","這座教堂可追溯到 14 世紀中葉,收藏大量傑出的雕像和壁畫。"],["guide-112-20","The Duomo di Milano in Italy has over 3,400 sculptures, making it the place with the most \u0001statues\u0002 in the world.","義大利的米蘭大教堂有超過 3,400 座雕塑,使它成為全世界擁有最多雕像的地方。"]],"stow (v.)":[["guide-114-63","To ensure flight safety, passengers are to safely \u0001stow\u0002 their carry-on baggage under the seat or in the overhead baggage compartment to prevent them from sliding or falling off.","為確保飛航安全,旅客應將隨身行李妥善收放在座位下方或頭頂上方的行李櫃,以防滑動或掉落。"],["guide-112-69","Ladies and gentlemen, please be careful while opening the overhead compartment as any items \u0001stowed\u0002 inside might fall out, and take all your personal belongings with you.","各位女士先生,打開頭頂行李櫃時請小心,因為裡面放的物品可能掉出來;並請帶走所有隨身物品。"]],"subway (n.)":[["leader-112-59","We can take the \u0001subway\u0002 to the monument.",""],["leader-111-49","Many hotels in New York provide free airport shuttle service. You could also take the \u0001subway\u0002 if you are comfortable with public transportation.","紐約許多飯店提供免費機場接駁服務。若你習慣搭大眾運輸,也可搭地鐵。"]],"summit (n.)":[["guide-115-9","Tatajia is the jumping-off point for a variety of forested day hikes, as well as the non-technical, two-day ascent of Jade Peak, with an overnight stay at Paiyun Lodge en route to the \u0001summit\u0002.","塔塔加是各種森林一日健行的起點,也是玉山兩天非技術性攀登的出發點,途中在排雲山莊過夜後前往山頂。"],["guide-115-41","At the \u0001summit\u0002 of Bagua Mountain sits the Eight Trigram Mountains Buddha Landscape, a sight that can be seen from almost anywhere in Changhua City. It is a perfect place to go for a light hike.","八卦山頂坐落著八卦山大佛風景區,幾乎在彰化市任何地方都能看到。這裡是輕鬆健行的絕佳去處。"]],"supply (v.)":[["guide-112-30","A: Does your restaurant \u0001supply\u0002 a continental breakfast? B: Yes, we do, and it's served in a buffet style.","A:你們餐廳有供應歐陸式早餐嗎? B:有的,而且是自助式的。"],["guide-112-72","According to the passage, what is the most common way to \u0001supply\u0002 electricity?","根據本文,供應電力最常見的方式是什麼?"]],"symptom (n.)":[["guide-115-32","Elevations above 700 meters may trigger \u0001symptoms\u0002 of altitude sickness in some individuals, including rapid breathing, increased heart rate, fatigue, asthma, nausea, and vomiting.","海拔 700 公尺以上可能在某些人身上引發高山症的症狀,包括呼吸急促、心跳加快、疲勞、氣喘、噁心與嘔吐。"],["guide-112-59","Doctor: What are the \u0001symptoms\u0002?",""]],"technology (n.)":[["guide-108-43","Organizers use modern \u0001technology\u0002 to provide an exciting light display in addition to hanging elaborate traditional lanterns.","主辦單位運用現代科技提供精彩的燈光秀,還掛上精緻的傳統燈籠。"],["leader-107-66","Software developers incorporate AI \u0001technology\u0002 into their products and use it to deal with the complicated job of big-data sorting and analysis.","軟體開發者把 AI 技術整合進產品,用來處理大數據分類與分析這種複雜工作。"]],"terminal (n.)":[["leader-112-42","Excuse me, which \u0001terminal\u0002 should I go to for the connecting flight to Chicago?","不好意思,轉機到芝加哥要去哪個航廈?"],["leader-106-14","A \u0001terminal\u0002 is an airport building that has all the facilities for passengers that are arriving or departing.","航廈是一棟機場建築,提供入境或離境旅客所需的一切設施。"]],"territory (n.)":[["guide-114-70","In international practice, most countries and \u0001territories\u0002 may refuse entry to a foreign visitor if their passport will expire less than six months after the date of arrival.","依國際慣例,若外國旅客的護照在抵達日後不到六個月就到期,多數國家與地區可能拒絕其入境。"],["guide-110-14","It is hard to predict the success of space travel since it is an unexplored \u0001territory\u0002.","太空旅行的成功難以預測,因為它是一個未探索的領域。"]],"tour (n.)":[["guide-110-28","\u0001Tour\u0002 guides' primary responsibility is to make sure the tour is safe for the group of tourists.","導遊的首要責任是確保旅程對整團遊客而言是安全的。"],["guide-109-54","A: Where does the \u0001tour\u0002 start off? B: At the main entrance.","A:導覽從哪裡出發? B:在正門口。"]],"traditional (adj.)":[["leader-115-10","This ancient city is a must-visit destination for every tourist to experience the \u0001traditional\u0002 culture and old town atmosphere.","這座古城是每位遊客必訪的目的地,可體驗傳統文化與老城氛圍。"],["leader-114-77","What makes the Odyssey different from \u0001traditional\u0002 cruise ships?","Odyssey 與傳統郵輪有何不同?"]],"transfer (v.)":[["leader-111-38","Guest: Please \u0001transfer\u0002 my call to an international operator.",""],["guide-109-38","Bamboo furniture is popular in Latin America as a result of bamboo-weaving craftsmanship \u0001transferred\u0002 from Taiwan.","竹製家具在拉丁美洲很受歡迎,這是源自台灣的竹編工藝傳入(移轉)的結果。"]],"trend (n.)":[["leader-114-14","Eco-friendly travel is now one of the fastest-growing \u0001trends\u0002 in the industry, and many people embrace this promising development.","環保旅遊現在是業界成長最快的趨勢之一,許多人擁抱這個有前景的發展。"],["leader-111-76","Safety & hygiene tourism \u0001trends\u0002 Whether it is airlines, cruises, hotels, restaurants or bars, since the outbreak of COVID-19, safety and hygiene standards have been absolutely paramount.","",4]],"trip (n.)":[["leader-112-38","Here is the itinerary for my \u0001trip\u0002 to Europe this coming summer. Do you have any suggestions?","這是我今夏歐洲之旅的行程表。你有什麼建議嗎?"],["leader-110-62","Cathy: How's your \u0001trip\u0002 in Japan, Jerry? Jerry: I really enjoyed it.","Cathy:Jerry,你的日本之旅如何? Jerry:我非常喜歡。"]],"unattended (adj.)":[["guide-115-1","When you are in public places, be sure not to leave your personal belongings \u0001unattended\u0002.","在公共場所,務必不要讓你的個人隨身物品無人看管。"],["guide-108-48","Beware of strangers at the airport and do not leave your personal items \u0001unattended\u0002.","在機場要提防陌生人,別讓私人物品無人看管。"]],"upgrade (v.)":[["leader-112-13","Some hotel loyalty programs award elite members \u0001upgrade\u0002 benefits after staying a certain number of nights.","有些飯店會員計畫在住滿一定晚數後,給予尊榮會員升等優惠。"],["guide-110-37","Can I \u0001upgrade\u0002 to business class?","我可以升等到商務艙嗎?"]],"urgent (adj.)":[["leader-114-10","Leaders of European Union countries arrived in Brussels for a summit, where migration is an \u0001urgent\u0002 topic.","歐盟各國領袖抵達布魯塞爾參加高峰會,移民是緊急議題。"],["leader-114-21","The global scientific community comes together and calls for immediate action on the \u0001urgent\u0002 global problem—air pollution.","全球科學界團結起來,呼籲對空氣污染這個緊急全球問題採取立即行動。"]],"utensil (n.)":[["leader-113-5","Customer: May I have two plastic forks, please? Receptionist: Unfortunately, we no longer provide any disposable \u0001utensils\u0002 due to the new environmental protection act.","顧客:可以給我兩支塑膠叉子嗎? 櫃台:抱歉,因新環保法我們不再提供任何拋棄式餐具。"],["leader-109-47","The customer looking at the forks and spoons complained about the dirty and stained \u0001utensils\u0002 to the waiter.","看著叉子湯匙的顧客,向服務生抱怨這些又髒又有污漬的餐具。"]],"vacancy (n.)":[["leader-112-49","Is there any \u0001vacancy\u0002 today?",""],["leader-108-14","Receptionist: ABC Hotel, may I help you? Justin: Do you have a \u0001vacancy\u0002 for a double room on March First?","櫃台:ABC 飯店,能為您服務嗎? Justin:3 月 1 日有空房的雙人房嗎?"]],"vacation (n.)":[["guide-111-13","The last thing you want on a \u0001vacation\u0002 is to find out hidden fees that you must pay.","度假時你最不想遇到的,就是發現隱藏的費用得付。"],["guide-109-18","We are on a tight budget, so we want to plan a \u0001vacation\u0002 that doesn't cost too much.","我們預算緊,所以想規劃一趟不太花錢的旅行。"]],"vandalism (n.)":[["leader-113-63","Singapore is famous for its strict laws. Anyone who is found guilty and convicted for \u0001vandalism\u0002 may face a fine or imprisonment.","新加坡以嚴格法律聞名。任何被判破壞公物罪成立者,可能面臨罰款或監禁。"],["guide-113-49","Parks and recreation staff received numerous calls over the weekend regarding \u0001vandalism\u0002 and damage at The Central Park.","週末公園與遊憩管理人員接到大量來電,反映中央公園的惡意破壞與損害。"]],"VAT":[["leader-112-62","A: Besides the discount, we can also keep the receipts to get a \u0001VAT\u0002 (value-added tax) refund at the airport. B: So great!","A:除了折扣,我們還能留著收據到機場辦加值稅退稅。 B:太棒了!"],["leader-111-56","Visitors to the EU may buy goods free of \u0001VAT\u0002 at the check-out. The clerk will ask you to show your passport and fill out a tax refund form.","到歐盟的遊客結帳時可買免加值稅商品。店員會請你出示護照並填一張退稅表。"]],"vehicle (n.)":[["guide-115-27","Renting a 1,500c.c. five-seater car allows for 48 hours of use. Before picking up the \u0001vehicle\u0002, please call the rental company to assist you in arranging the pickup.","租一輛 1,500c.c. 五人座車可使用 48 小時。取車前,請致電租車公司協助安排取車。"],["leader-110-23","Wearing seat belts is mandatory in all \u0001vehicles\u0002 for drivers globally.","全球所有車輛的駕駛都強制規定要繫安全帶。"]],"via (prep.)":[["leader-110-55","It's great that we can buy flight tickets \u0001via\u0002 both phone and internet without calling the travel agents. It saves us a lot of time.","我們能透過電話和網路買機票,不用打給旅行社,真好。這省了我們很多時間。"],["leader-106-79","What does the word \"\u0001via\u0002\" mean?","via 這個字是什麼意思?"]],"view (n.)":[["leader-112-57","Everyone can come to this corner. Based on my experience, it is the best \u0001view\u0002 to take a selfie or a group photo.","大家都可以到這個角落。以我經驗,這是拍自拍或團體照最佳的取景點。"],["leader-109-20","The \u0001view\u0002 outside the train was suddenly gone because it went through a(n) tunnel and it was dark outside.","火車窗外的景色突然消失,因為它穿過一個隧道,外面一片漆黑。"]],"wallet (n.)":[["leader-114-37","When was the last time you took out your \u0001wallet\u0002?",""],["leader-112-69","My \u0001wallet\u0002 was gone.",""]],"accelerate (v.)":[["guide-110-34","How fast can his car \u0001accelerate\u0002?","他的車能加速到多快?"],["leader-109-78","Production and development of thousands of new plastic products \u0001accelerated\u0002 after World War II, so transforming the modern age that life without plastics would be unrecognizable today.","",4]],"acceptable (adj.)":[["leader-114-19","Common sense tells us that behavior that disrupts a classroom and disrupts the learning of others is not \u0001acceptable\u0002.","常識告訴我們,擾亂課堂、妨礙他人學習的行為是不可接受的。"],["leader-107-54","When you go out on a date for dinner, it is \u0001acceptable\u0002 to share the cost.","約會吃晚餐時,分攤費用是可以接受的。"]],"accessible (adj.)":[["guide-110-17","The yoga instructor believes that yoga should be \u0001accessible\u0002 to all people regardless of body-type, level of athleticism, and age.","這位瑜伽老師相信,不論體型、運動能力和年齡,瑜伽都應該人人都能接觸/從事。"],["guide-107-66","This building is renowned for its \u0001accessible\u0002 design. For example, people with injuries or in wheelchairs can use the elevator to reach the observatory.","這棟建築以其無障礙設計聞名。例如,受傷或坐輪椅的人可搭電梯抵達觀景台。"]],"acclaimed (adj.)":[["guide-107-5","National Taichung Theater was designed by the internationally \u0001acclaimed\u0002 Japanese architect, Toyo Ito.","臺中國家歌劇院是由享譽國際的日本建築師伊東豊雄所設計。"],["guide-106-71","For decades, B&R has been the widely \u0001acclaimed\u0002, award-winning world leader in luxury scheduled cycling trips, and over the years added hiking, kayaking, sailing and “multi-sport” departures.","",1]],"adamant (adj.)":[["leader-108-77","What does the word \"\u0001adamant\u0002\" in the first paragraph mean?","第一段的 adamant 是什麼意思?"],["leader-108-76","While many food-related museums of late have mostly just been opportunities for novel selfies, West is \u0001adamant\u0002 that the Disgusting Food Museum is there to help people learn and think critically, not just to pose for photos.","",1]],"address (v.)":[["guide-114-8","The Japanese use honorific titles as a form of respect in \u0001addressing\u0002 others.","日本人用敬稱頭銜作為稱呼他人時的一種尊重方式。"],["guide-113-52","How is this issue \u0001addressed\u0002?",""]],"adjacent (adj.)":[["leader-107-21","One of the most common problems for hotel guests is when the neighbors in \u0001adjacent\u0002 rooms are noisy.",""],["guide-107-48","The store \u0001adjacent\u0002 to the hotel is a convenience store which provides a range of everyday items such as groceries, snacks, or drinks.","飯店旁的便利商店提供各種日常用品,例如雜貨、零食或飲料。"]],"admission (n.)":[["leader-109-41","Official of the Immigration Area of the airport will stamp your passport once you are approved and granted \u0001admission\u0002.","機場移民區的官員會在你獲准並取得入境許可後,在護照上蓋章。"],["guide-108-11","What an expensive concert. The \u0001admission\u0002 was $100.","這場演唱會真貴,門票要 100 元。"]],"adopt (v.)":[["guide-111-51","Mary's pictures look all the same because she always \u0001adopts\u0002 the same posture for the camera.","Mary 的照片看起來都一樣,因為她面對鏡頭總是擺同一個姿勢。"],["leader-109-66","This is a city for bicycles and more tourists are \u0001adopting\u0002 this way of exploring the city.","這是座適合單車的城市,越來越多遊客採用這種探索城市的方式。"]],"adult (n.)":[["leader-114-51","Peggy: Do you know if there's an admission fee to get into the museum? John: Yes, it's $15 for \u0001adults\u0002 and $10 for students.","Peggy:你知道進博物館要入場費嗎? John:要,成人 15 元,學生 10 元。"],["guide-109-52","Let me remind you that all children must be accompanied by an \u0001adult\u0002 in the art center.","提醒你,在藝術中心所有孩童都必須有大人陪同。"]],"advancement (n.)":[["guide-114-48","The evolution of modern tourism owes much to the \u0001advancements\u0002 in transportation as a mode of mobility.","現代觀光的演進,很大程度歸功於作為移動方式的交通進步。"],["guide-108-76","Technological \u0001advancements\u0002 have resulted in rapid changes within the tourism industry.","",1]],"advise (v.)":[["leader-113-66","Due to limited space in the overhead bins, passengers are \u0001advised\u0002 to bring only one carry-on bag on the plane.","由於頭頂置物櫃空間有限,建議乘客只帶一件隨身行李上機。"],["leader-106-69","People living in the track of the hurricane have been \u0001advised\u0002 to leave their homes until it has passed.","住在颶風行進路徑上的居民,已被建議撤離家園直到颶風過去。"]],"aesthetic (adj.)":[["leader-110-80","Most importantly, a museum should not only be a place to see art but also should be an \u0001aesthetic\u0002 experience in itself.","",4]],"aggravate (v.)":[["guide-106-43","All John could do on his two-day trip to Beijing was to stay in the hotel: the air outside was so polluted that it would \u0001aggravate\u0002 his asthma.","約翰在北京兩天只能待在飯店:外頭空氣汙染嚴重,會加重他的氣喘。"]],"air-conditioning (n.)":[["guide-115-38","The buildings were designed to mitigate heat and curb \u0001air-conditioning\u0002 use.","這些建築的設計是為了減緩熱度、抑制空調使用。"],["leader-110-8","Our hotel is equipped with in-room facilities, such as \u0001air-conditioning\u0002, hairdryer, Wi-Fi, iron and hypoallergenic bedding.","我們飯店客房內配備各項設施,如空調、吹風機、Wi-Fi、熨斗和防過敏寢具。"]],"airline (n.)":[["leader-114-33","European \u0001airlines\u0002 are increasing their capacity as the expansion trend that began late last year continues.","隨著去年底開始的擴張趨勢持續,歐洲航空公司正在增加運能。"],["leader-109-50","On budget \u0001airlines\u0002 we pay less for our tickets, but have to pay for food, headsets, or drinks.","搭廉價航空機票較便宜,但要另付餐食、耳機或飲料。"]],"aisle (n.)":[["leader-115-51","During a crowded flight, she requested \u0001aisle\u0002 seat to avoid disturbing neighbors when standing up.","在擁擠的班機上,她要求走道座位,以免起身時打擾鄰座。"],["leader-114-71","Most travelers have a preference for window or \u0001aisle\u0002 seats when it comes to air travel, but have you ever given thought to which side of the plane you should sit on?","",1]],"all-you-can-eat":[["leader-115-26","Even though this is an \u0001all-you-can-eat\u0002 restaurant, you should still try to get only the portion of food that you need to prevent unnecessary waste.","即使這是吃到飽餐廳,你仍應只拿你需要的份量,以免不必要的浪費。"],["guide-110-22","Vacations are a much-needed break from life at work and home, but they can cause weight gain because many vacation packages include \u0001all-you-can-eat\u0002 and all-you-can-drink options.","度假是逃離工作與居家生活的必要喘息,但它們可能造成體重增加,因為許多度假套裝包含吃到飽、喝到飽的選項。"]],"allow (v.)":[["leader-115-17","Tour Leader: How much time should we \u0001allow\u0002 inside the British Museum? Local Guide: About two hours is ideal to see the highlights.","領隊:大英博物館裡面要預留多少時間? 當地導遊:大約兩小時剛好看完精華。"],["leader-114-11","Many national parks have trails and reachable adventures, \u0001allowing\u0002 everyone to enjoy the beauty of America's protected spaces.","許多國家公園有步道和可及的探險活動,讓每個人都能享受美國受保護空間之美。"]],"alternative (n.)":[["guide-108-60","Meals from fast food restaurants may be the easiest and cheapest \u0001alternatives\u0002 for a traveler.","速食店的餐點也許是旅客最方便又最便宜的選擇。"],["leader-107-64","In dense cities where huge numbers of people are moving in generally the same direction, there is no \u0001alternative\u0002 to the fixed route bus or train.","在人口密集的城市,大量人潮大致朝同一方向移動,除了固定路線的公車或火車別無他法。"]],"altitude (n.)":[["leader-110-43","We are currently cruising at an \u0001altitude\u0002 of 3,300 feet at an airspeed of 400 miles per hour.",""],["guide-106-14","Grown at an \u0001altitude\u0002 of 1,600m or higher, the high mountain teas enjoy colder weather, cleaner water and constant mist.","生長在海拔1,600 公尺以上,高山茶享有較冷的天氣、較潔淨的水與恆常的雲霧。"]],"amenities (n.)":[["leader-115-16","As an effort to protect our environment, the hotels in this region do not provide \u0001amenities\u0002 and you need to prepare those items by yourself.","為了保護環境,這個地區的飯店不提供備品,你需要自備那些用品。"],["guide-108-6","Some airlines might give you toothpaste and other personal \u0001amenities\u0002 when you took a long flight in the past.","過去搭長程航班時,有些航空公司會給你牙膏和其他盥洗備品。"]],"amount (n.)":[["guide-111-7","The \u0001amount\u0002 of alcohol passengers are allowed to carry onto a plane varies from country to country.","乘客可攜帶上機的酒精量因國而異。"],["guide-106-69","My Japanese friend found Taiwanese food too greasy for her, so she usually cooked by herself to control the \u0001amount\u0002 of oil in her meals.","我的日本朋友覺得台灣菜對她來說太油膩,所以她通常自己煮以控制餐點的油量。"]],"anniversary (n.)":[["leader-113-47","For their \u0001anniversary\u0002, the old couple celebrated in an extravagant manner, booking a luxurious cruise and dining in high-end restaurants, trying to create unforgettable memories.","為了結婚週年,這對老夫妻以奢華的方式慶祝,訂了豪華郵輪並在高檔餐廳用餐,想創造難忘回憶。"],["leader-107-12","On August 31, 2017, Britain paid tribute to Princess Diana on the twentieth \u0001anniversary\u0002 of her death. She died in a high-speed car crash in Paris on August 31, 1997.","2017 年 8 月 31 日,英國在黛安娜王妃逝世 20 週年向她致敬。她 1997 年同日在巴黎一場高速車禍中身亡。"]],"appeal (n.)":[["guide-112-48","Mineral fields used to be a marvelous scenic spot but it has lost its \u0001appeal\u0002 in recent years.","礦區曾是絕妙的風景勝地,但近年來已失去了它的吸引力。"],["leader-106-7","If the beach and the desert lose their \u0001appeal\u0002, visitors can always go skiing at Ski Dubai, an indoor ski resort.","如果海灘和沙漠失去吸引力,遊客隨時可到室內滑雪場 Ski Dubai 滑雪。"]],"appointment (n.)":[["leader-111-57","If you are sick when travelling, you could call the hospital and schedule an \u0001appointment\u0002. When you visit the hospital, you need to bring your health insurance policy documents.","旅途中生病,可打電話給醫院預約。看診時要帶健康保險保單文件。"],["leader-111-61","Tourist: Hello, I would like to schedule an \u0001appointment\u0002 to see a doctor.",""]],"appreciate (v.)":[["leader-108-3","In order to \u0001appreciate\u0002 the architecture of the castle, you need to get off the tour bus and get closer to it.","為了欣賞城堡的建築,你得下遊覽車靠近它。"]],"aquatic (adj.)":[["leader-109-80","Which of the following is similar in meaning to \"\u0001aquatic\u0002 species\"?","與 aquatic species 意思相近的是?"],["leader-109-76","Microplastics have been found in more than 100 \u0001aquatic\u0002 species, including fish, shrimp, and mussels destined for our dinner plates.","",1]],"architectural (adj.)":[["guide-115-31","Longshan Temple, located in Wanhua, is one of Taipei's finest examples of Taiwan's \u0001architectural\u0002 and historical heritage.","位於萬華的龍山寺,是台灣建築與歷史遺產的最佳範例之一。"],["guide-114-5","The historical value of the museum lies in its exterior design which preserves the \u0001architectural\u0002 trends of the early 20th century.","博物館的歷史價值在於其外觀設計保留了 20 世紀初的建築風潮。"]],"artisan (n.)":[["guide-107-73","Five Swedish designers have worked with \u0001artisans\u0002 in Taiwan to explore different lacquer techniques, and presented their works in an exhibition – “A New Layer.” The exhibition shows contemporary objects made with an ancient technique.","",4]],"artwork (n.)":[["guide-114-33","The National Palace Museum is home to hundreds of thousands of ancient Chinese artifacts and \u0001artwork\u0002, which are of great historical value.","故宮博物院收藏著數十萬件古代中華文物與藝術品,深具歷史價值。"]],"asset (n.)":[["guide-114-1","Kaohsiung Port has been a key \u0001asset\u0002 for the city's growth and modernization with many opportunities.","高雄港一直是這座城市成長與現代化的關鍵資產,帶來許多機會。"],["leader-106-24","An employee who can do business in more than one language is a valuable \u0001asset\u0002 to most companies.","能用多種語言做生意的員工,對多數公司是寶貴的資產。"]],"athlete (n.)":[["guide-107-51","When the \u0001athlete\u0002 pulled off one of his greatest performances, he received a standing ovation from the audience.","當這位運動員完成他最精彩的表現之一時,獲得觀眾起立鼓掌。"]],"attract (v.)":[["leader-115-50","A local travel agency hung several scenic posters in the company window to \u0001attract\u0002 pedestrians to come inside and purchase their historical tour.","當地旅行社在櫥窗掛了幾張風景海報,以吸引行人進來購買他們的歷史導覽行程。"],["guide-107-27","Hualien is a small city, but even so, it \u0001attracts\u0002 many tourists.","花蓮是座小城市,但即使如此,仍吸引許多觀光客。"]],"autonomous (adj.)":[["guide-115-77","Which companies are specifically mentioned as working on \u0001autonomous\u0002 ride-hailing?","文中明確提到哪些公司在做自駕叫車?"],["guide-115-76","New findings from Lux Research suggest that while \u0001autonomous\u0002 robotaxis will further disrupt the conventional taxi and ride sharing spaces, car ownership will not be affected.","",1]],"avalanche (n.)":[["leader-108-52","There is a very high risk of \u0001avalanche\u0002 in this area. Two skiers were buried alive last week.","這區雪崩風險很高。上週有兩名滑雪者被活埋。"],["leader-107-25","Staying safe when skiing or snowboarding in the mountains is crucial, and an important part of that is being aware of the risk of \u0001avalanche\u0002.","在山上滑雪或滑雪板時保持安全至關重要,其中重要的一環是意識到雪崩的風險。"]],"aware (adj.)":[["leader-107-25","Staying safe when skiing or snowboarding in the mountains is crucial, and an important part of that is being \u0001aware\u0002 of the risk of avalanche.","在山上滑雪或滑雪板時保持安全至關重要,其中重要的一環是意識到雪崩的風險。"],["guide-107-43","People use their electronic devices while walking. When they do so, it is very difficult to be \u0001aware\u0002 of what is going on around them.","人們邊走邊用電子裝置,這樣一來,很難察覺周遭發生的事。"]],"bamboo (n.)":[["guide-115-65","Designed to look like a pole of \u0001bamboo\u0002, this skyscraper is the tallest and most iconic landmark of the city.","這棟以竹節造型設計的摩天大樓(台北 101),是該市最高、最具代表性的地標。"],["guide-109-38","\u0001Bamboo\u0002 furniture is popular in Latin America as a result of bamboo-weaving craftsmanship transferred from Taiwan.","竹製家具在拉丁美洲很受歡迎,這是源自台灣的竹編工藝傳入(移轉)的結果。"]],"battery (n.)":[["leader-113-23","Tour Leader: I'd like you to check if you put any lithium \u0001batteries\u0002, power bank or valuable items in your checked luggage. If you did, please move them to your carry-on bag.","領隊:我想請你檢查託運行李裡有沒有放鋰電池、行動電源或貴重物品。如果有,請把它們移到隨身行李。"],["guide-112-72","There are various methods to supply electricity; however, the most common way is to use \u0001batteries\u0002.","",4]],"blanket (n.)":[["leader-110-48","Yes, I can give you a blanket.","好,我給你毯子。",2]],"blizzard (n.)":[["leader-113-8","A group of travelers were stranded in a \u0001blizzard\u0002; fortunately, they were accepted into a stranger's home for two nights.","一群旅客受困暴風雪中;幸好被一位陌生人收留兩晚。"],["guide-106-35","Due to the \u0001blizzard\u0002, all the guests had no choice but to stay in the hotel and eat together in the communal dining hall.","因暴風雪,所有客人只能待在飯店,並在公用餐廳一起用餐。"]],"booming (adj.)":[["guide-113-52","A: I heard the natural beauty of Hawaii is under threat due to its \u0001booming\u0002 travel industry.",""],["guide-107-56","Even though a \u0001booming\u0002 economy has brought benefits to Southeast Asian countries, the major problem of traffic congestion has resulted, leading to pollution and delays.","儘管繁榮經濟為東南亞國家帶來好處,但也造成交通壅塞的大問題,導致汙染與延誤。"]],"bottle (n.)":[["leader-110-48","Traveler: Excuse me, I need some hot water to make the milk for my baby. Flight attendant: Sure, I can fill the \u0001bottle\u0002 for you.","旅客:不好意思,我需要熱水幫寶寶泡奶。 空服員:好的,我幫你裝奶瓶。"],["guide-108-57","In Taiwan, guests of the hotel cannot drink the tap water. The hotel usually provides two complimentary \u0001bottles\u0002 of water instead.","在台灣,飯店客人不能喝自來水,飯店通常改提供兩瓶免費瓶裝水。"]],"brand (n.)":[["leader-107-71","In the age of ubiquitous social media, these booths and rooms seem to be the latest way to attract customers and build a \u0001brand\u0002.","",4],["leader-106-5","Companies use social network sites like Facebook so that people can share information about the \u0001brand\u0002.","公司利用臉書等社群網站,好讓人們能分享品牌資訊。"]],"break (v.)":[["guide-107-15","He always keeps promises and never \u0001breaks\u0002 his word.","他總是信守承諾,從不食言。"],["guide-106-23","If I hadn't slipped on the stairs, I would not have \u0001broken\u0002 my arm.","如果我沒在樓梯上滑倒,就不會摔斷手臂。"]],"breeze (n.)":[["guide-115-37","These connected walkways act like funnels that draw in \u0001breezes\u0002 in summer.","這些相連的走道像漏斗一樣,在夏天引入微風。"],["guide-112-34","A: I love this \u0001breeze\u0002.",""]],"bumpy (adj.)":[["guide-111-78","Your ride will be \u0001bumpy\u0002, but it will offer unforgettable views of thick jungle and spectacular peaks.","",4]],"campaign (n.)":[["leader-107-13","A couple grieving over the death of their son in a traffic accident blamed his death on the driver's lack of driver training and launched a public \u0001campaign\u0002 calling for mandatory education for new drivers.","一對痛失兒子(死於車禍)的夫妻,把死因歸咎於駕駛訓練不足,發起公開活動,呼籲對新手駕駛實施強制教育。"],["leader-107-79","\"Pressing flesh\" has become a byword on political \u0001campaigns\u0002.","",4]],"camping (n.)":[["leader-109-35","Cindy: Would you like to go on a backpacking tour? Danial: Yes, I like going \u0001camping\u0002 on the mountains.","Cindy:你想去背包客旅行嗎? Danial:好,我喜歡去山上露營。"],["guide-109-17","Setting up a campfire is the most classic outdoor activity for \u0001camping\u0002.","生營火是露營最經典的戶外活動。"]],"cancel (v.)":[["leader-111-44","Flight attendant: Your flight has been \u0001cancelled\u0002 due to a hurricane in Florida. Passenger: Will the airline company arrange accommodation for us?","空服員:你的航班因佛州颶風取消了。 乘客:航空公司會為我們安排住宿嗎?"],["guide-111-6","If your flight has been \u0001canceled\u0002 by the airline, you are entitled to a refund that only applies to services you have not received.","若你的航班被航空公司取消,你有權獲得退款,但僅限你尚未使用的服務。"]],"cancellation (n.)":[["leader-115-41","Before going on the adventure tour, the travel agency advised all participants to check their insurance coverage to ensure medical expenses and trip \u0001cancellations\u0002 are included.","出發冒險行程前,旅行社建議所有團員確認他們的保險範圍,以確保涵蓋醫療費用和行程取消。"]],"carefully (adv.)":[["leader-109-10","Although most snakes in the park are not poisonous, you need to watch \u0001carefully\u0002 where you put your hands and feet.","雖然公園裡多數蛇沒毒,你仍需小心留意手腳擺放的位置。"],["leader-106-1","If you plan your trip \u0001carefully\u0002 and learn to take precautions, you can relax and enjoy yourself.","如果你仔細規劃行程並學會採取預防措施,就能放鬆好好享受。"]],"carnival (n.)":[["guide-114-54","Shilin Night Market has a fun, \u0001carnival\u0002-like atmosphere with arguably the best mix of food, games, and shopping stalls, but just be prepared to elbow your way through the crowds.","士林夜市有歡樂、嘉年華般的氛圍,可說是美食、遊戲與購物攤販的最佳組合,但要有心理準備用手肘擠過人群。"],["leader-108-43","The \u0001carnival\u0002 features people dressed in colorful costumes parading through the city's streets.","嘉年華以身穿繽紛服裝的人們遊行穿越市街為特色。"]],"carry-on (adj.)":[["leader-113-66","Due to limited space in the overhead bins, passengers are advised to bring only one \u0001carry-on\u0002 bag on the plane.","由於頭頂置物櫃空間有限,建議乘客只帶一件隨身行李上機。"],["leader-112-43","Each passenger can have two pieces of checked baggage allowance and one \u0001carry-on\u0002 bag.","每位乘客可有兩件託運行李額度和一件隨身行李。"]],"cash (v.)":[["leader-111-13","They can't be easily \u0001cashed\u0002, even at the banks that issued them.",""],["guide-108-55","If you want to \u0001cash\u0002 your traveler's checks, you must pay a handling charge. We charge a 2% commission on each check.","若你想兌現旅行支票,必須付手續費。我們每張收 2% 佣金。"]],"catering (n.)":[["leader-106-35","A: Which job might require some \u0001catering\u0002 or culinary experience? B: Banquet server.","A:哪個工作可能需要一些外燴或烹飪經驗? B:宴會服務生。"],["leader-106-50","The \u0001catering\u0002 for all wedding receptions at Princeton Hall is often done by Joy Eats.","Princeton Hall 所有婚宴的外燴,常由 Joy Eats 承辦。"]],"change (v.)":[["leader-109-69","Clerk: What currency would you like to have your money \u0001changed\u0002, sir? Customer: I need some Japanese yen, please.","櫃台:先生,你想把錢換成什麼貨幣? 顧客:我要一些日圓。"],["leader-106-15","If you want to \u0001change\u0002 your booking, we will try to help you, but we cannot guarantee that we will be able to do this.","如果你想改訂位,我們會盡力協助,但我們不能保證一定辦得到。"]],"channel (n.)":[["guide-115-55","Kenting National Park is in the southernmost area of the Taiwan island along Bashi \u0001Channel\u0002, which attracts tourists who wish to experience beautiful sunshine, ocean and nature.","墾丁國家公園位於台灣島最南端、巴士海峽沿岸,吸引想體驗美麗陽光、海洋與自然的遊客。"],["guide-109-39","The Trending Taiwan \u0001channel\u0002 on YouTube launched in 2015 presents short films that share impressive scenes of Taiwan.","YouTube 上於 2015 年開設的 Trending Taiwan 頻道,呈現分享台灣動人景象的短片。"]],"character (n.)":[["guide-110-54","The interior surface of the Mao Gong Ding is covered in a/an inscription of 500 \u0001characters\u0002.","毛公鼎的內壁刻滿了 500 字的銘文。"]],"characteristic (n.)":[["leader-112-72","Which of the following is not a possible \u0001characteristic\u0002 of green products?","下列何者不是綠色產品可能的特徵?"],["guide-107-77","According to the passage, what is one main \u0001characteristic\u0002 of the modern world?","根據本文,現代世界的一個主要特徵是什麼?"]],"checkpoint (n.)":[["leader-114-57","Any liquids you're carrying through \u0001checkpoints\u0002 must be less than 3.4 ounces and placed in a see-through bag no larger than a quart.","你通過安檢帶的任何液體必須少於 3.4 盎司,並放在不大於一夸脫的透明袋裡。"],["guide-113-55","Airline regulations insist on passengers using transparent plastic bags for carrying personal belongings through security \u0001checkpoints\u0002, ensuring swift inspection and compliance with safety measures.","航空規定要求旅客使用透明塑膠袋攜帶隨身物品通過安檢,以確保快速檢查並符合安全措施。"]],"chef (n.)":[["leader-111-59","In a Japanese restaurant, your personal \u0001chef\u0002 brings in the ingredients and cooks the food in front of you. He then serves the steaming hot gourmet dish.","在日式餐廳,你的專屬主廚會端上食材並在你面前烹調,接著上熱騰騰的美食。"],["leader-107-56","In order to run a profitable restaurant, you need to get a talented \u0001chef\u0002.","要經營一家賺錢的餐廳,你需要請一位有才華的主廚。"]],"coast (n.)":[["guide-114-25","If you are staying near the \u0001coast\u0002 in Taiwan, some homestays might offer activities like snorkeling in the sea.","如果你在台灣海邊住宿,有些民宿可能提供像浮潛這類的海上活動。"],["leader-106-20","When tourism is badly managed, it can destroy a place. \u0001Coasts\u0002, for example, are extremely vulnerable.","觀光管理不當會摧毀一個地方。例如海岸就極為脆弱易受害。"]],"coating (n.)":[["guide-113-2","To protect the houses from air pollution, a special \u0001coating\u0002 was applied on the exterior surface of the walls for all the houses in the town.","為保護房屋免受空氣污染,鎮上所有房屋的牆面外表都塗上了特殊塗層。"],["guide-107-72","Artisans have not only mastered a single method, but developed a variety of ways in which the \u0001coating\u0002 is used, both as a functional and a decorative material.","",4]],"collaborate (v.)":[["leader-114-7","I get along with my coworkers quite well. We often \u0001collaborate\u0002 on projects and enjoy spending time together during breaks.","我跟同事相處得很好。我們常一起合作專案,休息時也喜歡待在一起。"],["guide-107-73","Who \u0001collaborates\u0002 to present the exhibition “A New Layer”?","是誰合作呈現「A New Layer」這場展覽?"]],"commemorate (v.)":[["guide-114-4","The museum holds events to \u0001commemorate\u0002 the significance of the February 28 Incident in Taiwan's history.","博物館舉辦活動來紀念二二八事件在台灣歷史上的意義。"],["guide-112-26","The Dragon Boat Festival \u0001commemorates\u0002 Qu-Yuan, an old poet who drowned himself when a ruler ignored his advice.","端午節紀念屈原,一位在君王忽視其忠言後投江自盡的古代詩人。"]],"comment (n.)":[["guide-113-24","It is a good habit for students to keep a diary every day. However, it will be a time-consuming task for their teachers to review the diary and make some \u0001comments\u0002 on it every week.","學生每天寫日記是好習慣。然而,對老師來說,每週批閱日記並寫評語會是件耗時的工作。"],["guide-106-59","Dave checked out the \u0001comments\u0002 on the restaurant's Facebook page, only to find that most of them were negative.","戴夫查看了餐廳臉書頁面上的評論,卻發現大多是負評。"]],"comparable (adj.)":[["guide-113-22","Those items in this show room are \u0001comparable\u0002 in price and quality, so it's really a matter of what your own preference is in weight and color.","展示間裡的這些商品在價格與品質上相當(不相上下),所以真的取決於你自己對重量與顏色的偏好。"],["guide-110-8","A report indicates that Taiwanese people consume almost 7.9 kilograms of apples per person every year, \u0001comparable\u0002 to the quantity of bananas a Taiwanese has a year.","一份報告指出,台灣人每人每年食用將近 7.9 公斤蘋果,和台灣人一年吃的香蕉量相當。"]],"compartment (n.)":[["leader-111-4","Guest: Could you please help me put my carry-on bag into the overhead \u0001compartment\u0002? Flight attendant: Yes, no problem.","旅客:能幫我把隨身行李放進頭頂置物櫃嗎? 空服員:好的,沒問題。"],["leader-109-23","The overhead \u0001compartments\u0002 here seem to be full; we need to see if there is any space in another one.","這裡的頭頂置物櫃好像滿了,我們得看看另一個有沒有空間。"]],"compensation (n.)":[["leader-113-21","When the flight is delayed, the tour leader should calm the tourists and wait patiently for the airline to solve the problem. Also, the tour leader can ask the airline for \u0001compensation\u0002.","班機延誤時,領隊應安撫遊客,並耐心等候航空公司解決問題。領隊也可向航空公司要求補償。"],["leader-110-17","By the way, will the airline offer any \u0001compensation\u0002 for meals or accommodations?",""]],"competitive (adj.)":[["leader-114-69","Some local boutiques may offer \u0001competitive\u0002 pricing, especially on off-season items.","一些當地精品店可能提供有競爭力的價格,尤其是淡季商品。"],["guide-108-71","According to the article, which of the following does NOT explain why Taiwan is disadvantageous for developing large-scale, internationally \u0001competitive\u0002 hot spring resort centers?","根據本文,下列何者「不」是台灣不利發展大型、具國際競爭力溫泉度假中心的原因?"]],"competitor (n.)":[["leader-107-67","All businesses face competition. Your business \u0001competitor\u0002 could offer a substitute or similar product that makes your own redundant.","所有企業都面臨競爭。你的競爭對手可能推出替代或類似產品,讓你的產品變得多餘(被取代)。"],["guide-106-70","Compared with its \u0001competitor\u0002, CATE Travel is undoubtedly a leading travel agency. It is successful because it provides excellent services at affordable prices.","與競爭對手相比,CATE 旅行社無疑是領先的旅行社。它成功是因為以實惠價格提供優質服務。"]],"complacent (adj.)":[["leader-113-77","A passport validity of 10 years can make people \u0001complacent\u0002, forgetting that it actually requires renewing.","",4]],"complain (v.)":[["guide-111-64","When Lisa \u0001complained\u0002 about the slow service, the manager apologized.","當 Lisa 抱怨服務太慢時,經理道了歉。"],["leader-109-47","The customer looking at the forks and spoons \u0001complained\u0002 about the dirty and stained utensils to the waiter.","看著叉子湯匙的顧客,向服務生抱怨這些又髒又有污漬的餐具。"]],"conceal (v.)":[["leader-113-30","The purpose of a hidden door is for security; it is often used to \u0001conceal\u0002 a safe room or valuables.","隱藏門的目的是安全;它常用來隱藏密室或貴重物品。"]],"consent (n.)":[["guide-113-66","Guests must not interfere with the electrical network in the hotel rooms without the prior \u0001consent\u0002 of the management department.","未經管理部門的事先同意,房客不得干擾飯店房間的電力網路。"],["leader-108-61","The child should not participate in the experiment without his parents' \u0001consent\u0002.","未經父母同意,這孩子不應參加這項實驗。"]],"consumer (n.)":[["leader-112-34","The online food delivery industry has a special relationship with users in a three-way structure that includes \u0001consumers\u0002, restaurants, and couriers.","線上外送產業與用戶形成三方結構,包含消費者、餐廳和外送員。"]],"controversial (adj.)":[["guide-113-30","The \u0001controversial\u0002 art exhibit was designed to provoke thought and discussion among its viewers.","這場具爭議的藝術展旨在激發觀眾的思考與討論。"],["leader-110-76","His proposal for a glass pyramid was extremely \u0001controversial\u0002.","",1]],"cost (v.)":[["leader-111-19","This melon only \u0001costs\u0002 me $200 dollars.",""],["leader-107-27","A medical emergency can \u0001cost\u0002 you a lot of money. It is suggested that you buy travel insurance before you start your trip.","醫療緊急狀況可能花你很多錢。建議你出發前購買旅遊保險。"]],"courtesy (adj.)":[["leader-112-16","Some pet-friendly hotels offer \u0001courtesy\u0002 bags for walking your dog.","有些寵物友善飯店提供遛狗用的免費袋子。"],["leader-108-6","A \u0001courtesy\u0002 room is a room in a hotel made available to guests for a short period of time at no additional charge.","禮遇房是飯店免費提供給客人短時間使用的房間。"]],"cover (v.)":[["leader-114-27","I apologize on behalf of the company for our waitress's error, and we will \u0001cover\u0002 the cost of dry cleaning.","我代表公司為我們服務生的錯誤道歉,我們會負擔乾洗費用。"],["leader-107-73","When the restaurant was launched, it was \u0001covered\u0002 by CBC and other news outlets just for the selfie room, and it was a hot talking point on social media.","",4]],"coveted (adj.)":[["guide-106-72","What does the word “\u0001coveted\u0002” mean?","「coveted」這個字是什麼意思?"],["guide-106-71","A little known company that had never appeared in the rankings before took the \u0001coveted\u0002 Number One spot as the World's Best Tour Operator.","",1]],"craft (n.)":[["guide-108-32","Through holding many festivals and exhibitions, the government is dedicated to promoting Taiwanese traditional \u0001crafts\u0002 and performing arts.","政府透過舉辦許多節慶與展覽,致力於推廣台灣傳統工藝與表演藝術。"],["guide-107-28","Miaoli offers a wide variety of classic souvenirs ranging from wood \u0001craft\u0002, Tung blossom art, and Hakka cuisine.","苗栗提供各式各樣的經典伴手禮,從木雕、桐花藝術到客家美食。"]],"crucial (adj.)":[["leader-107-25","Staying safe when skiing or snowboarding in the mountains is \u0001crucial\u0002, and an important part of that is being aware of the risk of avalanche.","在山上滑雪或滑雪板時保持安全至關重要,其中重要的一環是意識到雪崩的風險。"]],"culture (n.)":[["guide-115-20","Make sure to include Chiayi in your trip to southern Taiwan if you are interested in traditional Taiwanese \u0001culture\u0002 such as embroidery and carpentry.","如果你對刺繡、木工等傳統台灣工藝文化有興趣,南台灣行程一定要納入嘉義。"],["guide-107-2","Be prepared to represent your country, because many foreigners will expect you to know a lot about history and \u0001culture\u0002 in your home country.","要準備好代表你的國家,因為許多外國人會期待你熟知母國的歷史與文化。"]],"curfew (n.)":[["guide-110-79","Amid the practice of social distancing, \u0001curfews\u0002, and lockdowns, it is very difficult for ordinary people to stay mentally sane and physically fit.","",4]],"custom (n.)":[["leader-107-53","B: Well, it's the \u0001custom\u0002 to bring a small gift.",""],["leader-107-61","We learn to be respectful to foreign cultures and do not judge carelessly other \u0001customs\u0002.","我們學著尊重外國文化,不輕率評斷別人的習俗。"]],"Customs (n.)":[["leader-114-45","Linda: After we land, we need to go through \u0001Customs\u0002 before leaving the airport.",""],["guide-112-40","If passengers have anything that needs to be declared, they should go through \u0001Customs\u0002.","若旅客有任何需要申報的物品,應走海關。"]],"dairy (adj.)":[["leader-108-47","\u0001Dairy\u0002 products refer to foods such as butter and cheese that are made from milk.","乳製品指的是由牛奶製成的食物,如奶油和起司。"],["leader-106-27","In less developed regions, avoid eating uncooked \u0001dairy\u0002 products, vegetables and salads.","在較不發達的地區,要避免吃未煮熟的乳製品、蔬菜和沙拉。"]],"debris (n.)":[["leader-112-80","The volunteers collect marine \u0001debris\u0002 to create an art wall near the beach.","",4]],"decade (n.)":[["leader-110-39","In the last \u0001decade\u0002, online shopping has experienced an explosive growth due to the fact it represents a more economic and convenient approach to purchasing in comparison to traditional shopping.","過去十年,網購爆炸性成長,因為相較於傳統購物,它是更經濟便利的購買方式。"],["guide-108-62","Since the cessation of the conflict over two \u0001decades\u0002 ago, many people have visited Kinmen, which boasts famous specialties and souvenirs.","自從二十多年前衝突停止以來,許多人造訪金門,那裡以名產與伴手禮聞名。"]],"decline (v.)":[["leader-115-28","Politely \u0001decline\u0002 and walk away if you feel uncomfortable with a taxi driver's or a vendor's offer.","如果你對計程車司機或攤販的開價感到不舒服,就禮貌地婉拒然後走開。"],["leader-110-19","Reception clerk: Sir, your credit card has been \u0001declined\u0002.",""]],"decouple (v.)":[["leader-115-80","…ons and an acceleration of climate action overall, it will have to join forces to strengthen the innovation needed for new technologies and alternative fuels to \u0001decouple\u0002 Travel & Tourism growth rates from resource use and emissions for a net zero future.","",4]],"dedicated (adj.)":[["leader-107-71","At Doomie's, a vegetarian restaurant in Toronto, there is a \u0001dedicated\u0002 selfie room where persons stand in front of a mirror, take a photo and post it to social media, often with a caption like \"just emerged from my food coma.\" When they were planning the …","",1]],"describe (v.)":[["leader-111-15","Police: Could you \u0001describe\u0002 the situation?",""],["leader-109-4","Clerk: Could you \u0001describe\u0002 to me what your bag looks like? Traveler: It's a black duffle bag with a yellow strap.","人員:能描述一下你的包長什麼樣子嗎? 旅客:是個黑色行李袋配黃色背帶。"]],"desert (n.)":[["guide-110-18","The Atacama \u0001Desert\u0002 in Peru and Chile resembles Mars in many ways. Soil samples taken from Mars have been found to be surprisingly similar to those taken from this desert.","祕魯和智利的阿他加馬沙漠在許多方面類似火星。從火星取得的土壤樣本被發現與這座沙漠取得的驚人地相似。"],["leader-106-7","If the beach and the \u0001desert\u0002 lose their appeal, visitors can always go skiing at Ski Dubai, an indoor ski resort.","如果海灘和沙漠失去吸引力,遊客隨時可到室內滑雪場 Ski Dubai 滑雪。"]],"designate (v.)":[["leader-111-22","Kaeng Krachan Forest Complex is \u0001designated\u0002 as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2021. This area is located between the Himalayan, Indochina, and Sumatran faunal with rich biodiversity and home to many endangered plants and wildlife species.","Kaeng Krachan 森林區於 2021 年被指定為聯合國教科文組織世界遺產。此區位於喜馬拉雅、中南半島與蘇門答臘動物區系之間,生物多樣性豐富,是許多瀕危植物與野生動物的家園。"],["guide-106-12","The Taj Mahal was \u0001designated\u0002 as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1983 for being “the jewel of Muslim art in India.”","泰姬瑪哈陵於 1983 年被指定為聯合國教科文組織世界遺產,譽為「印度穆斯林藝術的珍寶」。"]],"designated (adj.)":[["guide-114-14","Foreign travelers who make purchases of at least NT$2,000 on the same day from the same \u0001designated\u0002 stores with the “Taiwan Tax Refund”-label are eligible to request the refund.","外國旅客在同一天於同一貼有「Taiwan Tax Refund」標誌的指定商店消費滿新台幣 2,000 元,即有資格申請退稅。"],["guide-108-33","On the MRT of Taiwan, visitors carrying bicycles can get on and off the train only at \u0001designated\u0002 stations.","在台灣捷運,攜帶單車的旅客只能在指定車站上下車。"]],"devastating (adj.)":[["leader-110-71","Which of the following is closest in meaning to \"\u0001devastating\u0002\"?","與 devastating 意思最接近的字是?"],["leader-110-71","Unfortunately, the environmental impacts of tourism can be \u0001devastating\u0002 when profit takes precedence.","",1]],"diet (n.)":[["leader-108-79","However, people in other parts of the world think this food is totally normal and is a regular part of their \u0001diet\u0002.","",4],["leader-106-53","Fresh fruit and vegetables are an essential component of a healthy \u0001diet\u0002.","新鮮蔬果是健康飲食不可或缺的一部分。"]],"dining (n.)":[["guide-114-19","Taipei 101 is a landmark of Taiwan. It is Taiwan's tallest building as well as a great place for shopping, \u0001dining\u0002 and seeing sights.","台北 101 是台灣的地標。它是台灣最高的建築,也是購物、用餐與觀光的好去處。"],["leader-112-71","For example, the Environmental Protection Administration (EPA) held a reward program that customers could earn \"green points\" after \u0001dining\u0002 at environmentally friendly restaurants.","",4]],"dip (v.)":[["guide-115-59","A hot pot meal includes a table-side pan of boiling soup where you can \u0001dip\u0002 meat and vegetables in to cook before you eat.","火鍋餐會有一鍋桌邊沸騰的湯,你可以把肉和蔬菜涮(浸)進去煮熟再吃。"],["guide-110-15","The temperature has \u0001dipped\u0002 so low that the mountain is blanketed with snow.","氣溫驟降到很低,以致山上覆滿了雪。"]],"direct (v.)":[["guide-113-23","The signs will \u0001direct\u0002 you there.",""],["guide-110-51","Guide signs are installed to \u0001direct\u0002 disabled passengers to the trains.","車站裝設了引導標誌,以引導身障旅客前往列車。"]],"disabled (adj.)":[["leader-111-34","Hotel Customer: Do you provide facilities for \u0001disabled\u0002 people, such as adjustable beds, shower chairs, and barrier-free paths?","飯店客人:你們有為身障者提供設施嗎?例如可調式床、淋浴椅和無障礙通道。"],["guide-110-49","Every station has a ticket gate for the \u0001disabled\u0002, wheelchair users, or passengers with strollers or bulky packages.","每個車站都有一個給身障者、輪椅使用者,或帶嬰兒車、大型包裹旅客的票閘。"]],"discerning (adj.)":[["guide-114-76","With the rise of online booking platforms, social media, and review sites, guests have become more \u0001discerning\u0002 and demanding.","",1]],"disembark (v.)":[["leader-113-75","If you book a layover flight, it means the plane will make a stop en route, with passengers \u0001disembarking\u0002 the flight and changing services.","",4]],"displace (v.)":[["guide-115-76","But those costs aren't low enough, nor is the culture surrounding car ownership weak enough, to \u0001displace\u0002 private cars.","",4]],"disposable (adj.)":[["leader-113-5","Customer: May I have two plastic forks, please? Receptionist: Unfortunately, we no longer provide any \u0001disposable\u0002 utensils due to the new environmental protection act.","顧客:可以給我兩支塑膠叉子嗎? 櫃台:抱歉,因新環保法我們不再提供任何拋棄式餐具。"],["leader-109-76","Plastic pollution has become one of the most pressing environmental issues, as rapidly increasing production of \u0001disposable\u0002 plastic products overwhelms the world's ability to deal with them.","",1]],"distance (n.)":[["leader-115-33","Please keep a safe \u0001distance\u0002 between yourself and the cliff edge while taking photos.","拍照時請與懸崖邊緣保持安全距離。"],["leader-113-60","In Europe, where travel \u0001distances\u0002 are often short, it is usually more convenient and inexpensive to travel by train than by airplane.","在歐洲,由於旅行距離常常很短,搭火車通常比搭飛機更方便且便宜。"]],"district (n.)":[["leader-115-6","In many major US cities, people can visit the shopping \u0001districts\u0002 there to make purchases.","在許多美國大城市,人們可以去購物區採買。"],["guide-112-17","Yingge \u0001District\u0002 in New Taipei City has been renowned for its pottery for a long time, but recently, tourists have realized that this area offers so much more.","新北市鶯歌區長久以來以陶瓷聞名,但最近遊客發現這個地區能提供的遠不止於此。"]],"diversity (n.)":[["guide-112-76","To discover the diversity of the natural world.","為了探索自然界的多樣性。",2]],"document (n.)":[["leader-108-46","The \u0001document\u0002 was supposed to be confidential and to keep secret the names of the parties involved.","這份文件本應保密,以保守相關當事人的姓名。"],["leader-106-2","Having an important \u0001document\u0002 expire before or during your trip is the last thing you want to happen.","重要證件在旅行前或旅行中過期,是你最不希望發生的事。"]],"dominant (adj.)":[["guide-113-48","English became the \u0001dominant\u0002 language in international business, facilitating communication among people from diverse linguistic backgrounds in the global market.","英語成為國際商業的主導語言,促進了全球市場中不同語言背景者之間的溝通。"],["leader-106-25","Even though Mandarin may soon become an important world language, it probably won't be the \u0001dominant\u0002 language because the writing system is too difficult.","儘管中文可能很快成為重要的世界語言,但因書寫系統太難,它大概不會成為主導語言。"]],"drastically (adv.)":[["guide-106-45","The number of refugees in European countries such as Germany and France has soared so \u0001drastically\u0002 over the past few years.","過去幾年,德法等歐洲國家的難民人數激增,劇烈程度使公眾意見分歧。"]],"driver (n.)":[["guide-113-17","Tourism is one of the city's economic mainstays and an important \u0001driver\u0002 of economic growth that provides more employment opportunities to people.","觀光是這座城市的經濟支柱之一,也是提供更多就業機會、推動經濟成長的重要動力。"],["guide-107-41","Even if I could drive the tour bus, I wouldn't. Let's wait for the \u0001driver\u0002.","就算我會開遊覽車,我也不會開。我們等司機吧。"]],"durable (adj.)":[["leader-114-28","Make sure to purchase a strong and \u0001durable\u0002 carry-on bag to ensure your belongings are safe during travel.","務必買一個堅固耐用的隨身包,確保旅行時物品安全。"],["leader-112-60","I highly recommend this blue tote bag because of its high quality. It is very \u0001durable\u0002 and water-resistant.","我強力推薦這個藍色托特包,品質很好。它非常耐用又防水。"]],"duty-free (adj.)":[["leader-112-46","If you carry more than the \u0001duty-free\u0002 allowance, including a bottle of alcohol, the items will be confiscated.","若攜帶超過免稅額度(含一瓶酒),物品將被沒收。"],["guide-108-52","For some passengers, browsing the \u0001duty-free\u0002 catalogue during the flight is a highlight of the journey.","對某些旅客來說,飛行中瀏覽免稅商品目錄是旅程的一大亮點。"]],"eager (adj.)":[["guide-113-80","Culinary tourists are \u0001eager\u0002 to learn more about different cultures through their foods.","",4],["guide-109-76","In much of the world, there are places that are \u0001eager\u0002 to welcome tourists.","",1]],"earthquake (n.)":[["guide-108-29","Visitors sometimes experience \u0001earthquakes\u0002 during their stay in Taiwan and may suffer from power cuts and hampered transportation.","旅客在台停留期間有時會遇到地震,並可能因停電與交通受阻而受苦。"],["leader-107-65","\u0001Earthquakes\u0002 are not uncommon for residents in Japan, but the 7.1-magnitude quake, one of the strongest in recent years, came as a shock.","對日本居民來說地震並不罕見,但這場近年最強的 7.1 級地震仍令人震驚。"]],"ease (v.)":[["leader-110-50","I am having a headache. Do you have any painkiller to \u0001ease\u0002 the uncomfortable feeling?","我頭痛。你有止痛藥能緩解這不適嗎?"],["leader-109-54","To \u0001ease\u0002 the customer's anger, the manager offered her a free meal to make up for the problem. But she still felt displeased.","為平息顧客的怒氣,經理招待她一頓免費餐彌補問題,但她仍不滿意。"]],"eatery (n.)":[["guide-113-61","In Taiwan, you don't need to worry about traveling far to find \u0001eateries\u0002 that offer inexpensive food.","在台灣,你不用擔心要跑很遠才能找到提供便宜食物的餐館。"],["guide-110-9","Summertime is definitely the best time to visit Penghu Islands. There are \u0001eateries\u0002 open the whole day, and mini cruise ships would take you to fascinating places.","夏天絕對是造訪澎湖群島的最佳時機。整天都有餐館營業,迷你郵輪還會帶你到迷人的地方。"]],"eco-friendly (adj.)":[["leader-114-14","\u0001Eco-friendly\u0002 travel is now one of the fastest-growing trends in the industry, and many people embrace this promising development.","環保旅遊現在是業界成長最快的趨勢之一,許多人擁抱這個有前景的發展。"],["guide-113-46","More and more governments are making commitments to sustainable tourism by providing \u0001eco-friendly\u0002 accommodations, conservation efforts, and community engagement initiatives.","越來越多政府承諾推動永續觀光,提供環保住宿、保育行動與社區參與計畫。"]],"ecological (adj.)":[["leader-113-45","\u0001Ecological\u0002 tourism encourages sustainable travel, fostering appreciation for natural wonders while promoting conservation efforts crucial for preserving our planet's biodiversity.","生態旅遊鼓勵永續旅行,培養對自然奇景的欣賞,同時推動對保護地球生物多樣性至關重要的保育工作。"],["leader-112-74","In general, green products are known as \u0001ecological\u0002 products or environmentally friendly products that impact less on the environment.","",4]],"edible (adj.)":[["guide-112-65","The plastic vegetable leaves on the plate are for decoration only. They are not \u0001edible\u0002.","盤子上的塑膠菜葉只是裝飾用的。它們不能食用。"]],"efficient (adj.)":[["guide-113-29","If you're traveling to the airport, the shuttle bus will only stop up to two more times after your pickup. By reducing the number of stops, we strive to provide a safer, more \u0001efficient\u0002, and more pleasant transportation experience.","如果你要去機場,接駁車在載你之後最多只再停兩站。透過減少停靠次數,我們努力提供更安全、更有效率、更愉快的交通體驗。"],["leader-107-58","Sending text messages over the phone is a very \u0001efficient\u0002 way to communicate. It is faster and easier than calling.","用手機傳簡訊是很有效率的溝通方式,比打電話更快更容易。"]],"eliminate (v.)":[["guide-115-63","The team is committed to implementing strategies to \u0001eliminate\u0002 fatal and serious traffic crashes in the city.","該團隊致力於推行策略,以消除城市中致命與嚴重的交通事故。"],["leader-114-58","You can buy some disinfecting wipes in order to \u0001eliminate\u0002 viruses and bacteria on surfaces.","你可以買一些消毒濕巾來清除表面的病毒和細菌。"]],"embrace (v.)":[["guide-115-4","In Kaohsiung City, which \u0001embraces\u0002 the largest seaport in Taiwan, the streets are broad and the weather is sunny most of the time.","高雄市擁有全台最大的海港,街道寬闊,天氣多半晴朗。"],["leader-114-14","Eco-friendly travel is now one of the fastest-growing trends in the industry, and many people \u0001embrace\u0002 this promising development.","環保旅遊現在是業界成長最快的趨勢之一,許多人擁抱這個有前景的發展。"]],"emphasize (v.)":[["guide-114-74","What is a likely reason why effective governance practices are \u0001emphasized\u0002 in the passage?","本文為何強調有效的治理作為,最可能的原因為何?"],["leader-112-71","Countries all over the world are increasingly \u0001emphasizing\u0002 environmental conservation matters.","",4]],"enact (v.)":[["guide-112-74","Austria and France have \u0001enacted\u0002 bans on short-haul domestic flights.","",4]],"encounter (v.)":[["leader-115-54","When you \u0001encounter\u0002 crowds in a popular tourist site, remember to pay more attention to your surroundings.","在熱門觀光景點遇到人潮時,記得多留意你的周遭環境。"],["guide-113-13","When traveling to popular tourist destinations during peak season, \u0001encountering\u0002 crowds is inevitably a part of the experience.","在旺季前往熱門旅遊景點時,遇到人潮不可避免地是體驗的一部分。"]],"enforce (v.)":[["leader-114-70","The inspector expressed his concerns about the lack of an adequate effort to \u0001enforce\u0002 customs laws along the border.","稽查員表達他對邊境缺乏足夠努力執行海關法規的擔憂。"],["leader-108-55","To save the animals in the reserve, police officers are working to \u0001enforce\u0002 the anti-poaching laws in Africa.","為了拯救保護區的動物,警察正努力執行非洲的反盜獵法。"]],"engaged (adj.)":[["guide-109-73","You may also get some ideas about which diamond to buy when you're getting \u0001engaged\u0002.","",4]],"enormous (adj.)":[["guide-114-27","The Mazu pilgrimage, which lasts over a week and covers hundreds of kilometers, is one of Taiwan's religious festivals. It is like an \u0001enormous\u0002 birthday celebration for the “Goddess of the Sea.”","媽祖遶境進香持續一週以上、綿延數百公里,是台灣的宗教節慶之一,就像為「海上女神」舉辦的盛大生日慶典。"],["leader-106-39","Most visitors to Easter Island come specifically to see the 887 moai, \u0001enormous\u0002 statues carved out of volcanic rock, scattered around the island.","多數到復活節島的遊客,是專程來看散布全島的 887 尊摩艾——用火山岩雕成的巨大石像。"]],"entertainment (n.)":[["leader-111-45","Passenger: Could you show me how to operate the in-flight \u0001entertainment\u0002?",""],["leader-109-63","Passengers can stay connected with onboard WiFi or enjoy films, music, and other inflight \u0001entertainment\u0002 available during their flight.","乘客可用機上 WiFi 保持連線,或享受電影、音樂和其他機上娛樂。"]],"entitled (adj.)":[["guide-111-6","If your flight has been canceled by the airline, you are \u0001entitled\u0002 to a refund that only applies to services you have not received.","若你的航班被航空公司取消,你有權獲得退款,但僅限你尚未使用的服務。"],["leader-109-48","All the room guests are \u0001entitled\u0002 to use the hotel facilities during their stay.","所有房客在住宿期間都有權使用飯店設施。"]],"entrée (n.)":[["leader-108-37","Dinner features a hot \u0001entrée\u0002 of chicken, veal, or lamb. After the main course, dessert will be served.","晚餐主打雞、小牛或羊肉的熱主菜。主菜之後會上甜點。"],["guide-108-17","For my \u0001entrée\u0002, I will have the T-bone steak, please.","我的主菜要點丁骨牛排,謝謝。"]],"entry (n.)":[["leader-113-39","The sign \"Do Not Enter\" marks the restricted area where only those with permission are allowed \u0001entry\u0002.","「禁止進入」的標誌標示限制區,只有獲准者才能進入。"],["leader-111-40","If your passport is lost or stolen abroad, and you need to return to Taiwan right away, you may apply for a(n) \"\u0001Entry\u0002 Certificate for the Republic of China Nationals.\"","若你在國外遺失或被竊護照,又需立刻返台,可申請「中華民國國民入國證明書」。"]],"equipment (n.)":[["leader-110-1","Clerk: Someone will get the first aid \u0001equipment\u0002 and come straight up.",""],["leader-110-41","Lisa: Do you have any exercise facilities? Hotel clerk: You can go to the 15th floor where our gym is and as long as you have running shoes with you, you can use all of our \u0001equipment\u0002 with no extra charge.","Lisa:你們有健身設施嗎? 櫃台:可以到 15 樓的健身房,只要隨身帶著跑鞋,所有器材都能免費使用。"]],"establish (v.)":[["guide-115-53","Yushan National Park is the biggest park in Taiwan and was \u0001established\u0002 in 1985.","玉山國家公園是台灣最大的國家公園,於 1985 年設立。"]],"ethical (adj.)":[["guide-115-28","With a growing focus on responsible and \u0001ethical\u0002 tourism, sustainable tourism is becoming an increasingly important industry worldwide.","隨著對負責任且合乎道德的觀光日益重視,永續觀光正成為全球日益重要的產業。"]],"evacuate (v.)":[["guide-106-55","The US has \u0001evacuated\u0002 all the ambassadors and diplomatic staff because that country is on the verge of civil war.","美國已撤離所有大使與外交人員,因為那個國家正瀕臨內戰邊緣。"]],"expense (n.)":[["guide-114-52","If you do not have appropriate insurance before you travel, you could be liable for emergency \u0001expenses\u0002.","如果你在旅行前沒有適當的保險,可能需要自行負擔緊急費用。"],["leader-108-67","In many companies, employees will be reimbursed for paying business travel \u0001expenses\u0002 from their own funds.","在許多公司,員工自掏腰包墊付商務差旅費後可獲核銷退還。"]],"expiration (n.)":[["leader-115-29","Passenger: How long is my ticket good for? Station staff: It's good until the \u0001expiration\u0002 date written on the ticket.","乘客:我的票有效到什麼時候? 站務員:到票上寫的到期日為止。"],["leader-107-16","The \u0001expiration\u0002 date for a medicine is the last date that the manufacturer guarantees the medicine is safe or effective.","藥品的有效期限日期,是製造商保證藥品安全或有效的最後日期。"]],"exploitation (n.)":[["guide-111-74","Nonetheless, it also brings the change or loss of indigenous identity and values, culture clashes, and ethical issues (such as an increase in sex tourism or the \u0001exploitation\u0002 of child workers).","",4]],"exterior (n.)":[["guide-115-71","The male bird, with its deep blue feathers and scarf-like orange markings, inspired the \u0001exterior\u0002 design, bringing vitality to the otherwise subdued color palette.","",4],["guide-114-5","The historical value of the museum lies in its \u0001exterior\u0002 design which preserves the architectural trends of the early 20th century.","博物館的歷史價值在於其外觀設計保留了 20 世紀初的建築風潮。"]],"extra (adj.)":[["guide-113-54","Is it possible to order an \u0001extra\u0002 serving for him?",""],["guide-109-23","Guest: Is the tip included in the bill? Server: The tip is \u0001extra\u0002, sir.","客人:帳單有含小費嗎? 服務生:小費另計,先生。"]],"facility (n.)":[["leader-108-66","John: Do you have any other \u0001facilities\u0002 in the hotel? Hotel clerk: We have an indoor swimming pool.","John:飯店還有其他設施嗎? 櫃台:我們有室內游泳池。"]],"fair (adj.)":[["guide-114-23","We recommend exchanging your money at the bank because you get a \u0001fair\u0002 rate.","我們建議在銀行換錢,因為你能拿到公道的匯率。"]],"fantastic (adj.)":[["guide-113-11","The city of Kaohsiung in Taiwan has been performing a \u0001fantastic\u0002 job in enhancing its network of off-road bicycle trails, providing ample chances for leisure activities, family outings, and daily commutes.","高雄市在擴展自行車道路網方面表現出色,為休閒活動、家庭出遊與日常通勤提供充足機會。"],["guide-107-14","Many historical stores and buildings have been transformed into \u0001fantastic\u0002 restaurants.","許多歷史悠久的店家與建築已改造成很棒的餐廳。"]],"feature (v.)":[["guide-113-9","The park's landscape \u0001features\u0002 unique coastal rock formations shaped by natural forces over several million years.","這座公園的地景以…為特色,擁有由自然力量歷經數百萬年塑造的獨特海岸岩層。"],["leader-111-52","This particular restaurant in Marriott \u0001features\u0002 and serves authentic Greek dishes.","萬豪這間餐廳主打並供應道地的希臘菜。"]],"feet (n.)":[["leader-110-52","Can you raise your \u0001feet\u0002 a little off the floor? I want to clean the floor under the table.","你能把腳稍微抬離地板嗎?我想清潔桌子底下的地板。"],["leader-109-53","The plane is now cruising at 30,000 \u0001feet\u0002 and the \"fasten seat belts\" sign has just been turned off.","飛機現在在 3 萬英尺巡航,「繫安全帶」燈號剛熄滅。"]],"fill (v.)":[["guide-112-37","The doctor wrote me a/an prescription. I need to get it \u0001filled\u0002 at the pharmacy.","醫生開給我一張處方箋。我需要拿去藥局配藥。"],["leader-110-48","Traveler: Excuse me, I need some hot water to make the milk for my baby. Flight attendant: Sure, I can \u0001fill\u0002 the bottle for you.","旅客:不好意思,我需要熱水幫寶寶泡奶。 空服員:好的,我幫你裝奶瓶。"]],"financial (adj.)":[["leader-111-2","Do you have a(n) \u0001financial\u0002 proof to verify that you have enough money to stay in this country?","你有財力證明來核實你有足夠的錢待在這個國家嗎?"],["guide-106-3","The service of PayPal gives people simpler ways to send money without sharing \u0001financial\u0002 information.","PayPal 的服務讓人們能以更簡單的方式匯款,而不必分享財務資訊。"]],"fine (n.)":[["guide-110-4","Taiwan has become the first country in Asia to totally ban the eating of dog and cat meat, and violating the rule is punishable by up to $8,000 in \u0001fines\u0002.","台灣成為亞洲第一個完全禁止食用貓狗肉的國家,違規者最高可罰 8,000 元。"],["guide-107-45","The city government legislated an increase in \u0001fines\u0002 for those who do not fasten their seat belts.","市府立法提高對不繫安全帶者的罰款。"]],"flavor (n.)":[["guide-114-59","Featuring the most local and complex \u0001flavors\u0002, the coffee served in most of the coffee shops at Alishan is grown and roasted by the owner.","阿里山多數咖啡館供應的咖啡,具有最在地、最複雜的風味,由店主親自栽種與烘焙。"],["guide-112-31","A: How does Mexican cuisine taste? B: It has a spicy and heavy \u0001flavor\u0002.","A:墨西哥菜嚐起來如何? B:它味道又辣又重。"]],"flush (v.)":[["leader-115-9","Guest: The toilet won't \u0001flush\u0002. Receptionist: We'll send a repairperson within half an hour.","房客:馬桶沖不了水。 櫃台:我們半小時內派維修人員過去。"],["leader-113-56","Tour Leader: Hi, we have a problem in one of our rooms—the toilet isn't \u0001flushing\u0002 properly.",""]],"focus (n.)":[["leader-115-76","What is the main \u0001focus\u0002 of this passage?","本文的主要焦點為何?"],["leader-113-76","What is the primary \u0001focus\u0002 of this passage?","本文的主要焦點為何?"]],"forbidden (adj.)":[["guide-115-44","A: Can I bring my pet along on the trip? B: No, to protect the rights and comfort of all passengers, pets are \u0001forbidden\u0002 on board.","A:我可以帶寵物一起去嗎? B:不行,為保障所有乘客的權益與舒適,寵物禁止上車/機。"]],"force (v.)":[["leader-108-56","The approaching fire \u0001forced\u0002 hundreds of people to abandon their homes.","逼近的大火迫使數百人拋棄家園。"],["leader-107-70","Uber drivers will now be \u0001forced\u0002 to take a six-hour break after a total of 12 hours of driving time. Drivers will not be able to accept new riders during that rest period.","Uber 司機累計開 12 小時後,將被強制休息六小時。休息期間不能接新乘客。"]],"foreigner (n.)":[["leader-110-59","Alice has learned from the news that \u0001foreigners\u0002 cannot enter Taiwan because of the COVID-19.","Alice 從新聞得知,由於 COVID-19,外國人不能入境台灣。"],["guide-107-2","Be prepared to represent your country, because many \u0001foreigners\u0002 will expect you to know a lot about history and culture in your home country.","要準備好代表你的國家,因為許多外國人會期待你熟知母國的歷史與文化。"]],"forte (n.)":[["guide-111-30","Given her angelic voice, there is no doubt that singing is her \u0001forte\u0002.","憑她天籟般的嗓音,毫無疑問唱歌是她的專長。"],["guide-106-71","…cally to address the demands of deep-pocketed, experienced travelers who had “been there and done that.” Owner Cari Gray's \u0001forte\u0002 is finding awesome places to ride, with great scenery, hotels, food, and most of all, fantastic pavement with little traffic.","",1]],"fortress (n.)":[["leader-110-78","Louvre, originally constructed as a \u0001fortress\u0002, was the home of the kings of France until Louis XIV chose Versailles for his household, leaving the Louvre primarily as a home for artists and intellectuals.","",4]],"fragile (adj.)":[["leader-107-19","When travelling with delicate or breakable objects, you'd better declare them as \u0001fragile\u0002. The airline will put stickers on the boxes or bags and take special care of them.","攜帶精細或易碎物品旅行時,最好申報為易碎品。航空公司會在箱子或袋子上貼標籤並特別照料。"],["guide-106-38","Items such as glass bottles and ceramic vases are \u0001fragile\u0002. Be careful if you have them in your luggage.","玻璃瓶、陶瓷花瓶等物品很易碎。如果放在行李中要小心。"]],"fragmented (adj.)":[["leader-115-78","What does the word \"\u0001fragmented\u0002\" in the phrase \"fragmented regulatory landscape\" most nearly mean?","在「fragmented regulatory landscape(破碎/各自為政的法規環境)」這個詞組中,\"fragmented\" 一字最接近的意思是?"],["leader-115-76","These include emission measurement, especially Scope 3 emissions, the \u0001fragmented\u0002 regulatory landscape, inconsistencies in reporting standards and insufficient budgets remains issues.","",1]],"free (adj.)":[["leader-115-20","We will stop at this location for two hours, and you are \u0001free\u0002 to walk around and make some small purchases.","我們會在這裡停留兩小時,你可以自由四處走走、買點小東西。"],["leader-106-36","Tourist: What is the admission fee? Receptionist: It's \u0001free\u0002.","遊客:門票多少錢? 櫃台:免費。"]],"frequent (adj.)":[["guide-111-8","Please pay close attention to the safety instructions even if you are a \u0001frequent\u0002 flyer.","即使你是常飛的旅客,也請密切注意安全須知。"],["leader-109-15","Janet uses her \u0001frequent\u0002 flyer miles to get a free flight from Tokyo to Taipei.","Janet 用她的常客飛行哩程換一趟東京到台北的免費航班。"]],"gallery (n.)":[["guide-111-50","Alex has such a strong passion for art that he spends most of his spare time in museums and \u0001galleries\u0002.","Alex 對藝術有如此強烈的熱情,以致他大部分空閒時間都待在博物館和藝廊。"],["leader-108-69","A crowd already filled the art \u0001gallery\u0002 in order to see the famous paintings of Van Gogh.","人群已擠滿藝術展場(畫廊),只為看梵谷的名畫。"]],"gastronomic (adj.)":[["guide-113-79","Which of the following has the closest meaning to the word “\u0001gastronomic\u0002” in the first paragraph?","下列何者與第一段的 gastronomic 意思最接近?"],["guide-113-76","Experts estimate interest in \u0001gastronomic\u0002 tours will increase more than 16 percent a year for the next ten years.","",1]],"generous (adj.)":[["guide-106-27","Resolve to be tender with the young, compassionate with the aged, understanding of those who are wrong, and \u0001generous\u0002 to the poor.","下定決心要對年輕人溫柔、對老者慈悲、對犯錯者體諒、對貧者慷慨。"]],"glacier (n.)":[["guide-111-76","The seven-hour trip gives tourists breathtaking views of snow-capped mountains, \u0001glaciers\u0002 and fjords.","",1],["leader-106-45","Across India, poverty and a degraded environment are two increasingly difficult issues. Forests and \u0001glaciers\u0002 are dwindling, air and land are being polluted, and coastlines are disappearing.","在印度各地,貧窮與惡化的環境是兩大日益棘手的問題。森林與冰川逐漸消失,空氣和土地遭受污染,海岸線也逐漸消失。"]],"gluten (n.)":[["leader-115-1","A \u0001gluten\u0002-intolerant meal does not contain any gluten-based product.","(給)麩質不耐者的餐點不含任何麩質製品。"],["leader-112-11","\u0001Gluten\u0002 intolerant meal does not contain any gluten-based product.","不耐麩質餐點不含任何麩質產品(即無麩質餐)。"]],"goddess (n.)":[["guide-115-14","The Mazu pilgrimage is one of the most noted folk religious festivals in Taiwan. People go on a journey to honor the \u0001goddess\u0002 Mazu.","媽祖遶境進香是台灣最著名的民間宗教節慶之一。人們踏上旅程來敬奉媽祖女神。"],["guide-114-27","The Mazu pilgrimage, which lasts over a week and covers hundreds of kilometers, is one of Taiwan's religious festivals. It is like an enormous birthday celebration for the “\u0001Goddess\u0002 of the Sea.”","媽祖遶境進香持續一週以上、綿延數百公里,是台灣的宗教節慶之一,就像為「海上女神」舉辦的盛大生日慶典。"]],"gourmet (n.)":[["guide-113-28","Aaron is a \u0001gourmet\u0002. He likes to try exotic food whenever he travels in foreign countries.","Aaron 是美食家。每當在外國旅行時,他喜歡嘗試異國美食。"]],"grab (v.)":[["leader-112-64","A: I am hungry and want to \u0001grab\u0002 some food. B: Try this toll-free number 1-800-522-5942 for Burger Hot to order a meal.","A:我餓了,想找點吃的。 B:打這支免付費電話 1-800-522-5942 向 Burger Hot 點餐。"],["leader-109-49","Let's \u0001grab\u0002 some snacks to eat.",""]],"gratuity (n.)":[["guide-112-21","In many countries, it is customary to leave a \u0001gratuity\u0002 while dining out.","在許多國家,外出用餐時留小費是慣例。"],["guide-108-16","The service was terrible at the restaurant, so we didn't leave a \u0001gratuity\u0002.","這家餐廳服務很糟,所以我們沒留小費。"]],"groceries (n.)":[["leader-115-49","Our hotel is a bit far away from the city center; if you need to buy some \u0001groceries\u0002, there is a small store nearby.","我們飯店離市中心有點遠;如果你需要買些生活雜貨,附近有間小店。"],["guide-107-48","The store adjacent to the hotel is a convenience store which provides a range of everyday items such as \u0001groceries\u0002, snacks, or drinks.","飯店旁的便利商店提供各種日常用品,例如雜貨、零食或飲料。"]],"guideline (n.)":[["leader-109-16","Please check with your airline and look at the Restricted Articles \u0001Guidelines\u0002 before packing your suitcases.","打包行李前,請洽航空公司並查看違禁物品指南。"]],"handicraft (n.)":[["leader-115-56","In the areas around this lake, you can find many boutiques selling refined clothes and local \u0001handicrafts\u0002.","在這座湖周邊,你可以找到許多販售精緻服飾和當地手工藝品的精品店。"],["guide-108-34","Launched in 2017, a new government sponsored TV station provides a variety of indigenous programming on folk music, dance, \u0001handicraft\u0002, and so on.","2017 年開播、由政府贊助的新電視台,提供多樣的原住民節目,包含民族音樂、舞蹈、手工藝等。"]],"harmful (adj.)":[["leader-114-15","Scientists found \u0001harmful\u0002 particles in dolphins' breath off Florida, raising concerns for their health and the environment.","科學家在佛州外海海豚的呼吸中發現有害微粒,引發對牠們健康和環境的擔憂。"],["leader-107-62","A study points out that when you are in a plane, the sun's rays are much more \u0001harmful\u0002, and you face an increased risk of skin damage, skin ageing, and skin cancer.","研究指出,在飛機上時陽光更有害,你面臨皮膚傷害、老化和皮膚癌的風險增加。"]],"heavenly (adj.)":[["guide-111-33","Our last holiday was a five-day trip to Bali. We enjoyed \u0001heavenly\u0002 weather during our vacation on the tropical island.","我們上次假期是去峇里島玩五天。在那座熱帶島嶼度假時,我們享受了絕佳(宜人)的天氣。"],["leader-106-28","Anybody looking for a truly \u0001heavenly\u0002 experience will think that they have walked into paradise at the Chocolate Show in New York.","任何想尋求極致美妙體驗的人,到紐約巧克力展會覺得自己彷彿走進了天堂。"]],"highway (n.)":[["leader-112-56","I am afraid that part of the \u0001highway\u0002 to the airport is under construction, so you may need to take a detour.","恐怕往機場的部分公路正在施工,所以你可能得繞道。"],["leader-107-1","I enjoyed my vacation in San Francisco. I was most impressed by the beautiful scenes along the Pacific Coast \u0001Highway\u0002.","我很享受在舊金山的假期。太平洋海岸公路沿途的美景讓我印象最深刻。"]],"hover (v.)":[["leader-111-72","Therefore, your takeaway might not come with a knock at the door, but with a drone \u0001hovering\u0002 outside your window.","",4],["leader-111-73","Which word is closest in meaning to the word \"\u0001hovering\u0002\" in the passage?","與文中 hovering 意思最接近的字是?"]],"hurricane (n.)":[["leader-111-44","Flight attendant: Your flight has been cancelled due to a \u0001hurricane\u0002 in Florida. Passenger: Will the airline company arrange accommodation for us?","空服員:你的航班因佛州颶風取消了。 乘客:航空公司會為我們安排住宿嗎?"],["leader-106-69","People living in the track of the \u0001hurricane\u0002 have been advised to leave their homes until it has passed.","住在颶風行進路徑上的居民,已被建議撤離家園直到颶風過去。"]],"iconic (adj.)":[["guide-115-65","Designed to look like a pole of bamboo, this skyscraper is the tallest and most \u0001iconic\u0002 landmark of the city.","這棟以竹節造型設計的摩天大樓(台北 101),是該市最高、最具代表性的地標。"],["guide-111-29","Those who gave valedictory speeches paid their tribute to one of the most \u0001iconic\u0002 figures in the history of contemporary music.","致告別演說者向當代音樂史上最具代表性的人物之一致敬。"]],"ideal (adj.)":[["leader-115-17","Tour Leader: How much time should we allow inside the British Museum? Local Guide: About two hours is \u0001ideal\u0002 to see the highlights.","領隊:大英博物館裡面要預留多少時間? 當地導遊:大約兩小時剛好看完精華。"],["leader-113-71","If time is not an issue, direct flights are \u0001ideal\u0002 since they are often less expensive than non-stop flights.","",4]],"identify (v.)":[["leader-114-36","Ground Staff: Can you \u0001identify\u0002 which one resembles your luggage? (Showing a card with various types of luggage.) Amy: Mine looks similar to Type D.","地勤:你能辨認出哪一個像你的行李嗎?(出示各種行李款式的卡片) Amy:我的很像 D 型。"],["guide-111-19","\u0001Identifying\u0002 the problem is the first step to help us make an informed decision.","找出問題是幫助我們做出明智(有根據)決定的第一步。"]],"immigrant (n.)":[["leader-111-53","Many \u0001immigrants\u0002 live in Australia, so ethnic food is very popular here.","許多移民住在澳洲,所以異國(族裔)料理在這很受歡迎。"],["leader-106-70","In Europe, illegal \u0001immigrants\u0002 are used to seek sanctuary in a local church.","在歐洲,非法移民習慣到當地教堂尋求庇護。"]],"impact (n.)":[["leader-110-71","Unfortunately, the environmental \u0001impacts\u0002 of tourism can be devastating when profit takes precedence.","",4],["leader-106-21","Overconsumption is having a serious \u0001impact\u0002 on natural resources.","過度消費正對自然資源造成嚴重衝擊。"]],"impede (v.)":[["guide-110-77","What does the word “\u0001impede\u0002” mean?","impede 這個字是什麼意思?"],["guide-110-76","Mandatory mask-wearing may \u0001impede\u0002 the drive to communicate, and the constant fear of contagion may lead to social isolation.","",1]],"impose (v.)":[["guide-114-55","A no-show fee will be \u0001imposed\u0002 on passengers who do not cancel their reservations 3 hours before the flight's takeoff, or do not board their flights after completion of the check-in process.","對於未在航班起飛前 3 小時取消訂位、或完成報到後未登機的旅客,將課徵失約費。"],["guide-111-10","Customs Duty is a tax \u0001imposed\u0002 on imports and exports of goods in accordance with the Customs Import Tariff.","關稅是依《海關進口稅則》對貨物進出口所課徵的稅。"]],"impressive (adj.)":[["guide-113-32","Taiwan is listed as one of the top 15 hot spring sites, possessing an \u0001impressive\u0002 variety of springs such as warm, cool, mud, and even underwater hot springs.","台灣名列全球前 15 大溫泉勝地,擁有令人印象深刻的多樣泉種,如溫泉、冷泉、泥泉,甚至海底溫泉。"],["guide-109-39","The Trending Taiwan channel on YouTube launched in 2015 presents short films that share \u0001impressive\u0002 scenes of Taiwan.","YouTube 上於 2015 年開設的 Trending Taiwan 頻道,呈現分享台灣動人景象的短片。"]],"include (v.)":[["leader-110-28","Waiter: Yes, it \u0001includes\u0002 French fries and a soup.",""],["guide-109-23","Guest: Is the tip \u0001included\u0002 in the bill? Server: The tip is extra, sir.","客人:帳單有含小費嗎? 服務生:小費另計,先生。"]],"incorporate (v.)":[["leader-107-66","Software developers \u0001incorporate\u0002 AI technology into their products and use it to deal with the complicated job of big-data sorting and analysis.","軟體開發者把 AI 技術整合進產品,用來處理大數據分類與分析這種複雜工作。"]],"inflation (n.)":[["leader-115-71","In other cases, tourism leads to \u0001inflation\u0002 and drives up the cost of living for local residents, particularly in areas where the demand for goods and services rises sharply during peak tourist seasons.","",1],["leader-113-70","With air fares rising faster than \u0001inflation\u0002, global airline bosses now expect $9.8 billion in net income this year, more than double the amount initially forecasted.","由於機票上漲速度快過通膨,全球航空業主管如今預期今年淨利達 98 億美元,是原先預估的兩倍多。"]],"inform (v.)":[["guide-113-21","As your tour guide, I would like to \u0001inform\u0002 you a few things concerning your departure.",""],["guide-110-5","During the COVID-19 pandemic, travelers should remember to share their previous travel history with their health care providers and make every effort to \u0001inform\u0002 them by phone before visiting a medical facility.","疫情期間,旅客應記得與醫療人員分享先前的旅遊史,並在就醫前盡力以電話通知他們。"]],"information (n.)":[["leader-106-11","There is so much \u0001information\u0002 to browse through the Internet that it is easy not to find what you want.","網路上有太多資訊要瀏覽,以致很容易找不到你要的。"],["guide-106-3","The service of PayPal gives people simpler ways to send money without sharing financial \u0001information\u0002.","PayPal 的服務讓人們能以更簡單的方式匯款,而不必分享財務資訊。"]],"innovative (adj.)":[["leader-111-75","more innovative delivery method","更創新的送法",2]],"inquiry (n.)":[["leader-109-19","The receptionist in the Tourist Information Center asks a guest to look through the brochure first and then he will answer his \u0001inquiry\u0002 later.","遊客中心的櫃台請客人先翻閱簡介,之後再回答他的詢問。"]],"interact (v.)":[["guide-108-80","Which kind of technology enables tourism businesses and visitors to use video to \u0001interact\u0002 and provide services through the virtual assistant platform?","哪種科技讓觀光業者與遊客透過虛擬助理平台以影像互動並提供服務?"],["guide-107-12","Most people \u0001interact\u0002 using both verbal and nonverbal communications, so paying attention to facial expressions can help you read a situation.","多數人互動時會運用語言與非語言溝通,所以留意臉部表情能幫你讀懂情況。"]],"interpersonal (adj.)":[["guide-114-10","Good \u0001interpersonal\u0002 skills in guiding include understanding and respecting personal boundaries.","帶團良好的人際技巧,包括理解並尊重個人界線(分際)。"]],"interpreter (n.)":[["guide-114-43","An \u0001interpreter\u0002 is a person who converts a thought or expression of a source language into an expression with a comparable meaning in a target language.","口譯員是把來源語言的想法或表達轉換成目標語言中意義相當之表達的人。"],["guide-107-50","A person whose job is to translate information from one language to another is called an \u0001interpreter\u0002.","工作是把資訊從一種語言翻成另一種語言的人,稱為口譯員。"]],"intervention (n.)":[["leader-107-23","New research suggests our memory can be improved when we give our brain the chance for a complete recharge with no distractions from \u0001interventions\u0002 such as checking emails or surfing the web on a smartphone.","新研究指出,當我們給大腦一個完全充電的機會、不受收信或用智慧型手機上網等干擾時,記憶力能獲改善。"]],"intolerant (adj.)":[["leader-112-11","Gluten \u0001intolerant\u0002 meal does not contain any gluten-based product.","不耐麩質餐點不含任何麩質產品(即無麩質餐)。"]],"invite (v.)":[["leader-107-53","A: I just got \u0001invited\u0002 to my boss's house for dinner!",""],["leader-107-57","A: We should not have \u0001invited\u0002 my wife's boss to the dinner party yesterday.",""]],"invoice (n.)":[["leader-109-40","Front desk clerk: What seems to be the problem with your \u0001invoice\u0002? Hotel Guest: I think I have been overcharged.","櫃台:你的帳單有什麼問題嗎? 飯店客人:我覺得我被多收費了。"]],"island (n.)":[["leader-107-51","The tiny Pacific \u0001island\u0002 of Palmerston is one of the most remote islands in the world. The journey takes nine days from Tahiti, and is long and dangerous.","太平洋上的小島帕默斯頓是世界最偏遠的島嶼之一。從大溪地過去要九天,漫長又危險。"],["guide-106-26","Hawaii, which consists of eight principal \u0001islands\u0002, is a favorite vacation spot.","由八座主要島嶼組成的夏威夷,是熱門的度假勝地。"]],"jade (n.)":[["guide-110-53","One of the most popular pieces of \u0001jade\u0002 carvings in the museum is the Jadeite Cabbage.","博物館裡最受歡迎的玉雕之一是翠玉白菜。"],["leader-109-51","Clerk: Are you looking for some souvenirs? Guest: Yes, I need a \u0001jade\u0002 necklace for my mother.","店員:你在找紀念品嗎? 客人:對,我要幫媽媽買條玉項鍊。"]],"journal (n.)":[["leader-109-71","in a referred journal","在審查期刊",2]],"journey (n.)":[["guide-113-56","Captain: We're thrilled to have you with us today and hope you're as excited as we are for this \u0001journey\u0002 ahead. Our flight time today is estimated to be approximately five hours.","機長:今天很高興有您同行,希望您和我們一樣期待這趟旅程。今天的飛行時間預估約五小時。"],["leader-107-51","The tiny Pacific island of Palmerston is one of the most remote islands in the world. The \u0001journey\u0002 takes nine days from Tahiti, and is long and dangerous.","太平洋上的小島帕默斯頓是世界最偏遠的島嶼之一。從大溪地過去要九天,漫長又危險。"]],"kaleidoscopic (adj.)":[["guide-110-75","With its multicultural characteristics and abundant food sources, Taiwan boasts \u0001kaleidoscopic\u0002 cuisines to live up to its name of a food paradise.","",4]],"lacquer (n.)":[["guide-107-71","Five Swedish designers have worked with artisans in Taiwan to explore different \u0001lacquer\u0002 techniques, and presented their works in an exhibition – “A New Layer.” The exhibition shows contemporary objects made with an ancient technique.","",4]],"launch (v.)":[["leader-114-78","What challenge did \"The World\" face when it was first \u0001launched\u0002?","「The World」剛推出時面臨什麼挑戰?"],["guide-109-39","The Trending Taiwan channel on YouTube \u0001launched\u0002 in 2015 presents short films that share impressive scenes of Taiwan.","YouTube 上於 2015 年開設的 Trending Taiwan 頻道,呈現分享台灣動人景象的短片。"]],"layover (n.)":[["leader-114-50","Tom: Our flight to Barcelona has a long \u0001layover\u0002 in London.",""],["leader-113-71","Did you know there is a difference between a direct, non-stop and a \u0001layover\u0002 flight?","",1]],"leakage (n.)":[["leader-110-72","Which of the following best explains \"… most of the money from tourism may undergo \u0001leakage\u0002\" in the second paragraph?","下列何者最能解釋第二段中「… most of the money from tourism may undergo leakage(觀光財大多外流)」?"],["leader-110-71","…el responsibly as a \"green tourist.\" Being a green tourist starts eating out on trips with a philosophy of \"buy local, eat and drink local.\" Try not to go for the international fast-food chains, because most of the money from tourism may undergo \u0001leakage\u0002.","",1]],"legendary (adj.)":[["guide-109-71","On the walls, you can see paintings of \u0001legendary\u0002 lovers, such as the god Cupid and his lover, Psyche.","",1],["guide-108-18","After taking in the rock formations of the Northeast Coast, it's time to head to the \u0001legendary\u0002 gold mining town of Jinguashi.","欣賞完東北角的岩石地形後,該前往傳奇的金瓜石採金小鎮了。"]],"leisure (n.)":[["leader-113-2","The Forestry and Nature Conservation Agency has been developing forest recreation sites to cater to the citizens' \u0001leisure\u0002 and entertainment needs.","林業及自然保育署一直在開發森林遊憩場所,以滿足民眾休閒娛樂需求。"],["guide-106-74","When the 2016 edition of the popular Travel + \u0001Leisure\u0002 Magazine World's Best Awards came out recently, tour operators were stunned.","",4]],"lemon (n.)":[["guide-112-64","Today's special is steamed fish. You can sprinkle the \u0001lemon\u0002 and salt on the fish.","今日特餐是清蒸魚。你可以把檸檬和鹽灑在魚上。"],["guide-111-3","Buying a second-hand car may save you some money, but make sure you don't buy a(an) \u0001lemon\u0002.","買二手車可能省錢,但要確定你別買到瑕疵品(爛車)。"]],"leverage (v.)":[["guide-114-78","Which of the following is closest in meaning to the word “\u0001leveraging\u0002” in the third paragraph?","下列何者與第三段的 leveraging 意思最接近?"],["guide-114-76","By \u0001leveraging\u0002 AI technologies, hotels and other hospitality establishments can provide personalized recommendations to guests based on their preferences, automate routine tasks through virtual assistants and chatbots, and implement voice recognition syst…","",1]],"limit (n.)":[["leader-110-5","What's the weight \u0001limit\u0002?",""]],"linguistic (adj.)":[["guide-113-48","English became the dominant language in international business, facilitating communication among people from diverse \u0001linguistic\u0002 backgrounds in the global market.","英語成為國際商業的主導語言,促進了全球市場中不同語言背景者之間的溝通。"],["guide-106-17","Taiwanese aborigines are Austronesian peoples, with \u0001linguistic\u0002 and genetic ties to other Austronesian ethnic groups.","台灣原住民屬南島語族,與其他南島民族有語言與基因上的關聯。"]],"lobby (n.)":[["leader-106-43","Homeless are, by definition, people who sleep in streets, parks, shelters, and places that were never intended for living in, such as bus stations, \u0001lobbies\u0002, or empty buildings.","遊民,顧名思義,是睡在街頭、公園、收容所,以及公車站、大廳、空屋等從未打算/設計用來居住之處的人。"]],"lock (v.)":[["leader-112-39","I \u0001locked\u0002 my key in the room, and fortunately, I have a spare set in the office to use.","我把鑰匙鎖在房裡,幸好辦公室有一副備用鑰匙可用。"],["leader-106-17","The cabin doors have been \u0001locked\u0002.",""]],"lodging (n.)":[["guide-115-39","In Taiwan, special rental places such as \"whole-house \u0001lodging\u0002\" can be found. You can rent a whole house just for your party and have access to your own private facilities.","在台灣可找到「整棟出租(包棟民宿)」這類特別的租宿。你可以只為自己的團體租下整棟房子,擁有使用自己專屬設施的權利。"],["leader-108-25","The company provided free \u0001lodging\u0002 for the entire group of guests to stay for two nights.","公司免費提供住宿給整團客人住兩晚。"]],"lounge (n.)":[["guide-114-45","To access the business class \u0001lounges\u0002 in the Taoyuan International Airport, all passengers must have already checked in for their onward flight and be in possession of a valid boarding pass.","要進入桃園國際機場的商務艙貴賓室,所有旅客必須已辦好接續航班的報到,並持有有效的登機證。"]],"magazine (n.)":[["guide-111-80","In which \u0001magazine\u0002 would you most likely find this article?","你最可能在哪本雜誌找到這篇文章?"]],"magnificent (adj.)":[["leader-115-18","The \u0001magnificent\u0002 waterfall is truly the most breathtaking feature of this national park.","那壯麗的瀑布真是這座國家公園最令人屏息的特色。"],["guide-107-1","The traveling office recommended 10 locations to offer people multiple choices to enjoy the \u0001magnificent\u0002 sunsets in a relaxing way.","這個行動辦公室推薦了 10 個地點,讓人們有多種選擇,悠閒地欣賞壯麗的夕陽。"]],"magnitude (n.)":[["leader-115-48","magnitude","規模",2]],"mainly (adv.)":[["leader-112-76","What is the passage \u0001mainly\u0002 about?","本文主要在談什麼?"]],"mainstream (adj.)":[["guide-112-71","Electric air travel (i.e. traveling with an electric-powered aircraft) is going \u0001mainstream\u0002.","",4]],"mall (n.)":[["leader-113-50","A: Do you know where I can buy a plug adaptor around here? B: If you follow the signs to the train station, there is a \u0001mall\u0002 on the way.","A:你知道這附近哪裡能買到轉接插頭嗎? B:沿指標往火車站走,路上有間購物中心。"],["leader-106-78","Much of the infrastructure that supports mass tourism—large tourist hotels, restaurants, \u0001malls\u0002, tour companies—may be owned and operated by companies based outside the tourist areas.","",4]],"Mandarin (n.)":[["leader-106-25","Even though \u0001Mandarin\u0002 may soon become an important world language, it probably won't be the dominant language because the writing system is too difficult.","儘管中文可能很快成為重要的世界語言,但因書寫系統太難,它大概不會成為主導語言。"],["guide-106-42","Though \u0001Mandarin\u0002 Chinese is the official language of Taiwan, many people use Taiwanese in daily life.","雖然國語是台灣的官方語言,但許多人在日常生活使用台語。"]],"mandatory (adj.)":[["leader-110-23","Wearing seat belts is \u0001mandatory\u0002 in all vehicles for drivers globally.","全球所有車輛的駕駛都強制規定要繫安全帶。"],["leader-107-13","A couple grieving over the death of their son in a traffic accident blamed his death on the driver's lack of driver training and launched a public campaign calling for \u0001mandatory\u0002 education for new drivers.","一對痛失兒子(死於車禍)的夫妻,把死因歸咎於駕駛訓練不足,發起公開活動,呼籲對新手駕駛實施強制教育。"]],"masterpiece (n.)":[["leader-115-63","This artist's \u0001masterpieces\u0002 are on exhibition at the museum.","這位藝術家的傑作正在博物館展出。"],["guide-108-20","At Juming Museum, you may see many \u0001masterpieces\u0002 of Taiwanese sculptor Ju Ming.","在朱銘美術館,你能看到許多台灣雕塑家朱銘的傑作。"]],"mention (v.)":[["leader-113-80","Which of the following is \u0001mentioned\u0002 as an illegal activity in a foreign country?","下列何者被提到是某外國的違法行為?"],["leader-111-65","John: Some customers \u0001mentioned\u0002 that the meals are good but they are a bit expensive.",""]],"metro (n.)":[["guide-114-30","Taiwan's \u0001metro\u0002 system has been praised by locals for its effectiveness in relieving growing traffic congestion in Taipei and its surrounding satellite towns.","台灣的捷運系統因有效紓解台北及周邊衛星城鎮日益嚴重的交通壅塞,而受到當地人稱讚。"],["leader-109-65","Steven: Let's take the \u0001metro\u0002 instead.",""]],"mind (v.)":[["guide-113-65","Clerk: Please \u0001mind\u0002 the gap between the train and the platform when leaving the train.","站務員:下車時請留意火車與月台之間的間隙。"],["guide-107-38","Would you \u0001mind\u0002 waiting around here for a few minutes?","你介意在這附近等幾分鐘嗎?"]],"mineral (n.)":[["guide-115-50","Because of the soil's \u0001mineral\u0002 content, the rocks in the waterfall have acquired a golden yellow color over time.","由於土壤的礦物質含量,瀑布中的岩石隨時間染上了金黃色。"],["guide-107-17","The hot springs at Guanziling are located on the side of Zhentou Mountain, and their water is abundant in \u0001minerals\u0002.","關子嶺的溫泉位於枕頭山側,泉水富含礦物質。"]],"minimize (v.)":[["leader-114-56","Practices that \u0001minimize\u0002 environmental impact and support local communities are key principles of sustainable tourism.","減少環境衝擊、支持當地社區的做法,是永續觀光的關鍵原則。"],["leader-110-75","According to the passage, what \"key factor\" \u0001minimizes\u0002 damage?","根據本文,將傷害降至最低的「關鍵因素」是什麼?"]],"mobility (n.)":[["guide-114-48","The evolution of modern tourism owes much to the advancements in transportation as a mode of \u0001mobility\u0002.","現代觀光的演進,很大程度歸功於作為移動方式的交通進步。"],["leader-113-46","After a severe injury, Hanna underwent intensive rehabilitation, working tirelessly to regain her strength, \u0001mobility\u0002, and independence, ultimately recovering well.","嚴重受傷後,Hanna 接受密集復健,不懈努力以恢復力量、行動力和獨立,最終復原良好。"]],"motivation (n.)":[["guide-114-46","Many explorer travelers allude to spiritual or transcendental \u0001motivations\u0002 for seeking out risky and far-away places.","許多探險型旅人把尋找危險、遙遠地點的動機歸諸/提及於精神或超凡的追求。"]],"multiple (adj.)":[["leader-113-28","Any traveler who plans to make \u0001multiple\u0002 stops around Japan is advised to check out the Japan Rail Pass.","打算在日本各地多次停留的旅客,建議查看日本鐵路周遊券(JR Pass)。"],["leader-109-32","The reason why the tour guide was hired was that she could speak \u0001multiple\u0002 languages, including English, Korean, German, and Russian.","這位導遊被錄用的原因,是她會說多種語言,包括英、韓、德、俄語。"]],"nearby (adv.)":[["leader-112-58","Instead of driving a long way for vacation, we had a staycation, visiting the local museums and staying in a hotel \u0001nearby\u0002.","我們沒有開很遠去度假,而是來個宅度假,參觀本地博物館、住附近飯店。"],["guide-109-53","A lady turned to an attendant standing \u0001nearby\u0002 and asked about the painting.","一位女士轉向站在附近的服務員,詢問那幅畫。"]],"nearest (adj.)":[["guide-109-48","A: Hi, do you know where the \u0001nearest\u0002 subway station is? B: Go down this street, turn left, and you should see it on your right.","A:嗨,你知道最近的地鐵站在哪嗎? B:沿這條街走,左轉,就會在你右手邊看到。"],["guide-107-34","A: Do you know where the \u0001nearest\u0002 washroom is? B: It's right around the corner.","A:你知道最近的洗手間在哪嗎? B:就在轉角處。"]],"non-native (adj.)":[["leader-110-12","People often keep \u0001non-native\u0002 animals as pets for fun. However, when pet owners release these animals back into the wild, indigenous animals may be unable to compete.","人們常養外來動物當寵物取樂。但當飼主把牠們野放,原生動物可能競爭不過。"],["guide-106-52","\u0001Non-native\u0002 species may be a disastrous threat to indigenous plants and animals that are native to Taiwan.","外來種可能對台灣原生的動植物構成災難性威脅。"]],"noxious (adj.)":[["leader-106-62","The unusually \u0001noxious\u0002 haze in Beijing was caused by several factors, including industrial pollution and auto emission trapped by cold and windless weather.","北京異常有害的霾,是多重因素造成的,包括工業污染和汽車廢氣被寒冷無風的天氣困住。"],["guide-106-9","These molecules react with sunlight and other compounds to form the \u0001noxious\u0002 vapors, ground level ozone, and particles that comprise smog.","這些分子與陽光及其他化合物反應,形成有毒蒸氣、地面臭氧與微粒,構成煙霧霾害。"]],"nuance (n.)":[["leader-113-78","In the passage, what does the word '\u0001nuances\u0002' most closely mean?","文中 nuances 一字最接近的意思是?"],["leader-113-76","While spontaneous travel seems fun, being aware of the \u0001nuances\u0002 of your destination country can be more practical.","",1]],"offensive (adj.)":[["leader-108-60","What John just said was rude and a bit \u0001offensive\u0002 but I am sure that he did not mean to insult you.","John 剛說的話很無禮、有點冒犯,但我相信他不是有意侮辱你。"]],"offer (n.)":[["leader-115-28","Politely decline and walk away if you feel uncomfortable with a taxi driver's or a vendor's \u0001offer\u0002.","如果你對計程車司機或攤販的開價感到不舒服,就禮貌地婉拒然後走開。"],["leader-111-55","This is my final \u0001offer\u0002.",""]],"onboard (adj.)":[["guide-115-10","Recent news about a fire \u0001onboard\u0002 an airliner has sparked renewed concerns over the safety of power banks during air travel.","近期一起客機機上失火的新聞引發了大家對航程中行動電源安全的重新關注。"],["leader-109-63","Passengers can stay connected with \u0001onboard\u0002 WiFi or enjoy films, music, and other inflight entertainment available during their flight.","乘客可用機上 WiFi 保持連線,或享受電影、音樂和其他機上娛樂。"]],"optimistic (adj.)":[["guide-108-72","The \u0001optimistic\u0002 advantage of Taiwan's development of its international hot springs brand is:","台灣發展國際溫泉品牌的樂觀優勢是:"]],"organized (adj.)":[["guide-110-1","The greatest tour guides are punctual and \u0001organized\u0002, helping their guests get to where they need to be on time.","最優秀的導遊準時又有條理,幫助客人準時抵達該去的地方。"],["leader-107-36","As more and more people were taking time away from studies and careers to travel and work overseas, there was increased demand for \u0001organized\u0002 travel programs.","隨著越來越多人暫離學業和職涯去海外旅遊打工,對套裝旅遊行程的需求增加了。"]],"originate (v.)":[["guide-114-66","Yenshui Fireworks Festival \u0001originated\u0002 in the past when people would ask the gods for help to get rid of the epidemic in Yenshui, and they would set off firecrackers to welcome the arrival of the gods.","鹽水蜂炮節起源於過去,當時鹽水人祈求神明協助驅除瘟疫,並施放鞭炮迎接神明降臨。"]],"over-the-counter (adj.)":[["guide-113-57","The pharmacy is where you can fill your prescriptions and purchase \u0001over-the-counter\u0002 medications and health-related products.","藥局是你可以領處方藥、購買成藥與健康相關產品的地方。"],["leader-112-68","It is \u0001over-the-counter\u0002, no prescription needed.",""]],"overbooking (n.)":[["leader-108-9","Due to the \u0001overbooking\u0002, we will upgrade you to business class.","由於超額訂位,我們將為你升等到商務艙。"],["leader-107-63","Many airlines operate \u0001overbooking\u0002 policies because a small number of passengers, having made their bookings, do not turn up for their flights.","許多航空公司採超額訂位政策,因為少數已訂位的乘客最後沒現身搭機。"]],"overhead (adj.)":[["leader-111-4","Guest: Could you please help me put my carry-on bag into the \u0001overhead\u0002 compartment? Flight attendant: Yes, no problem.","旅客:能幫我把隨身行李放進頭頂置物櫃嗎? 空服員:好的,沒問題。"],["leader-109-23","The \u0001overhead\u0002 compartments here seem to be full; we need to see if there is any space in another one.","這裡的頭頂置物櫃好像滿了,我們得看看另一個有沒有空間。"]],"overstay (v.)":[["leader-115-62","Aliens who \u0001overstay\u0002 their visas would be deported back to their country of birth.","逾期居留簽證的外國人會被遣返回其出生國。"],["leader-111-23","Those who \u0001overstay\u0002 their visa need to fill out an application form, provide a copy of passport, and book a ticket to leave the country in 7 days.","逾期居留者須填申請表、提供護照影本,並訂一張 7 天內離境的機票。"]],"overtourism (n.)":[["guide-109-76","The number of international tourists to France (87 million) is an indication of \u0001Overtourism\u0002.","到法國的國際旅客人數(8,700 萬)顯示了什麼?"],["guide-109-76","As a flood of news headlines highlighting \u0001overtourism\u0002, it's easy to think that the planet is simply full.","",1]],"painting (n.)":[["guide-109-53","A lady turned to an attendant standing nearby and asked about the \u0001painting\u0002.","一位女士轉向站在附近的服務員,詢問那幅畫。"],["leader-108-69","A crowd already filled the art gallery in order to see the famous \u0001paintings\u0002 of Van Gogh.","人群已擠滿藝術展場(畫廊),只為看梵谷的名畫。"]],"paradoxically (adv.)":[["guide-106-78","Which of the following is closest in meaning to the word “\u0001paradoxically\u0002” in the second paragraph?","下列何者與第二段的「paradoxically」意思最接近?"],["guide-106-76","\u0001Paradoxically\u0002, it could cause certain areas to get colder—a lot colder.","",1]],"paramount (adj.)":[["leader-111-77","What does the word \"\u0001paramount\u0002\" in the first paragraph mean?","第一段的 paramount 是什麼意思?"],["leader-111-76","Safety & hygiene tourism trends Whether it is airlines, cruises, hotels, restaurants or bars, since the outbreak of COVID-19, safety and hygiene standards have been absolutely \u0001paramount\u0002.","",1]],"participant (n.)":[["guide-115-49","The Yanshui Fireworks Festival involves shooting tens of thousands of bottle rockets and fireworks not into the sky, but directly into crowds of willing \u0001participants\u0002.","鹽水蜂炮節會發射數以萬計的沖天炮與煙火,不是射向天空,而是直接射向自願參與的人群。"],["guide-108-44","Rockets and fireworks are aimed at the crowds and explode around them. \u0001Participants\u0002 must wear a helmet and protective clothing to prevent injury.","蜂炮朝人群發射並在四周爆炸,參加者必須戴安全帽與防護衣以免受傷。"]],"participate (v.)":[["guide-114-61","Taiwan is known for its myriad festivals and holidays, and \u0001participating\u0002 in them may prove to be some of your most memorable Taiwan experiences.","台灣以其眾多(無數)的節慶和假日聞名,參與其中可能成為你最難忘的台灣體驗之一。"],["leader-108-61","The child should not \u0001participate\u0002 in the experiment without his parents' consent.","未經父母同意,這孩子不應參加這項實驗。"]],"particle (n.)":[["leader-114-15","Scientists found harmful \u0001particles\u0002 in dolphins' breath off Florida, raising concerns for their health and the environment.","科學家在佛州外海海豚的呼吸中發現有害微粒,引發對牠們健康和環境的擔憂。"],["guide-106-9","These molecules react with sunlight and other compounds to form the noxious vapors, ground level ozone, and \u0001particles\u0002 that comprise smog.","這些分子與陽光及其他化合物反應,形成有毒蒸氣、地面臭氧與微粒,構成煙霧霾害。"]],"passionate (adj.)":[["leader-107-6","She is such a lovely, honest, and \u0001passionate\u0002 lady that everyone likes to chat with her.","她是位如此可愛、誠實又熱情的女士,大家都喜歡跟她聊天。"],["guide-107-11","A tour guide needs to be people-friendly, \u0001passionate\u0002 about travel, and able to work in stressful circumstances.","導遊需要親和力強、對旅遊充滿熱情,並能在高壓環境下工作。"]],"patrol (n.)":[["leader-112-79","The team also has a sea turtle \u0001patrol\u0002 at night from 7:00 p.m. to 5:00 a.m., learning about how sea turtles lay their eggs.","",4]],"patron (n.)":[["guide-108-59","To meet customers' expectations and to improve the quality of the meals, a restaurant must obtain feedback from its \u0001patrons\u0002.","為了滿足顧客期望並提升餐點品質,餐廳必須從顧客那裡取得回饋。"],["leader-107-71","On evenings when there is a wait for the table, \u0001patrons\u0002 sometimes pass the time posing and posting.","",1]],"peak (n.)":[["leader-109-45","It is always cheaper to travel at off \u0001peak\u0002 train times that are less busy.","在較不繁忙的離峰火車時段旅行總是比較便宜。"],["guide-108-64","Legend has it that the mark of a footstep on the \u0001peak\u0002 of Wan-an Island is evidence that a fairy once visited this land.","傳說望安島峰頂上的足跡印記,是仙女曾造訪此地的證據。"]],"pebble (n.)":[["guide-115-66","Qixingtan Beach in Hualien is many people's favorite place to visit. It is noted for its unique \u0001pebble\u0002 beach and stunning stars at night.","花蓮七星潭是許多人最愛造訪的地方,以獨特的礫石(鵝卵石)海灘和夜晚璀璨星空著稱。"],["guide-114-22","Qixingtan in Hualien County is known for its unique \u0001pebble\u0002 beach where visitors can create art works with small stones.","花蓮縣的七星潭以獨特的礫石(鵝卵石)海灘聞名,遊客可用小石頭創作藝術品。"]],"penalty (n.)":[["guide-115-12","If you are bringing animals, plants, or their products into the country, to avoid \u0001penalties\u0002, apply for quarantine at customs or the Animal and Plant Health Inspection Agency upon entry.","若攜帶動物、植物或其產品入境,為免受罰,請於入境時在海關或動植物防疫檢疫署申請檢疫。"],["leader-111-47","I hereby certify that I have made a truthful declaration. I understand that if I provide false information, I may be issued with a fixed \u0001penalty\u0002 notice.","我茲此證明我做了真實的申報。我了解若提供不實資訊,可能被開立罰單。"]],"permeate (v.)":[["guide-115-78","In 2014, the price for a medallion surpassed $1 million, but crashed as ride hailing \u0001permeated\u0002 the marketplace.","",4],["guide-113-3","During the tea-picking and making season, the fragrance of tea \u0001permeates\u0002 tea factories in the mountain.","在採茶製茶的季節,茶的香氣瀰漫山中的茶廠。"]],"permission (n.)":[["guide-115-45","Ask for \u0001permission\u0002 before you take close-up photographs of people, and if payment is requested, either pay up or put the camera away.","拍攝人物特寫前先徵求許可;若對方要求付費,要嘛付錢,要嘛把相機收起來。"],["leader-113-39","The sign \"Do Not Enter\" marks the restricted area where only those with \u0001permission\u0002 are allowed entry.","「禁止進入」的標誌標示限制區,只有獲准者才能進入。"]],"permit (n.)":[["guide-113-16","Due to increased demand, the national park started issuing more \u0001permits\u0002 for overnight camping to accommodate more hikers.","由於需求增加,國家公園開始發放更多過夜露營許可證,以容納更多登山客。"],["guide-106-44","Without a \u0001permit\u0002, a group of cyclists made a bold attempt to transgress into the protected area. Nevertheless, they were soon stopped by the wildlife patrol.","一群單車客沒有許可證,大膽企圖擅闖保護區,但很快被野生動物巡邏隊攔下。"]],"perpetual (adj.)":[["leader-114-79","What does the word \"\u0001perpetual\u0002\" (in the second paragraph) mean?","(第二段中)「perpetual」一字的意思是?"],["leader-114-76","Nowadays, the notion of \u0001perpetual\u0002 cruises—where passengers live full-time on cruise ships—has attracted widespread attention of the wealthy.","",1]],"picturesque (adj.)":[["guide-111-76","The Koala Gardens, the Australian Butterfly Sanctuary, and Bird World Kuranda are among the many attractions in this \u0001picturesque\u0002 village.","",1]],"plumage (n.)":[["guide-115-73","What does the word “\u0001plumage\u0002” (in the second paragraph) mean?","第二段的 plumage 是什麼意思?"],["guide-115-71","Meanwhile, the female bird's soft yellow \u0001plumage\u0002 was adopted for the interior, brightening the overall look and moving away from the old red-and-yellow scheme.","",1]],"pocket (n.)":[["guide-111-40","Please empty out your \u0001pocket\u0002. Put your bag, phone and other electronic devices, belt or metal objects on the tray.","請清空你的口袋。把你的包包、手機和其他電子裝置、皮帶或金屬物品放在托盤上。"],["leader-110-57","For Jean, the price is the least important thing when she shops for jeans. She cares even more about the shape and the size of \u0001pockets\u0002.","對 Jean 來說,買牛仔褲時價格是最不重要的。她更在意口袋的形狀和大小。"]],"poisonous (adj.)":[["leader-109-10","Although most snakes in the park are not \u0001poisonous\u0002, you need to watch carefully where you put your hands and feet.","雖然公園裡多數蛇沒毒,你仍需小心留意手腳擺放的位置。"],["leader-106-65","If you are up for a luxury culinary adventure, then try the fugu sashimi, which is made from the flesh of the \u0001poisonous\u0002 puffer fish.","如果你想來場奢華的美食冒險,那就試試河豚生魚片,它由有毒的河豚肉製成。"]],"police (n.)":[["leader-112-32","\u0001Police\u0002: How may I help you? Ann: I want to report a crime.","警察:能為你效勞嗎? Ann:我想報案。"],["leader-106-51","His passport was confiscated by the \u0001police\u0002 to prevent him from leaving the country.","他的護照被警方沒收,以防他離境。"]],"pork (n.)":[["guide-110-40","I am allergic to \u0001pork\u0002. Is there any in this Pepper Bun?","我對豬肉過敏。這個胡椒餅裡有任何(豬肉)嗎?"],["guide-110-65","Taiwanese \u0001Pork\u0002 Sheets are made of pork mixed with almond in the form of a crisp as thin as a piece of paper.","台灣豬肉紙(薄片)是把豬肉與杏仁混合,做成薄如紙的脆片。"]],"portion (n.)":[["leader-115-26","Even though this is an all-you-can-eat restaurant, you should still try to get only the \u0001portion\u0002 of food that you need to prevent unnecessary waste.","即使這是吃到飽餐廳,你仍應只拿你需要的份量,以免不必要的浪費。"],["guide-112-63","If you are not hungry, we can order one meal and share it. The \u0001portions\u0002 are very big.","如果你不餓,我們可以點一份餐一起分。這裡的份量很大。"]],"precaution (n.)":[["guide-114-12","I'd like to take some time to familiarize you with today's schedule and discuss some brief safety \u0001precautions\u0002.","我想花點時間讓你熟悉今天的行程,並說明一些簡短的安全注意事項。"],["leader-106-1","If you plan your trip carefully and learn to take \u0001precautions\u0002, you can relax and enjoy yourself.","如果你仔細規劃行程並學會採取預防措施,就能放鬆好好享受。"]],"predict (v.)":[["leader-113-18","There are fewer guests showing up at the wedding banquet than the Lins originally \u0001predicted\u0002.","出席婚宴的客人比林家原本預估的少。"],["guide-110-14","It is hard to \u0001predict\u0002 the success of space travel since it is an unexplored territory.","太空旅行的成功難以預測,因為它是一個未探索的領域。"]],"prefer (v.)":[["leader-109-33","Some people \u0001prefer\u0002 taking a train than a bus because they think they travel more comfortably by train.","有些人偏好搭火車勝過巴士,因為他們認為搭火車旅行更舒適。"],["guide-109-6","Person A: Is the next seat taken? Person B: I \u0001prefer\u0002 to sit by myself.","A:旁邊的位子有人坐嗎? B:我比較喜歡自己坐。"]],"premium (adj.)":[["guide-112-12","Most \u0001premium\u0002 airlines provide passengers with superior levels of comfort, seats, amenities, and luggage management.","大多數高級航空公司為乘客提供更優越的舒適度、座椅、設施與行李管理。"],["guide-110-27","The \u0001premium\u0002 chocolate is a must-buy souvenir for tourists.","這款高級巧克力是遊客必買的伴手禮。"]],"pressing (adj.)":[["leader-109-77","Which of the following is closest in meaning to \"\u0001pressing\u0002\"?","與 pressing 意思最接近的字是?"],["leader-109-76","Plastic pollution has become one of the most \u0001pressing\u0002 environmental issues, as rapidly increasing production of disposable plastic products overwhelms the world's ability to deal with them.","",1]],"prevent (v.)":[["leader-106-51","His passport was confiscated by the police to \u0001prevent\u0002 him from leaving the country.","他的護照被警方沒收,以防他離境。"]],"prevention (n.)":[["leader-107-5","When it comes to cancer \u0001prevention\u0002, it is well known that we should avoid eating too many sweets and fast foods and spending too much time on the couch.","談到癌症預防,眾所周知我們應避免吃太多甜食、速食,以及久坐沙發。"]],"previously (adv.)":[["leader-114-67","People who haven't \u0001previously\u0002 contracted the virus are advised to get vaccinated at least four weeks before the travel.","先前沒有感染過病毒的人,被建議在旅行前至少四週接種疫苗。"],["guide-108-63","Shilin Official Residence, which is surrounded by a vibrant, ecological garden, was \u0001previously\u0002 the home of the former president, Chiang Kai-Shek.","被生機盎然生態花園環繞的士林官邸,先前是前總統蔣中正的住所。"]],"priceless (adj.)":[["guide-115-62","The National Palace Museum houses the world's largest collection of \u0001priceless\u0002 Chinese art treasures.","故宮博物院收藏著全世界最大的無價中華藝術珍寶典藏。"]],"procedure (n.)":[["leader-111-31","A cellphone parking lot is a parking lot where people wait for their friends to complete their landing \u0001procedures\u0002.","「手機停車場」是人們等候朋友完成降落(入境)手續的停車場。"],["leader-108-15","I would like to claim a tax refund. Do you know the refund application \u0001procedures\u0002?","我想申請退稅,你知道退稅申請流程嗎?"]],"proceed (v.)":[["leader-111-21","Please \u0001proceed\u0002 to the immigration service counter.",""],["leader-110-44","Clerk: This is the final boarding call for John and Mary Smith booked on flight 321C to Salt Lake City. Please \u0001proceed\u0002 to gate 3 immediately.","地勤:這是已訂位飛往鹽湖城 321C 班機的 John 和 Mary Smith 最後登機廣播,請立刻前往 3 號登機門。"]],"product (n.)":[["leader-113-25","All passengers arriving in the US must complete a US Declaration form. Besides, passengers carrying fruits, vegetables, plants, seeds or other agricultural \u0001products\u0002 are required to declare those items.","所有入境美國的旅客都須填寫美國申報單。此外,攜帶水果、蔬菜、植物、種子或其他農產品的旅客,須申報這些物品。"],["guide-111-52","Would you be willing to help Karen find information about our new \u0001product\u0002 in this catalog?","你願意幫 Karen 在這本型錄中找我們新產品的資訊嗎?"]],"profitable (adj.)":[["leader-107-56","In order to run a \u0001profitable\u0002 restaurant, you need to get a talented chef.","要經營一家賺錢的餐廳,你需要請一位有才華的主廚。"],["leader-106-47","While both a social business and a business run by an entrepreneur need to be \u0001profitable\u0002, the bottom line for a social business is how much impact it makes on society.","社會企業和創業者經營的企業都需要獲利,但社會企業的底線是它對社會造成多少影響。"]],"proximity (n.)":[["guide-113-69","Many cities in Japan are quite popular vacation destinations because of their \u0001proximity\u0002 to Taiwan.","日本許多城市是相當受歡迎的度假地,因為它們鄰近台灣。"],["guide-111-31","Okinawa is quite a popular vacation destination because of its \u0001proximity\u0002 to Taiwan.","沖繩是相當受歡迎的度假地,因為它鄰近台灣。"]],"puppet (n.)":[["guide-114-34","A palm \u0001puppet\u0002 museum has been established in Yunlin County, which is the “hometown of glove puppetry.” In the museum, you can admire beautifully crafted palm puppets, costumes, and headgear.","雲林縣設立了一座布袋戲(掌中戲)博物館,雲林是「手套(布袋)戲之鄉」。館內可欣賞做工精美的布袋戲偶、戲服與頭飾。"],["guide-112-28","Taiwan's \u0001puppet\u0002 shows have reached a new level of creativity and artistic excellence through the hard work of the Huang family in Yuenlin.","透過雲林黃家的努力,台灣的布袋戲表演已達到創意與藝術卓越的新境界。"]],"quantity (n.)":[["guide-110-8","A report indicates that Taiwanese people consume almost 7.9 kilograms of apples per person every year, comparable to the \u0001quantity\u0002 of bananas a Taiwanese has a year.","一份報告指出,台灣人每人每年食用將近 7.9 公斤蘋果,和台灣人一年吃的香蕉量相當。"]],"rainfall (n.)":[["leader-111-41","Drought happens when there is not enough water and \u0001rainfall\u0002.","當水和雨量不足時,就會發生乾旱。"],["leader-109-18","The city is suffering from a(n) severe lack of \u0001rainfall\u0002 at the moment.","這座城市目前正遭受嚴重缺雨之苦。"]],"rainforest (n.)":[["leader-113-65","Before you undertake a journey through the Amazon \u0001rainforest\u0002, it's essential to be well-prepared and informed.","在你展開穿越亞馬遜雨林的旅程前,充分準備和了解資訊至關重要。"],["guide-113-15","The conservation of jungles and \u0001rainforests\u0002 is critical to the survival of many species.","叢林與雨林的保育對許多物種的生存至關重要。"]],"rare (adj.)":[["guide-113-4","\u0001Rare\u0002, medium or well done?",""],["guide-108-21","Taiping Mountain is home to a \u0001rare\u0002 virgin forest and a rich animal and plant ecology.","太平山擁有罕見的原始森林與豐富的動植物生態。"]],"reasonable (adj.)":[["leader-112-22","Tipping is prevalent across most of North America, with 15%-20% being seen as a \u0001reasonable\u0002 amount.","給小費在北美大部分地區很普遍,15%–20% 被視為合理金額。"],["guide-111-53","I didn't think the price was too high at all; in fact, it seemed quite \u0001reasonable\u0002.","我完全不覺得價格太高;事實上,它似乎相當合理。"]],"rebuild (v.)":[["guide-107-63","This historical site was largely \u0001rebuilt\u0002 between the years of 1990 and 1995.","這處古蹟大部分是在 1990 到 1995 年之間重建的。"]],"regarding (prep.)":[["leader-113-77","According to the passage, what is a common mistake travelers make \u0001regarding\u0002 their passports?","根據本文,旅客對護照常犯的錯誤是什麼?"],["guide-112-10","Should you have any questions \u0001regarding\u0002 the loss of your wallet and passport abroad, feel free to contact us anytime during office hours.","若你在國外有任何關於錢包和護照遺失的問題,歡迎在辦公時間隨時與我們聯繫。"]],"reissue (v.)":[["leader-112-70","A: What can I do if I lose my passport during the trip? B: You have to go to the embassy to have a new one \u0001reissued\u0002.","A:旅途中護照弄丟了怎麼辦? B:你得去大使館補發一本新的。"],["leader-110-18","They can help us \u0001reissue\u0002 your passport.",""]],"relationship (n.)":[["leader-114-16","In a steady \u0001relationship\u0002, the partners are likely to stay together for long.","在穩定的關係中,伴侶較可能長久在一起。"]],"relax (v.)":[["leader-109-62","We need to \u0001relax\u0002 after our busy morning. Why don't we have a coffee break at a quarter to eleven?","忙了一早該放鬆了。我們何不在差一刻到 11 點(10:45)喝杯咖啡休息?"],["leader-106-1","If you plan your trip carefully and learn to take precautions, you can \u0001relax\u0002 and enjoy yourself.","如果你仔細規劃行程並學會採取預防措施,就能放鬆好好享受。"]],"relieve (v.)":[["leader-109-3","Do you have anything to \u0001relieve\u0002 the pain of a sore throat?","你有什麼能緩解喉嚨痛的嗎?"],["guide-106-11","Strolling in the lush woods with the murmuring brooks and bathing in the warm breeze can \u0001relieve\u0002 your anxiety and pressure.","在潺潺溪水的蓊鬱林間漫步、沐浴在暖風中,能減輕你的焦慮與壓力。"]],"remnant (n.)":[["guide-114-17","The people who previously inhabited Taiwan also left many cultural \u0001remnants\u0002 that can still be found around the island today, including traditional architecture, relics of prehistoric civilizations, folk art, and traditions.","過去居住在台灣的人們,也留下許多文化遺跡,至今仍能在島上各處看到,包括傳統建築、史前文明遺址、民間藝術與傳統。"],["leader-107-28","Gansu's diverse landscapes include the Gobi Desert, the Yellow River, numerous mountain formations, and \u0001remnants\u0002 of the Silk Road and the Great Wall.","甘肅多樣的地貌包括戈壁沙漠、黃河、眾多山脈,以及絲路和長城的遺跡。"]],"remote (adj.)":[["guide-108-76","These technologies can provide \u0001remote\u0002 support to enhance visitors' travel experience.","",1],["leader-107-51","The tiny Pacific island of Palmerston is one of the most \u0001remote\u0002 islands in the world. The journey takes nine days from Tahiti, and is long and dangerous.","太平洋上的小島帕默斯頓是世界最偏遠的島嶼之一。從大溪地過去要九天,漫長又危險。"]],"Renaissance (n.)":[["leader-115-68","The architecture of this building is typical of the \u0001Renaissance\u0002 age, and many tourists enjoy visiting this place.","這棟建築的建築(風格)是文藝復興時期的典型,許多遊客喜歡來參觀。"],["guide-114-32","The architecture of the Old Taichung Train Station is a mix of traditional Japanese and late \u0001Renaissance\u0002 themes. It is now listed as a national monument.","台中舊火車站的建築融合了傳統日式與晚期文藝復興的風格。它現在被列為國定古蹟。"]],"renew (v.)":[["leader-113-77","A passport validity of 10 years can make people complacent, forgetting that it actually requires \u0001renewing\u0002.","",4],["guide-112-36","A: Have you had any issues \u0001renewing\u0002 your visa? B: Not yet.","A:你續簽簽證有遇到什麼問題嗎? B:還沒有。"]],"renovate (v.)":[["leader-108-51","The couple spent thousands \u0001renovating\u0002 the old house and got it back into good condition.","這對夫妻花了數千元翻修舊房子,讓它恢復良好狀態。"]],"renovation (n.)":[["leader-115-22","Seriously impacted by a storm last year, this tourist site was under a major \u0001renovation\u0002 for eight months.","去年遭風暴嚴重侵襲後,這個觀光景點進行了為期八個月的大規模整修。"],["leader-110-76","The \u0001renovation\u0002 project of the Louvre signifies the possibility of harmony between modernity and history.","",1]],"replace (v.)":[["leader-108-45","Most appliances come with a free one-year warranty. The goods can be repaired or \u0001replaced\u0002 under certain conditions.","多數家電附一年免費保固。在特定條件下商品可維修或更換。"]],"replacement (n.)":[["leader-111-33","Tourist: I've lost my key and I need to get into my room. Can I get a \u0001replacement\u0002?","遊客:我把鑰匙弄丟了,得進房間。我能拿一把備用(替換)鑰匙嗎?"],["leader-109-67","If the customer is not satisfied with the item for any reason, the shop will offer a \u0001replacement\u0002.","若顧客因任何原因對商品不滿意,商店會提供替換品。"]],"replenish (v.)":[["leader-108-72","What does the word \"\u0001replenishes\u0002\" in the first paragraph mean?","第一段的 replenishes 是什麼意思?"],["leader-108-71","As a result, the imbalance between what nature \u0001replenishes\u0002 and humans consume will probably continue to grow.","",1]],"repository (n.)":[["leader-110-77","What does the word \"\u0001repository\u0002\" mean?","repository 一字是什麼意思?"],["leader-110-76","The decision to turn the Louvre into a massive \u0001repository\u0002 of the world's greatest fine art collection was proposed in 1981 by the French President François Mitterrand.","",1]],"representative (n.)":[["leader-111-48","Airline \u0001representative\u0002: Please fill out this form.",""],["guide-108-39","Taiwan hosts many modern cultural festivals. The Taiwan International Festival of the Art and Spring Scream is one of the \u0001representatives\u0002.","台灣舉辦許多現代文化節慶,台灣國際藝術節與春吶就是其中的代表。"]],"requirement (n.)":[["guide-112-16","Simply give our customer service a call, and we will gladly customize your trips to match any particular \u0001requirements\u0002 or interests you may have.","只要打電話給我們的客服,我們很樂意客製化你的行程,以符合你任何特定的需求或興趣。"],["leader-109-27","Each country has varying processes and \u0001requirements\u0002 for customs and rules about declaration of items.","每個國家對海關的程序、規定與物品申報要求各不相同。"]],"rewarding (adj.)":[["leader-110-3","Tom: Do not go into it for money. The most \u0001rewarding\u0002 aspect of my job is that I go to different places and talk about my own travel experiences.","Tom:別為錢入這行。我工作最有成就感的部分,是能到不同地方、分享自己的旅遊經驗。"],["guide-109-79","How \u0001rewarding\u0002 it can be to leave the popular sites behind.","",4]],"riverside (n.)":[["guide-115-13","Love River is a symbol of Kaohsiung City in southern Taiwan, with \u0001riverside\u0002 illuminations creating a twinkling night-time atmosphere, offering a romantic experience for visitors.","愛河是南台灣高雄市的象徵,河畔的燈飾營造出閃爍的夜間氛圍,為遊客帶來浪漫體驗。"],["leader-112-54","It is relaxing to sit in this café and hang out with my friends a bit. We can enjoy the \u0001riverside\u0002 view and have a chat.","坐在這咖啡館和朋友閒晃一下很放鬆。可以欣賞河景、聊聊天。"]],"romance (n.)":[["guide-107-78","There's a sense of \u0001romance\u0002 about a train that simply doesn't exist on a modern jet plane.","",4]],"rude (adj.)":[["leader-108-60","What John just said was \u0001rude\u0002 and a bit offensive but I am sure that he did not mean to insult you.","John 剛說的話很無禮、有點冒犯,但我相信他不是有意侮辱你。"],["guide-108-49","Although giving gifts is quite popular in Taiwan, it is \u0001rude\u0002 to bring inappropriate gifts such as a clock, umbrella, shoes, and so on.","雖然送禮在台灣很普遍,但送不合適的禮物,例如時鐘、雨傘、鞋子等,是不禮貌的。"]],"ruins (n.)":[["leader-113-44","During our exciting excursion, we explored ancient \u0001ruins\u0002, savored exotic cuisine, and connected with locals, making our travel unforgettable.","在這趟刺激的短程旅遊中,我們探索古蹟、品嚐異國料理、與當地人交流,讓旅程難忘。"],["guide-111-76","One of the world's highest railway trips takes you to Machu Picchu, the \u0001ruins\u0002 of an ancient city located in the Andes Mountains of South America.","",1]],"run (v.)":[["guide-109-3","Visitor: How often does the bus \u0001run\u0002 from here to the airport? Receptionist: Every 20 minutes.","旅客:這裡到機場的公車多久一班? 櫃台:每 20 分鐘一班。"],["leader-107-56","In order to \u0001run\u0002 a profitable restaurant, you need to get a talented chef.","要經營一家賺錢的餐廳,你需要請一位有才華的主廚。"]],"satisfied (adj.)":[["guide-112-46","If you are not completely \u0001satisfied\u0002 with our product, you can return it for a full refund.","如果你對我們的產品不完全滿意,可以退貨並獲得全額退款。"],["leader-109-67","If the customer is not \u0001satisfied\u0002 with the item for any reason, the shop will offer a replacement.","若顧客因任何原因對商品不滿意,商店會提供替換品。"]],"sauna (n.)":[["guide-113-23","Front Desk Clerk: Go pass the \u0001sauna\u0002 and turn right.",""],["guide-108-56","A resort hotel is a venue where travelers can relax. Accordingly, they emphasize recreational amenities such as \u0001saunas\u0002, swimming pools, etc.","度假飯店是讓旅客放鬆的場所,因此它們強調三溫暖、游泳池等休閒設施。"]],"save (v.)":[["leader-110-55","It's great that we can buy flight tickets via both phone and internet without calling the travel agents. It \u0001saves\u0002 us a lot of time.","我們能透過電話和網路買機票,不用打給旅行社,真好。這省了我們很多時間。"],["guide-107-46","If all of us travel to Penghu by ferry as opposed to flying, we could \u0001save\u0002 up to 10,000 dollars.","如果我們全都搭渡輪去澎湖而非搭飛機,可省下多達一萬元。"]],"savory (adj.)":[["guide-113-44","The restaurant's appetizers, including crispy calamari, stuffed mushrooms, and \u0001savory\u0002 sliders, left us eagerly anticipating the main course.","這家餐廳的開胃菜,包括酥炸花枝、鑲蘑菇和美味小漢堡,讓我們熱切期待主餐。"],["leader-110-14","Fresh herbs such as chives and parsley are essential ingredients in the sauces that accompany most French \u0001savory\u0002 dishes.","細香蔥、巴西里等新鮮香草是醬汁的必要食材,這些醬汁搭配多數法式鹹食。"]],"scene (n.)":[["leader-107-1","I enjoyed my vacation in San Francisco. I was most impressed by the beautiful \u0001scenes\u0002 along the Pacific Coast Highway.","我很享受在舊金山的假期。太平洋海岸公路沿途的美景讓我印象最深刻。"]],"scenic (adj.)":[["leader-115-50","A local travel agency hung several \u0001scenic\u0002 posters in the company window to attract pedestrians to come inside and purchase their historical tour.","當地旅行社在櫥窗掛了幾張風景海報,以吸引行人進來購買他們的歷史導覽行程。"],["guide-115-70","The riverside bikeways are beautifully \u0001scenic\u0002, and on holidays they bustle with cyclists of all ages.","河濱自行車道風景優美,假日時擠滿(熱鬧)了各年齡層的自行車騎士。"]],"sculpture (n.)":[["guide-113-74","… hall was built with bronze dragons on right and left pillars symbolizing protections to the hall, and decorations of delicate \u0001sculptures\u0002, detailed wood carvings and gorgeous buddha statues settle in the main chamber with an explosion of brilliant color.","",4],["guide-112-20","The Duomo di Milano in Italy has over 3,400 \u0001sculptures\u0002, making it the place with the most statues in the world.","義大利的米蘭大教堂有超過 3,400 座雕塑,使它成為全世界擁有最多雕像的地方。"]],"seated (adj.)":[["leader-112-4","Please remain \u0001seated\u0002 until the \"fasten seat belt\" sign is switched off and the aircraft has come to a complete stop.","請保持坐著,直到「繫安全帶」燈號熄滅且飛機完全停妥。"],["guide-109-60","Please fasten your seatbelt and remain \u0001seated\u0002.","請繫好安全帶並保持坐著。"]],"sector (n.)":[["leader-115-72","This influx of capital also creates many job opportunities, not only in tourism-related industries like hotels, restaurants, and travel agencies but also in other \u0001sectors\u0002 that support tourism, such as construction and retail business.","",4],["leader-115-76","While progress towards decarbonisation has been made, this research highlights the diversity within the \u0001sector\u0002, differences in context as well as variety in commitments across industries and companies in Travel & Tourism.","",4]],"secure (v.)":[["leader-111-51","You pay a deposit in advance to \u0001secure\u0002 the reservation.",""],["leader-110-45","Captain: We are going to take off. Please fasten your seatbelt at this time and \u0001secure\u0002 all baggage underneath your seat or in the overhead compartment.","機長:我們即將起飛。請此時繫好安全帶,並將所有行李固定放妥於座椅下方或頭頂置物櫃。"]],"security (n.)":[["guide-113-34","Airport \u0001security\u0002 rules state that passengers can only bring liquid items no larger than 100ml in their hand luggage.","機場安檢規定,旅客手提行李中只能攜帶不超過 100 毫升的液體物品。"],["guide-109-46","In addition to your passport, you need a boarding pass that lets you pass through \u0001security\u0002 and into the airport.","除了護照,你還需要一張登機證才能通過安檢進入機場。"]],"seize (v.)":[["guide-113-18","Customs and Border Protection officers \u0001seized\u0002 three shipments containing various luxury items, which were deemed to be counterfeits.","海關與邊境保護官員查扣了三批含各種奢侈品的貨物,這些貨物被認定為仿冒品。"],["guide-108-79","What kind of tool do people in the tourism industry use to analyze travelers' behavior patterns, change the way they interact with tourists, and \u0001seize\u0002 future business opportunities?","觀光業者用哪種工具分析旅客行為模式、改變互動方式並掌握未來商機?"]],"sensitive (adj.)":[["guide-108-8","Smoke detector is an electronic fire alarm that is \u0001sensitive\u0002 to smoke.","煙霧偵測器是一種對煙敏感的電子火災警報器。"],["guide-107-8","Tour guides will meet guests from all over the globe and all walks of life, so the best guides need to be \u0001sensitive\u0002 to cultural differences.","導遊會遇到來自世界各地、各行各業的客人,所以最好的導遊要對文化差異敏感。"]],"separate (v.)":[["guide-108-28","Taiwan, also known as Formosa, and mainland China are \u0001separated\u0002 by the Taiwan Strait.","台灣(又稱福爾摩沙)與中國大陸被台灣海峽分隔。"],["leader-106-33","Hong Kong consists of two parts: Hong Kong Island and Kowloon, \u0001separated\u0002 by Victoria Harbor.","香港由兩部分組成:香港島和九龍,以維多利亞港相隔。"]],"serene (adj.)":[["leader-112-24","The water in Sun Moon Lake is green and clear, reflecting the images of surrounding mountains and \u0001serene\u0002 landscape.","日月潭湖水碧綠清澈,倒映著周圍群山與寧靜的景致。"]],"service (n.)":[["guide-111-64","When Lisa complained about the slow \u0001service\u0002, the manager apologized.","當 Lisa 抱怨服務太慢時,經理道了歉。"],["guide-106-50","To use the \u0001services\u0002 provided on our website, you have to register an account first.","要使用本網站提供的服務,你必須先註冊一個帳號。"]],"serving (n.)":[["guide-113-54","Is it possible to order an extra \u0001serving\u0002 for him?",""],["guide-111-44","Would you like another \u0001serving\u0002 of bread?","你想再來一份麵包嗎?"]],"severe (adj.)":[["leader-109-18","The city is suffering from a(n) \u0001severe\u0002 lack of rainfall at the moment.","這座城市目前正遭受嚴重缺雨之苦。"],["leader-108-40","Passengers were asked not to leave their seats when the plane was flying through \u0001severe\u0002 turbulence.","飛機穿越劇烈亂流時,乘客被要求不要離開座位。"]],"shade (n.)":[["guide-115-35","The buildings are built very close to each other to provide \u0001shade\u0002 for pedestrians walking in the city.","建築物彼此蓋得很近,為在城市中行走的行人提供遮蔭。"],["guide-106-19","New 3D movie theatre technology has put older 3D movie technology in the \u0001shade\u0002.","新的 3D 電影院技術讓舊的 3D 技術相形失色。"]],"short-haul (adj.)":[["guide-112-74","Austria and France have enacted bans on \u0001short-haul\u0002 domestic flights.","",4]],"sightseeing (n.)":[["leader-110-7","Yosemite National Park, Yellowstone National Park, and Central Park all are on the top \u0001sightseeing\u0002 spots in USA.","優勝美地、黃石和中央公園都是美國頂級觀光景點。"],["leader-108-7","Are there any \u0001sightseeing\u0002 tours for the memorial hall?","有沒有紀念館的觀光導覽行程?"]],"sign (n.)":[["leader-112-20","We missed the warning \u0001signs\u0002 and that's why the car accident happened.","我們錯過了警告標誌,所以才發生車禍。"],["guide-111-12","You can get to Baggage Claim by going down the escalator and following the \u0001signs\u0002.","你可以下手扶梯後照著標示走到行李提領處。"]],"similarity (n.)":[["guide-108-74","There are many \u0001similarities\u0002 between Taiwan and Japan, such as culture and resources.","",4]],"size (n.)":[["guide-109-49","B: What \u0001size\u0002 do you wear?",""],["guide-108-68","I love the roll-neck sweater in blue, but I don't know what my \u0001size\u0002 is. Could you please take my measurements?","我很喜歡這件藍色高領毛衣,但不知道我的尺寸,能幫我量尺寸嗎?"]],"spark (v.)":[["guide-115-10","Recent news about a fire onboard an airliner has \u0001sparked\u0002 renewed concerns over the safety of power banks during air travel.","近期一起客機機上失火的新聞引發了大家對航程中行動電源安全的重新關注。"],["guide-109-70","Caoling's new “flying mountain” and barrier lake attracted the attention of the public, \u0001sparking\u0002 a new wave of tourism.","草嶺新形成的「飛山」與堰塞湖吸引了大眾目光,掀起一波新的觀光熱潮。"]],"spot (n.)":[["leader-110-7","Yosemite National Park, Yellowstone National Park, and Central Park all are on the top sightseeing \u0001spots\u0002 in USA.","優勝美地、黃石和中央公園都是美國頂級觀光景點。"],["guide-106-72","A little known company that had never appeared in the rankings before took the coveted Number One \u0001spot\u0002 as the World's Best Tour Operator.","",4]],"spread (n.)":[["guide-110-16","It takes the joint efforts of both the government and the general public to halt the \u0001spread\u0002 of the virus.","需要政府與大眾共同努力才能遏止病毒的傳播。"],["leader-106-41","Traveling from one city or country to another can contribute to the \u0001spread\u0002 of disease.","從一個城市或國家到另一處旅行,可能助長疾病傳播。"]],"stage (n.)":[["guide-111-18","It is hard to come to any conclusion given the rudimentary knowledge we have at this \u0001stage\u0002.","以我們現階段粗淺(基本)的知識,很難下任何結論。"],["guide-106-53","Refrain from talking when someone is giving a lecture on a \u0001stage\u0002.","當有人在台上演講時,請克制不要交談。"]],"staple (n.)":[["guide-115-16","Rice is a \u0001staple\u0002 that appears on most Taiwanese tables.","米飯是大多數台灣餐桌上都會出現的主食。"],["guide-112-18","You can't call a trip to Tainan complete without tasting the city's two breakfast \u0001staples\u0002: milkfish congee and beef soup.","沒嚐過台南兩樣早餐招牌(主食)——虱目魚粥和牛肉湯,就不算完整地遊過台南。"]],"steal (v.)":[["leader-107-24","As flying becomes increasingly time-consuming and less attractive, a new London-to-Amsterdam rail route could \u0001steal\u0002 passengers from the skies.","隨著搭飛機越來越費時、吸引力下降,一條新的倫敦到阿姆斯特丹鐵路線可能搶走空中的乘客。"],["guide-106-40","Lucy began to panic and cry as she realized that her passport and money might have been \u0001stolen\u0002.","露西發現護照和錢可能被偷了,開始驚慌大哭。"]],"stranger (n.)":[["leader-113-8","A group of travelers were stranded in a blizzard; fortunately, they were accepted into a \u0001stranger\u0002's home for two nights.","一群旅客受困暴風雪中;幸好被一位陌生人收留兩晚。"],["guide-108-48","Beware of \u0001strangers\u0002 at the airport and do not leave your personal items unattended.","在機場要提防陌生人,別讓私人物品無人看管。"]],"strap (n.)":[["leader-113-16","Then, pull the \u0001strap\u0002 to adjust it.",""],["leader-109-4","Clerk: Could you describe to me what your bag looks like? Traveler: It's a black duffle bag with a yellow \u0001strap\u0002.","人員:能描述一下你的包長什麼樣子嗎? 旅客:是個黑色行李袋配黃色背帶。"]],"strictly (adv.)":[["guide-109-15","Inside the museum, flash photography is \u0001strictly\u0002 prohibited.","在博物館內,嚴格禁止使用閃光燈拍照。"]],"strive (v.)":[["guide-113-29","If you're traveling to the airport, the shuttle bus will only stop up to two more times after your pickup. By reducing the number of stops, we \u0001strive\u0002 to provide a safer, more efficient, and more pleasant transportation experience.","如果你要去機場,接駁車在載你之後最多只再停兩站。透過減少停靠次數,我們努力提供更安全、更有效率、更愉快的交通體驗。"]],"stroll (v.)":[["guide-106-11","\u0001Strolling\u0002 in the lush woods with the murmuring brooks and bathing in the warm breeze can relieve your anxiety and pressure.","在潺潺溪水的蓊鬱林間漫步、沐浴在暖風中,能減輕你的焦慮與壓力。"],["guide-106-61","While he was \u0001strolling\u0002 on a beach in Kenting, he casually took a picture of a couple kissing against the backdrop of the setting sun.","他在墾丁海灘漫步時,隨手拍下一對情侶以夕陽為背景接吻的照片。"]],"structure (n.)":[["guide-114-7","In Japan, the society is known as a(n) hierarchical \u0001structure\u0002, with respect for seniority.","在日本,社會以階級(層級)結構聞名,講究對長幼/資歷的尊重。"]],"stuck (adj.)":[["leader-107-20","It was a rough night for travelers at Miami International Airport. Thousands of inbound passengers were \u0001stuck\u0002 behind customs screening stations for hours due to a computer failure.","對邁阿密國際機場的旅客來說,那是難熬的一夜。數千名入境旅客因電腦故障,被卡在海關查驗站後方好幾小時。"],["leader-107-39","I can't open the window in my room. It seems to be \u0001stuck\u0002.","我房間的窗戶打不開,好像卡住了。"]],"subdued (adj.)":[["guide-115-72","Which of the following is closest in meaning to the word “\u0001subdued\u0002” (in the second paragraph)?","下列何者與第二段的 subdued 意思最接近?"],["guide-115-71","The male bird, with its deep blue feathers and scarf-like orange markings, inspired the exterior design, bringing vitality to the otherwise \u0001subdued\u0002 color palette.","",1]],"substitute (n.)":[["leader-108-57","If you try to lose weight, reduced-calorie cheese is a great \u0001substitute\u0002 for cream cheese.","若你想減重,低卡起司是奶油起司很好的替代品。"],["leader-107-67","All businesses face competition. Your business competitor could offer a \u0001substitute\u0002 or similar product that makes your own redundant.","所有企業都面臨競爭。你的競爭對手可能推出替代或類似產品,讓你的產品變得多餘(被取代)。"]],"subtle (adj.)":[["guide-113-33","Experienced wine tasters can detect \u0001subtle\u0002 flavors and aromas that a casual drinker might miss.","經驗豐富的品酒師能察覺一般飲者可能忽略的細微風味與香氣。"]],"suitcase (n.)":[["guide-109-62","A: My \u0001suitcase\u0002 didn't appear on the carousel. B: Do you have your claim ticket?","A:我的行李箱沒出現在行李轉盤上。 B:你有行李領取單嗎?"],["leader-108-4","Please put your \u0001suitcase\u0002 on the scale. Oh, it is overweight.","請把行李箱放上磅秤。喔,它超重了。"]],"supply (n.)":[["guide-111-70","Taiwan is famous for its rich fruit \u0001supply\u0002.","台灣以豐富的水果供應聞名。"],["guide-110-50","According to a newspaper report, blood \u0001supplies\u0002 are running low across Taiwan, with blood banks reporting an average of less than five days of stock.","根據報導,全台血液供應吃緊,血庫平均庫存不到五天。"]],"sustainability (n.)":[["leader-114-31","The SDGs Asia Expo highlights Taiwan's firm commitment to transforming \u0001sustainability\u0002 from a concept into tangible action.","SDGs 亞洲博覽會凸顯台灣把永續從概念轉化為具體行動的堅定承諾。"],["leader-108-71","The key is \u0001sustainability\u0002—finding new and efficient ways of conserving more and consuming less—so that we do not ultimately exhaust our most valuable resources.","",1]],"swipe (v.)":[["leader-115-42","Passengers simply add value to a smart card and \u0001swipe\u0002 it at the gate to enter. The fare is automatically deducted.","乘客只要為智慧卡加值,在閘門刷卡進入,車資就會自動扣除。"],["guide-107-62","If you want to pay with a credit card, you can directly \u0001swipe\u0002 the card on the device.","如果你想用信用卡付款,可以直接在機器上刷卡。"]],"switch (v.)":[["leader-113-61","All mobile phones must be \u0001switched\u0002 to flight mode before takeoff and landing.","所有手機在起飛和降落前必須切換到飛航模式。"],["leader-110-24","B: You can take the green line to Harrington stop and \u0001switch\u0002 to the orange line.",""]],"take (v.)":[["guide-111-62","\u0001Take\u0002 a map with you in case you get lost.","帶張地圖在身上,以防迷路。"],["leader-110-47","Traveler: May I pay by new Taiwan dollar here? Clerk: Sorry, we only \u0001take\u0002 US dollar.","旅客:我能用新台幣付款嗎? 店員:抱歉,我們只收美金。"]],"take-off (n.)":[["leader-111-27","Guest: How much longer do we need to wait in line before the \u0001take-off\u0002? Flight attendant: It depends on how many planes are ahead of us.","客人:起飛前我們還要排隊等多久? 空服員:看我們前面有幾架飛機而定。"],["leader-108-10","Captain: Laptop computers and other electronic devices cannot be used until 15 minutes after \u0001take-off\u0002, or after the seat belt sign has been turned on prior to landing.","機長:筆電和其他電子裝置,須在起飛 15 分鐘後、或降落前安全帶燈亮起後才不能使用。"]],"takeaway (n.)":[["leader-111-71","Therefore, your \u0001takeaway\u0002 might not come with a knock at the door, but with a drone hovering outside your window.","",1],["leader-110-32","I would like a seafood fried rice. Please make it to \u0001takeaway\u0002.","我要一份海鮮炒飯,請做成外帶。"]],"temperature (n.)":[["guide-110-15","The \u0001temperature\u0002 has dipped so low that the mountain is blanketed with snow.","氣溫驟降到很低,以致山上覆滿了雪。"],["leader-108-32","Body \u0001temperatures\u0002 can fluctuate and become unstable when you are ill.","生病時體溫會起伏波動,變得不穩定。"]],"temporary (adj.)":[["leader-111-58","If a traveler loses his or her passport, he or she needs to find his or her country's embassy to apply for a \u0001temporary\u0002 passport.","若旅客遺失護照,須找到自己國家的大使館申請臨時護照。"],["leader-108-53","The drug will give you \u0001temporary\u0002 relief from the pain. However, you need to see a doctor if the pain persists.","這藥會給你暫時止痛。但若疼痛持續,你得看醫生。"]],"temptation (n.)":[["leader-110-20","Compulsive shopping is a kind of mental health disorder in which an individual cannot resist the \u0001temptation\u0002 to buy something, even if one does not need it.","強迫性購物是一種心理疾病,患者無法抗拒購買的誘惑,即使不需要。"],["guide-110-42","Planning how to spend next month's income will help you to save money and avoid the \u0001temptation\u0002 to make an impulse purchase.","規劃下個月收入怎麼花,能幫你省錢並避免衝動購物的誘惑。"]],"terrain (n.)":[["guide-110-75","With its special \u0001terrain\u0002, Taiwan is home to many breathtaking mountains, hills, and valleys.","",4]],"theft (n.)":[["leader-112-69","A: I would like to report a \u0001theft\u0002.",""],["leader-111-15","Tourist: I'd like to report a \u0001theft\u0002 case.",""]],"therapeutic (adj.)":[["guide-110-45","These Herbal Mineral Springs provide herbal \u0001therapeutic\u0002 springs and beautifying mineral baths.","這些草本礦泉提供草本療效溫泉與美容礦物浴。"],["guide-108-71","Over the history of the development of \u0001therapeutic\u0002 spas, hot springs have been regarded as a valuable resource for preventive health care in many countries.","",1]],"threat (n.)":[["leader-108-58","Hunting and habitat loss often pose a huge \u0001threat\u0002 to the wild animals.","狩獵和棲地喪失常對野生動物構成巨大威脅。"],["guide-108-47","Never make jokes about bombing, terrorism, smuggling, etc., as policemen of the airport are required to take all \u0001threats\u0002 seriously.","絕不要拿爆炸、恐怖攻擊、走私等開玩笑,因為機場警察必須認真看待所有威脅。"]],"through (prep.)":[["leader-106-58","It is a very old hotel. I still have to make calls \u0001through\u0002 the operator.","這是間很老的飯店,我仍得透過接線生打電話。"]],"throughout (prep.)":[["leader-112-21","Complimentary Wi-Fi is available \u0001throughout\u0002 the five-star hotel.","這間五星級飯店全館提供免費 Wi-Fi。"],["leader-108-12","Mary: Is Wi-Fi available at the hotel? Hotel clerk: A wireless internet connection is available \u0001throughout\u0002 the hotel.","Mary:飯店有 Wi-Fi 嗎? 櫃台:全館都有無線網路。"]],"time-consuming (adj.)":[["guide-113-24","It is a good habit for students to keep a diary every day. However, it will be a \u0001time-consuming\u0002 task for their teachers to review the diary and make some comments on it every week.","學生每天寫日記是好習慣。然而,對老師來說,每週批閱日記並寫評語會是件耗時的工作。"],["leader-107-24","As flying becomes increasingly \u0001time-consuming\u0002 and less attractive, a new London-to-Amsterdam rail route could steal passengers from the skies.","隨著搭飛機越來越費時、吸引力下降,一條新的倫敦到阿姆斯特丹鐵路線可能搶走空中的乘客。"]],"topping (n.)":[["guide-112-27","People in Taiwan like eating shaved ice with fruit or other delicious \u0001toppings\u0002.","台灣人喜歡吃加水果或其他美味配料的剉冰。"],["guide-108-36","Unlike western-style ice cream, shaved ice is a distinctive Taiwanese dessert. People enjoy ice covered with fruit or other tasty \u0001toppings\u0002.","不同於西式冰淇淋,剉冰是獨特的台灣甜點。人們享用覆蓋著水果或其他美味配料的冰。"]],"tourism (n.)":[["guide-112-23","Ancestry \u0001tourism\u0002 is a sort of tourism in which tourists visit locations where they may learn family history and develop family connections.","尋根(族譜)旅遊是一種旅遊,遊客造訪某些地點,以了解家族歷史、建立家族連結。"],["guide-109-70","Caoling's new “flying mountain” and barrier lake attracted the attention of the public, sparking a new wave of \u0001tourism\u0002.","草嶺新形成的「飛山」與堰塞湖吸引了大眾目光,掀起一波新的觀光熱潮。"]],"tourist (adj.)":[["leader-112-37","Taipei 101 is one of the top \u0001tourist\u0002 attractions in Taipei.","台北 101 是台北頂級旅遊景點之一。"],["leader-110-56","Jonny has planned to make a trip to Houston and visits some popular \u0001tourist\u0002 attractions.","Jonny 計畫到休士頓旅行,並造訪一些熱門的觀光景點。"]],"transaction (n.)":[["guide-112-45","We have been committed to delivering the best service and are always working to conduct business \u0001transactions\u0002 as smoothly as possible.","我們一直致力於提供最好的服務,並始終努力讓業務交易盡可能順暢地進行。"],["leader-111-29","We charge NT$100 dollars per \u0001transaction\u0002.",""]],"transfer (n.)":[["leader-114-42","When traveling between two cities by train, you may need to make a \u0001transfer\u0002 at an intermediate station.","搭火車在兩城市間移動時,你可能需要在中途站轉乘。"],["guide-112-38","Usually a \u0001transfer\u0002 passenger will change from one plane to another and stop over at a midpoint for at most 24 hours before continuing the next journey.","通常轉機旅客會從一架飛機換到另一架,並在中途點停留最多 24 小時,再繼續下一段旅程。"]],"transform (v.)":[["guide-115-54","Along Taiwan's northern coast, the wonders made by nature can be seen at Yehliu Geopark. Wind and waves have \u0001transformed\u0002 rocks into various shapes, including a queen with a beautiful, thin neck.","在台灣北部海岸,野柳地質公園可見大自然的鬼斧神工。風與海浪把岩石雕塑成各種形狀,包括有著美麗細頸的女王頭。"],["guide-107-14","Many historical stores and buildings have been \u0001transformed\u0002 into fantastic restaurants.","許多歷史悠久的店家與建築已改造成很棒的餐廳。"]],"transformer (n.)":[["guide-115-57","Taiwan uses electric current of 110 volts at 60 cycles; appliances from Europe, Australia, or South-East Asia will need a(n) converter or \u0001transformer\u0002.","台灣使用 110 伏特、60 赫茲的電流;來自歐洲、澳洲或東南亞的電器會需要轉換器或變壓器。"],["guide-114-15","Taiwan uses electric current of 110 volts at 60 cycles, so appliances from Europe, Australia or South-East Asia will need an adapter or \u0001transformer\u0002.","台灣使用 110 伏特、60 赫茲的電流,所以來自歐洲、澳洲或東南亞的電器會需要轉接器或變壓器。"]],"transit (v.)":[["guide-109-43","Tourist: I was just here to \u0001transit\u0002.",""]],"transparent (adj.)":[["guide-113-55","Airline regulations insist on passengers using \u0001transparent\u0002 plastic bags for carrying personal belongings through security checkpoints, ensuring swift inspection and compliance with safety measures.","航空規定要求旅客使用透明塑膠袋攜帶隨身物品通過安檢,以確保快速檢查並符合安全措施。"],["guide-110-48","In case of emergency, open the \u0001transparent\u0002 plastic cover and press the red button to stop the escalator.","緊急情況時,打開透明塑膠蓋並按紅色按鈕停止手扶梯。"]],"tribe (n.)":[["guide-115-46","The indigenous people of Alishan, the Tsou people, are comprised of nine major \u0001tribes\u0002, each holding their own celebrations every year from September to December jointly referred to as the famous \"Tsou Annual Festival\" of Alishan.","阿里山的原住民鄒族由九大部落組成,各部落每年 9 月至 12 月舉辦自己的慶典,合稱著名的阿里山「鄒族年度祭典」。"],["guide-110-67","Taiwan's indigenous \u0001tribes\u0002 produce a wide variety of products in their local villages and sell as souvenirs.","台灣的原住民部落在當地村落生產各式各樣的產品,當作伴手禮販售。"]],"tropical (adj.)":[["guide-114-57","Climbing over 2KM, the famous Alishan forest railway passes through several climate zones, including \u0001tropical\u0002, subtropical, temperate, and high-mountain forest ranges.","阿里山森林鐵路爬升超過 2 公里,穿越數個氣候帶,包括熱帶、亞熱帶、溫帶與高山森林帶。"],["guide-111-33","Our last holiday was a five-day trip to Bali. We enjoyed heavenly weather during our vacation on the \u0001tropical\u0002 island.","我們上次假期是去峇里島玩五天。在那座熱帶島嶼度假時,我們享受了絕佳(宜人)的天氣。"]],"try (v.)":[["leader-110-54","Do you want to \u0001try\u0002 some?",""],["leader-106-30","Which dish sounds nicest to you, and which dish would you least like to \u0001try\u0002?","哪道菜聽起來最棒?哪道菜你最不想試?"]],"undercut (v.)":[["guide-115-76","Which of the following is closest in meaning to the word “\u0001undercut\u0002” in the second paragraph?","下列何者與第二段的 undercut 意思最接近?"],["guide-115-76","In their new report called “The Economics of Robotaxis,” Lux found that the average cost of operating a robotaxi could be enough to \u0001undercut\u0002 human-driven taxis.","",1]],"undertake (v.)":[["leader-113-65","Before you \u0001undertake\u0002 a journey through the Amazon rainforest, it's essential to be well-prepared and informed.","在你展開穿越亞馬遜雨林的旅程前,充分準備和了解資訊至關重要。"],["leader-108-36","Do not \u0001undertake\u0002 hard exercise for a few hours after a meal to allow food to digest.","飯後幾小時內不要做劇烈運動,好讓食物消化。"]],"unlimited (adj.)":[["leader-115-14","To make getting around the city easier, the tour leader suggested that everyone buy a transportation pass, which allows \u0001unlimited\u0002 travel on buses and trains for a set period.","為了方便在市區移動,領隊建議大家買一張交通票券,可在一段期間內無限搭乘公車和火車。"],["guide-106-8","Taipei Pass cards are good for a(n) \u0001unlimited\u0002 number of rides during the period of validity.","台北觀光護照在效期內可無限次搭乘。"]],"upgrade (n.)":[["leader-114-49","Wife: I called the hotel to see if we could get an \u0001upgrade\u0002 for our room.",""],["leader-111-70","Passenger: Is there any chance for a(n) \u0001upgrade\u0002 to the business class? Check-in clerk: Let me check if there are any business class seats available.","乘客:有機會升等到商務艙嗎? 報到人員:讓我查查有沒有空的商務艙座位。"]],"valuables (n.)":[["leader-113-30","The purpose of a hidden door is for security; it is often used to conceal a safe room or \u0001valuables\u0002.","隱藏門的目的是安全;它常用來隱藏密室或貴重物品。"],["guide-109-51","Before entering the museum, please check in all \u0001valuables\u0002 and bags at the cloakroom.","進博物館前,請把所有貴重物品和包包寄存在寄物處。"]],"variant (n.)":[["leader-111-18","Have you read the news report on the new \u0001variant\u0002 of COVID-19?","你讀過關於 COVID-19 新變種的新聞報導了嗎?"],["guide-110-2","Many countries closed their borders to flights from the UK due to a new \u0001variant\u0002 of the disease COVID-19 that had been spreading in London and the southeast of England.","由於在倫敦與英格蘭東南部蔓延的 COVID-19 新變種,許多國家對來自英國的航班關閉了邊境(國界)。"]],"variety (n.)":[["guide-113-32","Taiwan is listed as one of the top 15 hot spring sites, possessing an impressive \u0001variety\u0002 of springs such as warm, cool, mud, and even underwater hot springs.","台灣名列全球前 15 大溫泉勝地,擁有令人印象深刻的多樣泉種,如溫泉、冷泉、泥泉,甚至海底溫泉。"],["guide-107-28","Miaoli offers a wide \u0001variety\u0002 of classic souvenirs ranging from wood craft, Tung blossom art, and Hakka cuisine.","苗栗提供各式各樣的經典伴手禮,從木雕、桐花藝術到客家美食。"]],"vary (v.)":[["leader-115-19","Tourists are highly recommended to pay attention to the opening hours of different museums because they \u0001vary\u0002 a lot.","強烈建議遊客留意各博物館的開放時間,因為差異很大。"],["guide-111-7","The amount of alcohol passengers are allowed to carry onto a plane \u0001varies\u0002 from country to country.","乘客可攜帶上機的酒精量因國而異。"]],"vineyard (n.)":[["guide-111-76","During the 27-hour trip, passengers view \u0001vineyards\u0002, sunflower farms and the ostrich-filled Karoo Desert.","",4]],"virtual (adj.)":[["leader-110-38","Technology allows people to go on \u0001virtual\u0002 tours on their computers to see museums, world heritage sites, and other attractions before they plan a trip.","科技讓人能在電腦上進行虛擬導覽,在規劃旅程前先看博物館、世界遺產和其他景點。"],["guide-108-77","What kind of technology does the tour trader use to provide a personalized \u0001virtual\u0002 tour guide service in a museum or any other sightseeing place?","觀光業者用哪種科技在博物館等景點提供個人化虛擬導覽服務?"]],"vitalize (v.)":[["guide-111-72","Which of the following words does NOT mean “\u0001vitalize\u0002”?","下列哪個字「不」是 vitalize 的意思?"],["guide-111-71","To begin with, it is evident that tourism industry has the power to improve and \u0001vitalize\u0002 local economies.","",1]],"vomit (v.)":[["leader-112-45","A: I feel dizzy and I am about to \u0001vomit\u0002.",""],["leader-111-46","Passenger: I feel like \u0001vomiting\u0002.",""]],"voucher (n.)":[["leader-114-38","The hotel provided each guest with a \u0001voucher\u0002 for a complimentary breakfast.","飯店提供每位客人一張免費早餐的兌換券。"]],"vulnerable (adj.)":[["leader-108-59","Old people and young children are particularly \u0001vulnerable\u0002 members of our society.","老人和幼童是社會中特別脆弱的成員。"],["leader-106-20","When tourism is badly managed, it can destroy a place. Coasts, for example, are extremely \u0001vulnerable\u0002.","觀光管理不當會摧毀一個地方。例如海岸就極為脆弱易受害。"]],"weather (n.)":[["leader-110-68","The \u0001weather\u0002 is going to be really hot and sunny, so I don't think you should take a heavy coat on your trip.","天氣會很炎熱晴朗,所以我認為你旅行不該帶厚外套。"],["leader-106-34","A: Do you know what the \u0001weather\u0002 will be like tomorrow? B: I am afraid that it will have heavy showers.","A:你知道明天天氣會如何嗎? B:恐怕會有大陣雨。"]],"wedding (n.)":[["leader-107-35","\u0001Weddings\u0002 can be expensive. In this week's News Report you can hear about a way to cut the cost of your wedding by 50%.","婚禮可能很花錢。本週新聞報導會告訴你把婚禮費用削減 50% 的方法。"],["leader-106-50","The catering for all \u0001wedding\u0002 receptions at Princeton Hall is often done by Joy Eats.","Princeton Hall 所有婚宴的外燴,常由 Joy Eats 承辦。"]],"well-worn (adj.)":[["guide-109-79","But away from the \u0001well-worn\u0002 tourist trails, you'll discover another travel story entirely different.","",4]],"while (conj.)":[["guide-112-19","\u0001While\u0002 beef may seem like a great choice for holidays and other special occasions, some research suggests it may not be the healthiest option.","雖然牛肉在節慶和其他特殊場合看似是絕佳選擇,但有些研究指出它可能不是最健康的選項。"],["leader-106-19","Many tourists in Europe are Europeans themselves, \u0001while\u0002 others come largely from Asia and the Americas.","歐洲許多遊客本身就是歐洲人,而其他遊客則大多來自亞洲和美洲。"]],"wildlife (n.)":[["guide-111-77","According to the article, in which community can you see lots of \u0001wildlife\u0002?","根據本文,你能在哪個社區看到大量野生動物?"]],"willing (adj.)":[["guide-115-49","The Yanshui Fireworks Festival involves shooting tens of thousands of bottle rockets and fireworks not into the sky, but directly into crowds of \u0001willing\u0002 participants.","鹽水蜂炮節會發射數以萬計的沖天炮與煙火,不是射向天空,而是直接射向自願參與的人群。"],["guide-111-52","Would you be \u0001willing\u0002 to help Karen find information about our new product in this catalog?","你願意幫 Karen 在這本型錄中找我們新產品的資訊嗎?"]],"withdraw (v.)":[["leader-107-59","Sometimes companies have to \u0001withdraw\u0002 their products from the market because of faults.","有時公司因產品有瑕疵,必須把產品下架/回收。"],["leader-106-48","If you need some cash, the new credit card will allow you to \u0001withdraw\u0002 up to $300 a day from a cash dispenser.","如果你需要現金,這張新信用卡讓你每天可從提款機提領最多 300 美元。"]],"witness (v.)":[["guide-115-68","The Taiwan International Hot-Air Balloon Festival in Taitung is one of the most anticipated summer events, attracting countless visitors who come to \u0001witness\u0002 and experience the spectacle.","台東的台灣國際熱氣球嘉年華是最令人期待的夏季盛事之一,吸引無數遊客前來見證與體驗這場盛況。"]],"yearning (n.)":[["guide-107-79","Yearning","渴望、思念",3]],"zone (n.)":[["leader-109-6","People live in different time \u0001zones\u0002. When it's 3 p.m. in Milan, it's 11 p.m. in Seoul.","人們住在不同的時區。米蘭下午 3 點時,首爾是晚上 11 點。"],["guide-109-61","We are now crossing a \u0001zone\u0002 of turbulence. Please return to your seats and keep your seat belts fastened.","我們正通過一段亂流區。請回座並繫好安全帶。"]]};
